/downloads/david-hume_a-treatise-of-human-nature.epub?source=feed"},{"type":"epub","url":"https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/david-hume/a-treatise-of-human-nature/downloads/david-hume_a-treatise-of-human-nature_advanced.epub?source=feed"},{"type":"epub","url":"https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/david-hume/a-treatise-of-human-nature/downloads/david-hume_a-treatise-of-human-nature.kepub.epub?source=feed"},{"type":"azw3","url":"https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/david-hume/a-treatise-of-human-nature/downloads/david-hume_a-treatise-of-human-nature.azw3?source=feed"},{"type":"html","url":"https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/david-hume/a-treatise-of-human-nature/text/single-page"}],"access":"public_domain","license":"Public domain / CC0 in the United States","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/david-hume/a-treatise-of-human-nature"},"providers":[{"source":"Standard Ebooks","source_id":"https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/david-hume/a-treatise-of-human-nature","source_url":"https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/david-hume/a-treatise-of-human-nature","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"epub","url":"https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/david-hume/a-treatise-of-human-nature/downloads/david-hume_a-treatise-of-human-nature.epub?source=feed"},{"type":"epub","url":"https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/david-hume/a-treatise-of-human-nature/downloads/david-hume_a-treatise-of-human-nature_advanced.epub?source=feed"},{"type":"epub","url":"https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/david-hume/a-treatise-of-human-nature/downloads/david-hume_a-treatise-of-human-nature.kepub.epub?source=feed"},{"type":"azw3","url":"https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/david-hume/a-treatise-of-human-nature/downloads/david-hume_a-treatise-of-human-nature.azw3?source=feed"},{"type":"html","url":"https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/david-hume/a-treatise-of-human-nature/text/single-page"}],"access":"public_domain","license":"Public domain / CC0 in the United States","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:33d8bbfa5a9af3c3a7613aab","title":"ABC Arts & Museums","subtitle":"Colonial History and Indigenous Voices","description":"The presence of non-Western material heritage in Western museum collections poses one of the most significant challenges today, raising critical questions about provenance, ownership, and the concept of “art”. This collective volume, structured as an ABC of arts and museums, offers an overview of the intersections between art history and postcolonial studies. In response to ongoing debates about the decolonization of museums, it provides a space for critical reflection on topics such as 'ethnographic' collections, colonial narratives, and Indigenous perspectives. Bringing together researchers, artists, activists, and committed experts, the book serves as a forum for exchange, blending scholarly articles, artistic contributions, and essays. Through these diverse voices, this Abécédaire rethinks the history of art and museums as an experimental space, transcending disciplinary and geographical boundaries. It offers a fresh, nuanced perspective on contemporary issues in the study of the past while paving new pathways for the future.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Postcolonialism","Provenance research","Museum history","Museumsgeschichte","Postkolonialismus","Provenienzforschung","thema EDItEUR::G Reference, Information and Interdisciplinary subjects::GL Library and information sciences / Museology::GLZ Museology and heritage studies","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181456","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/8e4ca056-688d-448e-845f-b5504a7fd772/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116773/1/9783112218259.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181456","handle":"20.500.12854/181456","dspace_uuid":"c3279f86-f020-4cb9-90a4-816d9624e613"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181456","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181456","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116773/1/9783112218259.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:9ca7e9ad1e829b2c82acc299","title":"Abel's Island","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["William Steig"],"language":"en","year":1976,"publisher":"Paw Prints","isbn":["9780753581902","9570803304","7556810119","9780606010870","9575358058","9781557361806","1557361800","0553150197","9780553152555","9780241894774","9781439596753","9782070331567","0753581906","1466839171","1466898704","141779383X","8804462493","9781466898707","0571120806","9780312371432","0833512498","9780685310212","843920907X","9780756982904","9780374400163","9787556810116","9789575358051","1782691472","9781417793839","0756982901","9780833512499","0006715265","0374342865","9780571120802","9781664429246","9789570803303","9780553150605","055315060X","9780374300104","0374300100","9788439209072","8417059555","8417059563","9780374342869","0685310213","9780374442859","9782211061339","1439596751","9788417059552","0374400164","0553152556","0606010874","0241894778","9780553150193","2211061338","9781782691471","2070331563","9781466839175","9788417059569","0613018117","9780613018111","0812419448","1664429247","0374442851","0312371438","9780006715269","9788804462491","9780812419443"],"doi":"","subjects":[],"source":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL22325W","cover_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/223655-M.jpg","formats":[],"access":"digital_lending","license":"","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"OL22325W","openlibrary_work":"OL22325W","openlibrary_edition":"OL43084103M","internet_archive":"laoshubeipiaoliu0000unse"},"providers":[{"source":"Open Library","source_id":"OL22325W","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL22325W","language":"en","formats":[],"access":"digital_lending","license":"","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:4b329acc746fc361870d8f9a","title":"Abjekte Weiblichkeit","subtitle":"Transgressive Inszenierungen des Körpers in der Literatur von Kōno Taeko, Kirino Natsuo und Kanehara Hitomi","description":"Der weibliche Körper und seine Inszenierung in Werken der zeitgenössischen japanischen Autorinnen Kōno Taeko, Kirino Natsuo und Kanehara Hitomi stehen im Mittelpunkt des vorliegenden Buches. Es fragt danach, wie Literatur subversiv gestaltet werden kann, um normative Weiblichkeitsideale und traditionelle Geschlechterrollen zu dekonstruieren. Dabei dienen Darstellungen von Sexualität, Gewalt und Körperlichkeit als Strategien der Kritik an patriarchalen Strukturen, internalisierter Misogynie und struktureller Diskriminierung, während transgressive Handlungen als Ausdruck von Widerstand fungieren. Auf der Basis von Judith Butlers und Michel Foucaults Konzepten zur sozialen Konstruktion von Geschlecht sowie Julia Kristevas Theorie des Abjekten zeigt das Buch, wie die Autorinnen weibliche Subjektivität jenseits der Mutter- oder Lustobjektrolle gestalten, und leistet damit einen Beitrag zum literaturwissenschaftlichen Genderdiskurs.","authors":["von Garnier, Anna-Lena"],"language":"de","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Gender","Body","Woman","Körper","Frau","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism::DSB Literary studies: general","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JB Society and culture: general::JBS Social groups, communities and identities::JBSF Gender studies, gender groups","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JB Society and culture: general::JBC Cultural and media studies::JBCC Cultural studies","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181428","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/88081944-c108-40b2-b387-0ad5465cca61/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116754/1/9783112212110.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/ · CC-BY-SA","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181428","handle":"20.500.12854/181428","dspace_uuid":"4fa539df-870b-4093-bb1a-142e93fe9fc0"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181428","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181428","language":"de","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116754/1/9783112212110.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/ · CC-BY-SA","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:b2c21647edb2a61cfa51a4d8","title":"Accumulating Notes","subtitle":"Note-taking and Multilayered Written Artefacts","description":"People take notes in different contexts of their daily lives and for various purposes. While brief handwritten notes can occur individually, for example, as a Post-it note, they are also collected over the course of time in notebooks, diaries, or logs. Recent scholarship has proposed to approach written artefacts as ‘evolving entities’ and suggested frameworks to analyse the layers of material and/or content that they acquire over time. Such a stratigraphic analysis has been fruitfully applied to many types of written artefacts, especially those produced during a clearly identifiable and planned project. However, the potential of this approach remained largely untapped for written artefacts whose production does not follow a predefined plan or necessarily proceed in an orderly fashion. Focusing on the multifarious manifestations of notes as material tools for the visualisation, organisation, and transmission of knowledge, this volume aims to fill this gap. The present volume sheds light on how practices of note-taking and knowledge organisation (re)shape written artefacts and vice-versa by dissecting the processes in which notes accumulate in a variety of multilayered written artefacts from different cultures and periods.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Manuscript studies","Written artefacts","Stratigraphy","Notebooks","Handschriftenkunde","Schriftartefakt","Stratigraphie","Notizbuch","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism::DSB Literary studies: general","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JB Society and culture: general","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116875","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/4950cd4d-e276-4645-88b8-34fd3f2e363c/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/d382c17a-88bd-4346-8076-d8e58c93b73a/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116875","handle":"20.500.12657/116875","dspace_uuid":"1b55cb22-4ca0-4bb5-b5f7-b7b817b0bc4d"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116875","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116875","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/d382c17a-88bd-4346-8076-d8e58c93b73a/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:278232e3b0e1518f4008ea02","title":"Acide sulfurique","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Amélie Nothomb"],"language":"und","year":2005,"publisher":"Editorial Empúries","isbn":["8497872193","9782210750975","9782253121183","8862432518","9788862432511","9788970753706","2253121185","8970753702","2210750970","9780571234929","8433971212","0571234925","9788433971210","9782226167224","2226167226","9788497872195","9780571234936","0571234933"],"doi":"","subjects":[],"source":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1724580W","cover_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/7255785-M.jpg","formats":[],"access":"digital_lending","license":"","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"OL1724580W","openlibrary_work":"OL1724580W","openlibrary_edition":"OL30200464M","internet_archive":"hwangsanacidesul0000noth"},"providers":[{"source":"Open Library","source_id":"OL1724580W","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1724580W","language":"und","formats":[],"access":"digital_lending","license":"","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:e242680eb4f5d1c0b1fe1933","title":"Actitud docente e inclusión educativa: Una mirada desde la primera infancia","subtitle":"","description":"This work offers a comprehensive perspective on inclusive education in early childhood, highlighting teacher attitudes as a determining factor in the construction of inclusive classrooms. Educational inclusion is not limited to regulations or the implementation of policies; rather, it constitutes a philosophy that recognizes and values human diversity in its cultural, social, emotional, and cognitive dimensions. From the earliest years of schooling, the way teachers perceive and respond to individual differences shapes each child’s socioemotional development, self-esteem, and disposition toward learning, laying the foundations for educational equity and the construction of more just societies. The book explores how teachers’ lived experiences, their initial and ongoing training, institutional support, and family and community contexts influence their attitudes toward inclusion. It also analyzes the everyday challenges of pedagogical practice, such as workload overload, stress, and resource limitations, showing how teachers’ sensitivity, commitment, and creativity can transform obstacles into learning opportunities. Concrete pedagogical strategies are highlighted, including active methodologies, collaborative projects, and curricular flexibility, which make it possible to address diversity effectively and promote essential socioemotional competencies. The work also emphasizes the ethical and social dimension of inclusive education, positioning teachers as agents of change who contribute to more cohesive, empathetic, and equitable societies. Overall, this text provides evidence, reflection, and practical tools to strengthen inclusive education from early childhood, inspiring action and transforming the educational experience into a pathway toward equity and the genuine appreciation of diversity.","authors":["Casimiro-Urcos, Consuelo Nor","Tobalino-López, Donatila","Pareja-Pérez, Lourdes Basilia","Vegas-Palomino, Elizabeth Mercedes","Sanabria-Boudri, Fanny Miriam","Orosco-Naveros, Aida Beatriz"],"language":"es","year":2025,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/mfea9416","subjects":["Educación inclusiva","Primera infancia","Actitud docente","Diversidad","Equidad educativa","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JN Education::JNF Educational strategies and policy::JNFK Educational strategies and policy: inclusion"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/ha