ook provides a holistic view of the economic, legal, and technical issues at play. It explores how blockchain's unique attributes - immutability, security, and digital accessibility - can help build trust in the respective data and carbon offset claims across global supply chains. From international carbon regulation to real-world pilot projects and digital asset standards, this book speaks to a rapidly evolving landscape. With insights from leading scholars and cutting-edge research, it offers valuable guidance for academics, policymakers, legal professionals, fintech innovators, and sustainability leaders alike.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["DLT","Blockchain technology","Crypto","MiCAR","Digital assets","Environmental","Social and Governance (ESG)","Tokenization","Tokenisation","Voluntary Carbon Credits (VCC)","Voluntary Carbon Markets (VCM)","Carbon offsetting","Climate finance","MiFID","Blockchain","ESG","Klimafinanzierung","Tokenisierung","Umwelt","thema EDItEUR::K Economics, Finance, Business and Management::KF Finance and accounting::KFF Finance and the finance industry","thema EDItEUR::L Law::LN Laws of specific jurisdictions and specific areas of law::LNC Company, commercial and competition law: general"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116795","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/7bd1bcfd-87a8-4885-ac99-2af5e7881764/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/31c2372e-53f1-429e-acd7-af03fbd33fa6/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116795","handle":"20.500.12657/116795","dspace_uuid":"0550437e-df8e-43a3-ab68-6856344408df"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116795","source_url":