k delves into the past and examines the origins of activism against child labour. It addresses a hitherto under-examined question: how and why did child labour develop into a key concern between the 1880s and 1930s? Who were the protagonists who first raised the issue of child labour as a global concern? The study aims to provide the first account of the history of diverse and locally grounded – but nationally and frequently globally connected – child labour opponents in the Americas, their motivations and campaigns, at the turn of the 20th century. I argue that, for the period between 1888 and 1938, one can identify similar protagonists, a joint goal, a broadly similar timing, common platforms, comparable campaigning mechanisms and many types of connections or entanglements across regions. Nevertheless, in contrast to the global anti-slavery movement, child labour opponents formed a loosely institutionalised network which lacked an international organisation that focused specifically on child labour. A global history approach to child labour opponents helps reveal large-scale patterns across societies and highlight similarities and differences between cases.","authors":["Schneider, Nina"],"language":"en","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["United States","Brazil","Child labour","Brasilien","Kinderarbeit","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History::NHB General and world history","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History::NHK History of the Americas"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181518","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/337b9029-5b47-4e94-92ab-effae851bbdd/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116745/1/9783112208229.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181518","handle":"20.500.12854/181518","dspace_uuid":"e47a3138-6ca9-4d6f-b4c2-5faf6ae4ac2e"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181518","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181518","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116745/1/9783112208229.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:f7e7cc191bf6215de514f69b","title":"Child Rehabilitation from the Holocaust to October 7","subtitle":"","description":"After October 7th, which confronted Israeli children with unimaginable violence, the potential to apply post-WW II and Holocaust child rehabilitation approaches became clearly visible and urgent. After 1945, hundreds of thousands of children had to be brought back to everyday life against the background of harrowing experiences during the Holocaust years. This volume bridges historical insights with current challenges, offering strategies for rehabilitating conflict-affected youth. It synthesizes knowledge from diverse fields to support victims of war and displacement. The work transforms past experiences into actionable support, equipping professionals with insights to reshape child rehabilitation in conflict zones, underscoring the importance of historical lessons in addressing present-day crises.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Child rehabilitation","Holocaust","Israel-Hamas war","Children of war","Genocide","Rehabilitation","Kinder","7. Oktober","Genozid","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History::NHT History: specific events and topics::NHTZ Genocide and ethnic cleansing::NHTZ1 The Holocaust"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116898","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/b13dd375-fbee-48a9-ba3b-dbd0a135a6b1/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/a2d8bec7-4bfc-499f-815d-e4ee3f8e277b/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116898","handle":"20.500.12657/116898","dspace_uuid":"bb461111-32ac-446f-9c3c-07994dc47228"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116898","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116898","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/a2d8bec7-4bfc-499f-815d-e4ee3f8e277b/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:fe000b2ee12b0d5145daae49","title":"Child Rehabilitation from the Holocaust to October 7","subtitle":"","description":"After October 7th, which confronted Israeli children with unimaginable violence, the potential to apply post-WW II and Holocaust child rehabilitation approaches became clearly visible and urgent. After 1945, hundreds of thousands of children had to be brought back to everyday life against the background of harrowing experiences during the Holocaust years. This volume bridges historical insights with current challenges, offering strategies for rehabilitating conflict-affected youth. It synthesizes knowledge from diverse fields to support victims of war and displacement. The work transforms past experiences into actionable support, equipping professionals with insights to reshape child rehabilitation in conflict zones, underscoring the importance of historical lessons in addressing present-day crises.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Child rehabilitation","Holocaust","Israel-Hamas war","Children of war","Genocide","Rehabilitation","Kinder","7. Oktober","Genozid","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History::NHT History: specific events and topics::NHTZ Genocide and ethnic cleansing::NHTZ1 The Holocaust"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181571","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/daef94b6-0e52-4776-b7fb-363026e65e19/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116898/1/9783111676883.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181571","handle":"20.500.12854/181571","dspace_uuid":"7ef40f93-6a07-4921-af4a-8298b4f14679"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181571","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181571","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116898/1/9783111676883.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:e5574d4a8589d5ff84d7f6fd","title":"Children of the Whirlwind","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Scott, Leroy"],"language":"en","year":null,"publisher":"Project Gutenberg","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Criminals -- Fiction","Ex-convicts -- Fiction","Love stories","Category: American Literature","Category: Crime, Thrillers and Mystery","Category: Novels"],"source":"Project Gutenberg","source_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/3321","cover_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/3321/pg3321.cover.medium.jpg","formats":[{"type":"html","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/3321.html.images"},{"type":"epub","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/3321.epub3.images"},{"type":"mobi","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/3321.kf8.images"},{"type":"text","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/3321.txt.utf-8"},{"type":"text","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/files/3321/3321-0.txt"}],"access":"public_domain","license":"Public domain in the United States","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"3321","gutenberg_id":"3321"},"providers":[{"source":"Project Gutenberg","source_id":"3321","source_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/3321","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"html","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/3321.html.images"},{"type":"epub","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/3321.epub3.images"},{"type":"mobi","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/3321.kf8.images"},{"type":"text","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/3321.txt.utf-8"},{"type":"text","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/files/3321/3321-0.txt"}],"access":"public_domain","license":"Public domain in the United States","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:edf4a04d006db0101e6ab162","title":"China","subtitle":"Linking Markets for Growth","description":"China's prosperity is at the core of the emerging Platinum Age of global economic growth. Rapid economic growth has been underpinned by expansion in its domestic markets, and the integration of domestic and international markets in goods, services, capital, labour and foreign exchange. Global commodity prices have reached historic highs, while China’s capital outflows have helped to hold down interest rates worldwide. Linking markets, both domestic and international, has been key to China’s success. In sustaining its strong economic growth, China has become one of the world’s most voracious consumers of energy. The challenge now facing the government and people of China is in achieving cooperation with the international community to avert the costs–both economic and environmental–of accelerating energy consumption. China–Linking Markets for Growth gathers together leading scholars on China’s economic success and its effect on the world economy into the next few decades.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2007,"publisher":"ANU Press","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["China","International partnerships","Trade","thema EDItEUR::K Economics, Finance, Business and Management::KC Economics::KCL International economics::KCLT International trade and commerce","thema EDItEUR::G Reference, Information and Interdisciplinary subjects::GT Interdisciplinary studies::GTM Regional / International studies","thema EDItEUR::K Economics, Finance, Business and Management::KC Economics::KCL International economics","thema EDItEUR::K Economics, Finance, Business and Management::KC Economics::KCM Development economics and emerging economies","thema EDItEUR::K Economics, Finance, Business and Management::KC Economics::KCS Economic systems and structures","thema EDItEUR::K Economics, Finance, Business and Management::KJ Business and Management::KJK International business","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JB Society and culture: general"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116559","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/a420052c-b33d-4de7-91f5-5e7d628b74a6/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/a559969a-e548-4a6c-a6fa-8093f37fd893/retrieve"}],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116559","handle":"20.500.12657/116559","dspace_uuid":"ff79a839-59e0-4cfe-a8ad-266c6641cc50"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116559","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116559","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/a559969a-e548-4a6c-a6fa-8093f37fd893/retrieve"}],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:b3ea4a0379ec201e09939581","title":"China in Myanmar","subtitle":"Geopolitics of Asymmetry","description":"This book explores the complex power dynamics shaping China-Myanmar relations within the framework of asymmetrical geopolitics. By examining disparities in resources, influence and capacity, it delves into how China leverages its economic and strategic dominance, particularly through the Belt and Road Initiative (BRI) and the China-Myanmar Economic Corridor (CMEC). It provides a nuanced understanding of Myanmar’s geopolitical significance as a site of competition and its delicate balance between dependence on China and autonomy. The book highlights China’s asymmetric foreign policy strategies, the impact of the 2021 Military Coup on bilateral relations, and the challenges posed by stalled BRI projects amidst ethnic conflict and local resistance. It also examines the socio-political and economic implications of China’s investments in Myanmar, addressing issues pertaining to migration, ethnic ties and security. Through rigorous analysis, the book connects these elements to broader South Asian geopolitics, emphasizing Myanmar’s pivotal role in China’s regional ambitions and its access to the Indian Ocean. This interdisciplinary volume is an essential resource for scholars, researchers and students in International Relations, South Asian studies, Area Studies, Global Studies and Geopolitics. Additionally, journalists, policymakers and academics interested in China’s rise, the Belt and Road Initiative and South Asian geopolitics will find this book insightful.","authors":["Aryal, Saroj Kumar","Pradhan, Rajyavishek"],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"Taylor & Francis","isbn":[],"doi":"10.4324/9781042009886","subjects":["South Asian Politics","Indo-China Politics","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JP Politics and government::JPS International relations::JPSL Geopolitics","thema EDItEUR::K Economics, Finance, Business and Management::KC Economics::KCL International economics::KCLT International trade and commerce","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JP Politics and government::JPS International relations","thema EDItEUR::G Reference, Information and Interdisciplinary subjects::GT Interdisciplinary studies::GTM Regional / International studies","thema EDItEUR::G Reference, Information and Interdisciplinary subjects::GT Interdisciplinary studies::GTP Development studies","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JP Politics and government","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JP Politics and government::JPS International relations::JPSD Diplomacy","thema EDItEUR::K Economics, Finance, Business and Management::KC Economics::KCL International economics"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/117009","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/8f7f5574-7167-44c7-92c7-e10cacdb8457/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/b94ad34f-72af-4fd4-9da9-87ce7439e036/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/117009","handle":"20.500.12657/117009","dspace_uuid":"31fbdbd4-f246-4904-b403-cd809801da34"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/117009","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/117009","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/b94ad34f-72af-4fd4-9da9-87ce7439e036/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:14bf26508a090a092d0149dd","title":"China's 40 Years of Reform and Development 1978–2018","subtitle":"","description":"The year 2018 marks 40 years of reform and development in China (1978–2018). This commemorative book assembles some of the world's most prominent scholars on the Chinese economy to reflect on what has been achieved as a result of the economic reform programs, and to draw out the key lessons that have been learned by the model of growth and development in China over the preceding four decades. This book explores what has happened in the transformation of the Chinese economy in the past 40 years for China itself, as well as for the rest of the world, and discusses the implications of what will happen next in the context of China’s new reform agenda. Focusing on the long-term development strategy amid various old and new challenges that face the economy, this book sets the scene for what the world can expect in China’s fifth decade of reform and development. A key feature of this book is its comprehensive coverage of the key issues involved in China’s economic reform and development. Included are discussions of China’s 40 years of reform and development in a global perspective; the political economy of economic transformation; the progress of marketisation and changes in market-compatible institutions; the reform program for state-owned enterprises; the financial sector and fiscal system reform, and its foreign exchange system reform; the progress and challenges in economic rebalancing; and the continuing process of China’s global integration. This book further documents and analyses the development experiences including China’s large scale of migration and urbanisation, the demographic structural changes, the private sector development, income distribution, land reform and regional development, agricultural development, and energy and climate change policies.","authors":["Garnaut, Ross","Fang, Cai","Song, Ligang"],"language":"en","year":2018,"publisher":"ANU Press","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["China","Economic reform","Development","Economic growth","Political economy","Fiscal system","Financial sector","Foreign exchange system","Migration","Urbanisation","Income distribution","Climate change policies","thema EDItEUR::K Economics, Finance, Business and Management::KC Economics::KCG Economic growth","thema EDItEUR::K Economics, Finance, Business and Management::KC Economics::KCM Development economics and emerging economies","thema EDItEUR::K Economics, Finance, Business and Management::KC Economics::KCP Political economy","thema EDItEUR::K Economics, Finance, Business and Management::KC Economics"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116550","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/c6c6f50d-6093-49a9-95d6-759a83f4d017/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/be4ce59e-438a-413d-8125-86c29e385712/retrieve"},{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116550/1/9781760462253.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116550","handle":"20.500.12657/116550","dspace_uuid":"b88bf404-c2cd-4caf-812a-70c01a1e6e61","doab_source_id":"20.500.12854/181562","doab_handle":"20.500.12854/181562","doab_dspace_uuid":"b9a39fa9-dc6b-44fd-8c8d-a2ae7339f4f2"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116550","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116550","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/be4ce59e-438a-413d-8125-86c29e385712/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true},{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181562","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181562","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116550/1/9781760462253.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:899919af80da2c499cec3bec","title":"China's Dilemma","subtitle":"Economic Growth, the Environment and Climate Change","description":"China's Dilemma—Economic Growth, the Environment and Climate Change examines the challenges China will have to confront in order to maintain rapid growth while coping with the global financial turbulence, some rising socially destabilising tensions such as income inequality, an over-exploited environment and the long-term pressures of global warming. China’s Dilemma discusses key questions that will have an impact on China’s growth path and offers some in-depth analyses as to how China could confront these challenges. The authors address the effect of the global credit crunch and financial shocks on China’s economic growth; China’s contribution to greenhouse gas emissions and emissions reduction schemes; the environmental consequences of foreign direct investment in China; the relationship between air pollution and mortality; the effect of climate change on agricultural output; the coal industry’s compliance with tougher regulations; and the constraints water shortages may impose on China’s economy. It also emphasises the importance of managing the rising demand for energy to moderate oil price increases and placating domestic and international concerns about global warming. In the thirty years since China started on the path of reform, it has emerged as one of the largest and most dynamic economies in the world. This carries with it the responsibility to balance the requirements of key industries that are driving its development with the need to ensure that its growth is both equitable and sustainable. China’s Dilemma highlights key lessons learned from the past thirty years of reform in order to pave the way for balanced and sustained growth in the future.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2008,"publisher":"ANU Press","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["China","Economics","thema EDItEUR::K Economics, Finance, Business and Management::KC Economics::KCL International economics","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JN Education::JNF Educational strategies and policy::JNFK Educational strategies and policy: inclusion","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History::NHF Asian history","thema EDItEUR::K Economics, Finance, Business and Management::KJ Business and Management::KJK International business","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JP Politics and government::JPQ Central / national / federal government::JPQB Central / national / federal government policies"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181411","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/5803fef8-0bfe-4639-9923-88176c27903d/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116557/1/9781921536038.pdf"}],"access":"open_access","license":"open access · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181411","handle":"20.500.12854/181411","dspace_uuid":"ed00642f-39f0-4506-b8f5-f3bb81cd823d"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181411","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181411","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116557/1/9781921536038.pdf"}],"access":"open_access","license":"open access · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:c25689c956e9ab8c210bd9e8","title":"China's Dilemma","subtitle":"Economic Growth, the Environment and Climate Change","description":"China's Dilemma—Economic Growth, the Environment and Climate Change examines the challenges China will have to confront in order to maintain rapid growth while coping with the global financial turbulence, some rising socially destabilising tensions such as income inequality, an over-exploited environment and the long-term pressures of global warming. China’s Dilemma discusses key questions that will have an impact on China’s growth path and offers some in-depth analyses as to how China could confront these challenges. The authors address the effect of the global credit crunch and financial shocks on China’s economic growth; China’s contribution to greenhouse gas emissions and emissions reduction schemes; the environmental consequences of foreign direct investment in China; the relationship between air pollution and mortality; the effect of climate change on agricultural output; the coal industry’s compliance with tougher regulations; and the constraints water shortages may impose on China’s economy. It also emphasises the importance of managing the rising demand for energy to moderate oil price increases and placating domestic and international concerns about global warming. In the thirty years since China started on the path of reform, it has emerged as one of the largest and most dynamic economies in the world. This carries with it the responsibility to balance the requirements of key industries that are driving its development with the need to ensure that its growth is both equitable and sustainable. China’s Dilemma highlights key lessons learned from the past thirty years of reform in order to pave the way for balanced and sustained growth in the future.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2008,"publisher":"ANU Press","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["China","Economics","thema EDItEUR::K Economics, Finance, Business and Management::KC Economics::KCL International economics","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JN Education::JNF Educational strategies and policy::JNFK Educational strategies and policy: inclusion","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History::NHF Asian history","thema EDItEUR::K Economics, Finance, Business and Management::KJ Business and Management::KJK International business","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JP Politics and government::JPQ Central / national / federal government::JPQB Central / national / federal government policies"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116557","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/6b536d8a-4b73-414f-b4aa-4e71d0299933/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/1ee69572-59d2-4f50-aeb3-ca75d79aa2ee/retrieve"}],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116557","handle":"20.500.12657/116557","dspace_uuid":"5ee75c49-ddba-4ce8-ae5f-45e02bf64a50"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116557","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116557","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/1ee69572-59d2-4f50-aeb3-ca75d79aa2ee/retrieve"}],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:bb6435323ce6cc13134e4aad","title":"China's New Place in a World in Crisis","subtitle":"Economic, Geopolitical and Environmental Dimensions","description":"The world and China's place in it have been transformed over the past year. The pressures for change have come from the most severe global financial crisis ever. The crisis has accelerated China’s emergence as a great power. But China and its global partners have yet to think or work through the consequences of its new position for the governance of world affairs. China’s New Place in a World in Crisis discusses and provides in-depth analysis of the following questions. How have China’s growth prospects been affected by the global crisis? How will the crisis and China’s response to it impact China’s major domestic issues, such as industrialisation, urbanisation and the reform of the state-owned sector of the economy? How will the crisis and the international community’s response to it affect the rapidly emerging new international order? What will be China’s, and other major developing countries’, new role? Can China and the world find a way of breaking the nexus between economic growth and environmental sustainability — especially on the issue of climate change?","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2009,"publisher":"ANU Press","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Financial crisis","China","Economic policy","thema EDItEUR::K Economics, Finance, Business and Management::KC Economics::KCX Economic and financial crises and disasters","thema EDItEUR::K Economics, Finance, Business and Management::KC Economics::KCL International economics","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JP Politics and government::JPS International relations","thema EDItEUR::K Economics, Finance, Business and Management::KC Economics::KCM Development economics and emerging economies","thema EDItEUR::G Reference, Information and Interdisciplinary subjects::GT Interdisciplinary studies::GTQ Globalization","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JP Politics and government::JPS International relations::JPSL Geopolitics"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116556","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/154fd6f4-01ed-43db-a8bb-64ca7213ea4c/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/005187a1-ed8f-4d60-b309-881e128573df/retrieve"}],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116556","handle":"20.500.12657/116556","dspace_uuid":"4d6a93b3-3645-4edd-832a-dd071c3400d1"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116556","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116556","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/005187a1-ed8f-4d60-b309-881e128573df/retrieve"}],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:ba9a62f4b5f88ea9220dd964","title":"China's New Sources of Economic Growth: Vol. 2","subtitle":"Human Capital, Innovation and Technological Change","description":"China's efforts in searching for new sources of growth are increasingly pressing given the persistence of the growth slowdown in recent years. This year’s book elucidates key present macroeconomic challenges facing China’s economy in 2017, and the impacts and readiness of human capital, innovation and technological change in affecting the development of China’s economy. The book explores the development of human capital as the foundations of China’s push into more advanced growth frontiers. It also explores the progress of productivity improvement in becoming the primary mechanism by which China can sustain economic growth, and explains the importance of China’s human capital investments to success on this front. The book demonstrates that technical change is a major contributor to productivity growth; and that invention and innovation are increasingly driving technical change but so far lumpily across regions, sectors and invention motivations. Included are chapters providing an update on reform and macroeconomic development, educational inequality, the role of intangibles in determining China’s economic growth, and China’s progress in transitioning towards being an innovative country. The book also covers the regional dimension of innovation and technological progress by sector: in agricultural productivity, renewable energy and financial markets. Chapters on trade, investment, regional cooperation and foreign aid explore further the mechanisms through which technological change and innovative activities are emerging locally and internationally.","authors":["Song, Ligang"],"language":"en","year":2017,"publisher":"ANU Press","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["China","Economic growth","Macroeconomic development","Educational inequality","Human capital","Renewable energy","Agricultural productivity","Financial markets","Foreign aid","Innovation","Technological change","thema EDItEUR::K Economics, Finance, Business and Management::KC Economics","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JP Politics and government::JPQ Central / national / federal government::JPQB Central / national / federal government policies","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JP Politics and government"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116551","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/0b943bc0-5c61-4c47-838a-cc6a9e8df995/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/12dab5ce-2899-4140-ab53-31fe0936d50d/retrieve"}],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116551","handle":"20.500.12657/116551","dspace_uuid":"22b38a58-898d-40d7-bbc1-db7ea4ed9047"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116551","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116551","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/12dab5ce-2899-4140-ab53-31fe0936d50d/retrieve"}],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:beca5e1f8ba85b429851843c","title":"Chomp","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Carl Hiaasen"],"language":"es","year":2012,"publisher":"Alfred A. Knopf","isbn":["1444006193","6077356158","1444005065","0375868429","0593177665","9781444006155","1444006150","9780375968426","9780375868429","9781410451019","9780593177662","9780375868276","9781444005066","9786077356158","9781444006452","0375898956","0375868275","9780375898952","0375968423","9786075277950","6075277951","1410451011","1444006452","9781444006193"],"doi":"","subjects":[],"source":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL16116923W","cover_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/7263633-M.jpg","formats":[],"access":"digital_lending","license":"","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"OL16116923W","openlibrary_work":"OL16116923W","openlibrary_edition":"OL34940252M","internet_archive":"chomp00hiaa"},"providers":[{"source":"Open Library","source_id":"OL16116923W","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL16116923W","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"digital_lending","license":"","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:120e161f19f8f0df32df398a","title":"Choreo-ethical Assemblages","subtitle":"Embodied Research as Cosmopoietic Œkology","description":"How can we understand the world around us through our bodies, ethical considerations, and œcological awareness, and how can we actively shape it through cosmopoietic, generative forces? Choreo-ethical Assemblages – Embodied Research as Cosmopoietic Œcology explores the interconnections between choreography, ethics, and œcology through embodied research. The book presents micro-phenomenological actualisation and purposeful polysemy as methods for exploring subjective experiences and opening them up to diverse interpretations. Methodical-artistic approaches, such as the generative forces in choreographic environments that do not determine experience but open up spaces of resonance through ambiguity, are discussed. Thus, comprehension itself becomes a process that allows for and stimulates diverse interpretations. The twin existence of aesthetics and ethics, as well as narratives of “bare bodies,” make the intertwining of body, narrative, and responsibility tangible. “Choreo-ethical assemblages” make socio-aesthetic sensitisation and epistemic singularities tangible and unfold the political and poetic dimension of an artistic research that lives the relationality of diverse forces as choreo-ethical practice. Interdisciplinary perspective: connects choreography, ethics, and ecology, thereby engaging diverse disciplines such as dance studies, philosophy, psychotherapy, ecology, and artistic research. Innovative research methods: introduces new approaches such as micro-phenomenological embodiment to explore subjective experience. Relevance to social issues: addresses topics like vulnerability, body politics, the environment, and ecological sustainability. Wie können wir die Welt um uns herum mithilfe unseres Körpers, ethischer Überlegungen und ökologischem Bewusstsein verstehen und durch kosmopoietische, generative Kräfte aktiv mitgestalten? Choreo-ethical Assemblages – Embodied Research as Cosmopoietic Œkology untersucht die Querverbindungen zwischen Choreographie, Ethik und Œkologie durch verkörperte Forschung. Das Buch stellt mikrophänomenologische Vergegenwärtigung des Begreifens und zielgerichtete Polysemie als Methoden vor, um subjektive Erfahrungen zu erforschen und für vielfältige Interpretationen zu öffnen. Methodisch-künstlerische Zugänge, wie etwa die generativen Kräfte in choreographischen Umgebungen, die Erfahrung nicht festlegen, sondern durch Mehrdeutigkeit Resonanzräume aufmachen, werden diskutiert. So wird das Begreifen selbst zu einem Prozess, der vielfältige Lesarten zulässt und anstößt. Das Zwillingsdasein von Ästhetik und Ethik sowie Narrationen von „Bare Bodies“ lassen die Verflechtung von Körper, Erzählung und Verantwortung spürbar werden. „Choreo-ethische Assemblagen“ machen sozial-ästhetische Sensibilisierung und epistemische Singularitäten erfahrbar und entfalten die politische wie poetische Dimension eines künstlerischen Forschens, das die Relationalität diverser Wirkkräfte als choreo-ethische Praxis lebt. Interdisziplinäre Perspektive: Verknüpft Choreographie, Ethik und Ökologie und spricht so unterschiedliche Disziplinen wie Tanzwissenschaften, Philosophie, Psychotherapie, Ökologie und Künstlerische Forschung an. Innovative Forschungsmethoden: Neue Ansätze wie mikrophänomenologische Verkörperung zur Erforschung subjektiver Erfahrungen. Relevanz für gesellschaftliche Themen: Auseinandersetzung mit Verwundbarkeit, Körperpolitik und Umwelt sowie ökologischer Nachhaltigkeit.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Choreography","Ethics","Ecology","Microphenomenology","Poetics of Research","Choreographie","Ethik","Ökologie","Mikrophänomenologie","Poetik des Forschens","thema EDItEUR::A The Arts::AG The Arts: treatments and subjects::AGA History of art"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181514","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/b5d82c3a-9aa0-4296-aac3-d750b22a9e58/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116887/1/9783689240905.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181514","handle":"20.500.12854/181514","dspace_uuid":"0c11aa68-968a-411f-a536-26ede48e4f3d"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181514","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181514","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116887/1/9783689240905.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:f9e026e9690a23c67e663c17","title":"Choreo-ethical Assemblages","subtitle":"Embodied Research as Cosmopoietic Œkology","description":"How can we understand the world around us through our bodies, ethical considerations, and œcological awareness, and how can we actively shape it through cosmopoietic, generative forces? Choreo-ethical Assemblages – Embodied Research as Cosmopoietic Œcology explores the interconnections between choreography, ethics, and œcology through embodied research. The book presents micro-phenomenological actualisation and purposeful polysemy as methods for exploring subjective experiences and opening them up to diverse interpretations. Methodical-artistic approaches, such as the generative forces in choreographic environments that do not determine experience but open up spaces of resonance through ambiguity, are discussed. Thus, comprehension itself becomes a process that allows for and stimulates diverse interpretations. The twin existence of aesthetics and ethics, as well as narratives of “bare bodies,” make the intertwining of body, narrative, and responsibility tangible. “Choreo-ethical assemblages” make socio-aesthetic sensitisation and epistemic singularities tangible and unfold the political and poetic dimension of an artistic research that lives the relationality of diverse forces as choreo-ethical practice. Interdisciplinary perspective: connects choreography, ethics, and ecology, thereby engaging diverse disciplines such as dance studies, philosophy, psychotherapy, ecology, and artistic research. Innovative research methods: introduces new approaches such as micro-phenomenological embodiment to explore subjective experience. Relevance to social issues: addresses topics like vulnerability, body politics, the environment, and ecological sustainability. Wie können wir die Welt um uns herum mithilfe unseres Körpers, ethischer Überlegungen und ökologischem Bewusstsein verstehen und durch kosmopoietische, generative Kräfte aktiv mitgestalten? Choreo-ethical Assemblages – Embodied Research as Cosmopoietic Œkology untersucht die Querverbindungen zwischen Choreographie, Ethik und Œkologie durch verkörperte Forschung. Das Buch stellt mikrophänomenologische Vergegenwärtigung des Begreifens und zielgerichtete Polysemie als Methoden vor, um subjektive Erfahrungen zu erforschen und für vielfältige Interpretationen zu öffnen. Methodisch-künstlerische Zugänge, wie etwa die generativen Kräfte in choreographischen Umgebungen, die Erfahrung nicht festlegen, sondern durch Mehrdeutigkeit Resonanzräume aufmachen, werden diskutiert. So wird das Begreifen selbst zu einem Prozess, der vielfältige Lesarten zulässt und anstößt. Das Zwillingsdasein von Ästhetik und Ethik sowie Narrationen von „Bare Bodies“ lassen die Verflechtung von Körper, Erzählung und Verantwortung spürbar werden. „Choreo-ethische Assemblagen“ machen sozial-ästhetische Sensibilisierung und epistemische Singularitäten erfahrbar und entfalten die politische wie poetische Dimension eines künstlerischen Forschens, das die Relationalität diverser Wirkkräfte als choreo-ethische Praxis lebt. Interdisziplinäre Perspektive: Verknüpft Choreographie, Ethik und Ökologie und spricht so unterschiedliche Disziplinen wie Tanzwissenschaften, Philosophie, Psychotherapie, Ökologie und Künstlerische Forschung an. Innovative Forschungsmethoden: Neue Ansätze wie mikrophänomenologische Verkörperung zur Erforschung subjektiver Erfahrungen. Relevanz für gesellschaftliche Themen: Auseinandersetzung mit Verwundbarkeit, Körperpolitik und Umwelt sowie ökologischer Nachhaltigkeit.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Choreography","Ethics","Ecology","Microphenomenology","Poetics of Research","Choreographie","Ethik","Ökologie","Mikrophänomenologie","Poetik des Forschens","thema EDItEUR::A The Arts::AG The Arts: treatments and subjects::AGA History of art"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116887","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/856c3280-cbb4-41b3-9ab6-8eed95c6a088/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/244de101-01ef-4659-8d19-525dc3078d94/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116887","handle":"20.500.12657/116887","dspace_uuid":"9ee69d5c-6cf6-43d7-ad79-2108405d83a3"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116887","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116887","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/244de101-01ef-4659-8d19-525dc3078d94/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:88ea969e7aa3e86cb1cd4c94","title":"Choreographing Copyright","subtitle":"Race, Gender, and Intellectual Property Rights in American Dance","description":"This book provides a historical and cultural analysis of US–based dance-makers’ investment in intellectual property rights. Although federal copyright law in the United States did not recognize choreography as a protectable class prior to the 1976 Copyright Act, efforts to win copyright protection for dance began eight decades earlier. In a series of case studies stretching from the late nineteenth century to the early twenty-first, the book reconstructs those efforts and teases out their raced and gendered politics. Rather than chart a narrative of progress, the book shows how dancers working in a range of genres have embraced intellectual property rights as a means to both consolidate and contest racial and gendered power. A number of the artists featured in the book are well-known white figures in the history of American dance, including modern dancers Loïe Fuller, Hanya Holm, and Martha Graham, and ballet artists Agnes de Mille and George Balanchine. But the book also uncovers a host of marginalized figures—from the South Asian dancer Mohammed Ismail, to the African American pantomimist Johnny Hudgins, to the African American blues singer Alberta Hunter, to the white burlesque dancer Faith Dane—who were equally interested in positioning themselves as subjects rather than objects of property, as possessive individuals rather than exchangeable commodities. Choreographic copyright, the book argues, has been a site for the reinforcement of gendered white privilege as well as for challenges to it.","authors":["Kraut, Anthea"],"language":"en","year":2015,"publisher":"Oxford University Press","isbn":[],"doi":"10.1093/acprof:oso/9780199360369.001.0001","subjects":["Choreographic copyright","Copyright law","Intellectual property rights","American dance","Loïe Fuller","Agnes de Mille","Martha eGraham","George Balanchine","Johnny Hudgins","White privilege","thema EDItEUR::A The Arts::AT Performing arts::ATQ Dance","thema EDItEUR::A The Arts::AT Performing arts::ATQ Dance::ATQC Choreography","thema EDItEUR::L Law::LN Laws of specific jurisdictions and specific areas of law::LNR Intellectual property law::LNRC Copyright law"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116965","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/868c72dc-5b6d-4c9d-adf6-80dca8595285/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/eeb3e1c0-5590-421b-839b-9ffd7d549f5a/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116965","handle":"20.500.12657/116965","dspace_uuid":"3fe38843-bf1d-4f3a-923f-02f9c12e8289"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116965","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116965","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/eeb3e1c0-5590-421b-839b-9ffd7d549f5a/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:f713a202d9d6ae2f2d21939c","title":"Christliches Reden von Gott I Christian Speaking of God","subtitle":"","description":"The Communion of Protestant Churches in Europe (CPCE), together with other churches, sees it as its duty to speak of God in an understandable, inspiring and encouraging way. This document, the result of a study process lasting several years, was approved by the 9th General Assembly of the CPCE in 2024 and is characterised as a groundbreaking contribution to the understanding of the current way of speaking about God in the CPCE. Following a presentation of the conditions for the discourse on God in European Protestantism, it outlines the basic features of a Trinitarian view of God and God's work, taking particular account of modern criticism of the concept of God's omnipotence. Christian speaking of God includes speaking to God, with God and from God in worship and prayer, which is considered in separate chapters. Finally, different social contexts in which the worth of Christian speaking of God must be proven are shown.","authors":[],"language":"de","year":2025,"publisher":"Evangelische Verlagsanstalt","isbn":[],"doi":"10.36199/978-3-374-07943-8","subjects":["Theology","Ecumenical Theology","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QR Religion and beliefs::QRV Aspects of religion::QRVG Theology","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QR Religion and beliefs::QRM Christianity"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/117080","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/5994ad7c-d331-478c-aa16-a6e2d3acb5a0/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/0824eade-3d92-40ed-a06d-5aa75b4d4994/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/117080","handle":"20.500.12657/117080","dspace_uuid":"1959574e-5284-49c9-907f-9cb5e8e7d9a9"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/117080","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/117080","language":"de","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/0824eade-3d92-40ed-a06d-5aa75b4d4994/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:10a253dbad288701e812ab60","title":"CHS Toolkit","subtitle":"Training group leaders how to include people with chronic disease in community activities","description":"The purpose of this package is to support you to improve the inclusion of people with chronic disease in community activities in your local area. It contains information and resources to help you to plan, deliver and evaluate educational activities with your local community. The first section details the aim, rationale and background for the development of this package. The overall aim of this package is to educate community group leaders about chronic disease issues. Community leaders equipped with such knowledge will be better able to support people with chronic disease to manage their conditions while encouraging their participation in community group activities.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2011,"publisher":"ANU Press","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Chronic disease","Community involvement","Inclusion","Local community","Toolkit","thema EDItEUR::M Medicine and Nursing::MK Medical specialties, branches of medicine::MKF Pathology::MKFK Chronic diseases and conditions","thema EDItEUR::M Medicine and Nursing::MB Medicine: general issues::MBN Public health and preventive medicine::MBNH Personal and public health / health education","thema EDItEUR::G Reference, Information and Interdisciplinary subjects::GB Encyclopaedias and reference works::GBC Reference works","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences","thema EDItEUR::V Health, Relationships and Personal development::VF Family and health::VFD Popular medicine and health","thema EDItEUR::V Health, Relationships and Personal development::VS Self-help, personal development and practical advice","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JB Society and culture: general::JBF Social and ethical issues::JBFM Disability: social aspects"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116548","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/af782b2a-d353-4300-8186-9a92ae996c60/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/7031d552-6dd3-407f-9ea7-a3b1481636fd/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/share-your-work/cclicenses/ · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116548","handle":"20.500.12657/116548","dspace_uuid":"13c92a2d-6175-422a-9018-ad98088ca77a"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116548","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116548","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/7031d552-6dd3-407f-9ea7-a3b1481636fd/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/share-your-work/cclicenses/ · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:6a47a47733591beff60c4490","title":"Cibercrimen","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Telly Frias Jr"],"language":"es","year":2021,"publisher":"Fiero Publishing Company","isbn":["1956768211","9781956768213"],"doi":"","subjects":[],"source":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL28682781W","cover_url":"","formats":[],"access":"metadata_only","license":"","verified_legal":false,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"OL28682781W","openlibrary_work":"OL28682781W","openlibrary_edition":"OL39364782M"},"providers":[{"source":"Open Library","source_id":"OL28682781W","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL28682781W","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"metadata_only","license":"","verified_legal":false}]},{"id":"work:ff0c4f1336cf10894b35563f","title":"Cibercrimen","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Frias, Telly, Jr."],"language":"es","year":2018,"publisher":"Fiero Publishing Company","isbn":["9781956768015","1956768017"],"doi":"","subjects":[],"source":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL28680636W","cover_url":"","formats":[],"access":"metadata_only","license":"","verified_legal":false,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"OL28680636W","openlibrary_work":"OL28680636W","openlibrary_edition":"OL39360871M"},"providers":[{"source":"Open Library","source_id":"OL28680636W","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL28680636W","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"metadata_only","license":"","verified_legal":false}]},{"id":"work:6e4a8eabe770bf54af6d7b84","title":"Ciberseguridad aplicada: un enfoque integral de riesgos, gobernanza y análisis forense digital","subtitle":"","description":"In a digital environment characterized by complexity, interconnectivity, and constant technological transformation, cybersecurity has become a strategic pillar for information protection and system continuity. This book offers a comprehensive perspective that goes beyond traditional approaches, coherently integrating conceptual foundations, governance models, attack and defense dynamics, and digital forensic analysis processes that help understand and address the current challenges of cyberspace. Through a structured and applied approach, the work explores how threats evolve alongside technology, highlighting the need to adopt adaptive strategies that integrate technical, organizational, and human factors. It also examines regulatory frameworks and methodologies that guide risk management, emphasizing their role in decision-making and in building resilient environments. Likewise, the book analyzes the offensive and defensive practices that shape the digital security landscape, as well as the influence of human behavior in generating vulnerabilities. Finally, it delves into forensic analysis as a key mechanism for incident reconstruction, evidence generation, and the strengthening of response capabilities. This work constitutes both an academic and professional resource that enables readers to understand cybersecurity as a dynamic system in which anticipation, adaptation, and continuous learning are essential to protecting the most critical asset of the digital age: information.","authors":["Carrizo-García, Luis Eduardo","Decimavilla-Alarcón, Diana Carolina","Pinela-Tigua, José Ottón","Caisaguano-Caisaguano, Luis Arturo","Mateo-Washbrum, Ivette Auxiliadora","Pineda-Calle, Zoila Amada"],"language":"es","year":2026,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/mxch1610","subjects":["Ciberseguridad estratégica","Gobernanza y gestión del riesgo","Amenazas y defensa digital","Análisis forense digital","Resiliencia y adaptación tecnológica","thema EDItEUR::U Computing and Information Technology::UR Computer security"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178513.2","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/77ff72e1-1838-4982-bfbf-d02a3f0f6e6a/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/178513.2","handle":"20.500.12854/178513.2","dspace_uuid":"90a278b8-4e67-4b30-924b-37b8ba6d2f45"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/178513.2","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178513.2","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:8f79ed5209bcccb6d817f9c3","title":"Cilsur","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Wiki Micronacional"],"language":"es","year":2022,"publisher":"","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Article","Articles","Artículo","Artículos","Micronation","Micronations","Micronación","Micronaciones"],"source":"Internet Archive","source_url":"https://archive.org/details/micronaciones-fandom-com-wiki-Cilsur","cover_url":"https://archive.org/services/img/micronaciones-fandom-com-wiki-Cilsur","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://archive.org/download/micronaciones-fandom-com-wiki-Cilsur/micronaciones-fandom-com-wiki-Cilsur.pdf"},{"type":"html","url":"https://archive.org/download/micronaciones-fandom-com-wiki-Cilsur/micronaciones-fandom-com-wiki-Cilsur_hocr.html"},{"type":"text","url":"https://archive.org/download/micronaciones-fandom-com-wiki-Cilsur/micronaciones-fandom-com-wiki-Cilsur_djvu.txt"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"micronaciones-fandom-com-wiki-Cilsur","internet_archive":"micronaciones-fandom-com-wiki-Cilsur"},"providers":[{"source":"Internet Archive","source_id":"micronaciones-fandom-com-wiki-Cilsur","source_url":"https://archive.org/details/micronaciones-fandom-com-wiki-Cilsur","language":"es","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://archive.org/download/micronaciones-fandom-com-wiki-Cilsur/micronaciones-fandom-com-wiki-Cilsur.pdf"},{"type":"html","url":"https://archive.org/download/micronaciones-fandom-com-wiki-Cilsur/micronaciones-fandom-com-wiki-Cilsur_hocr.html"},{"type":"text","url":"https://archive.org/download/micronaciones-fandom-com-wiki-Cilsur/micronaciones-fandom-com-wiki-Cilsur_djvu.txt"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:7e76c4660f89335fe0b2dd74","title":"Cinema and the City in the Age of Planetary Urbanization","subtitle":"","description":"Amid deepening socio-ecological crises, urban realities are changing fundamentally. Cinema, a medium historically intertwined with the city, has likewise undergone a profound transformation in its modes of representation and visual culture since the late 1980s. Today, filmmakers, photographers, and radical artists investigate the distant landscapes and territories of extended urbanization in all their complexity. Films like Behemoth (Zhao Liang, 2015), Homo Urbanus (Ila Bêka & Louise Lemoine, 2010), and Leviathan (Véréna Paravel, 2012) exemplify this practice. But how do cinema and the representation of the city mutually shape each other? This book stages an encounter between filmmaking and the built environment, as well as film theory and the theory of planetary urbanization by deploying the notion of the urban sensorium as a conceptual lens. It foregrounds the multifaceted sensory experiences of urban life within and beyond the city, and its representation in cinema. With a foreword by Neil Brenner and contributions by Nitin Bathla, Silvia Cipelletti, Markus Lähteenmäki, Klearjos E. Papanicolaou, Äsel Kadyrkhanova, Mosè Cometta, Jacqueline Maurer, Sofie Stilling, Søren Nielsen, Hans Teerds, Fred Truniger, Emil Hvelplund Kristiansen, Anne Romme, Lorenzo Tripodi, Adam Jasper, Junia Cambraia Mortimer, Roberto Luís Monte-Mór, Rosa Barba, Joshua Bonnetta and J.P. Sniadecki, Christian Schmid, Ana Vaz, Hira Nabi, Chrystel Oloukoï, Louise Lemoine and Ila Bêka Brings together contemporary visual culture with the transformative theory of planetary urbanization Features contributions from scholars, researchers, filmmakers, and practitioners Draws on various academic disciplines and creative practices including film, urban studies, geography, architecture, architectural history, and cultural studies Excerpts of works by the filmmakers featured in the book can be accessed via the ETH Zürich Research Collection: All the Dreams We Dream: Excerpt ÄSEL KADYRKHANOVA https://doi.org/10.3929/ethz-c-000788727 https://video.ethz.ch/!v/PcPvCeiplv6 55°42’14.8”N 12°33’18.4”E SOFIE STILLING, SØREN NIELSEN, and HANS TEERDS https://doi.org/10.3929/ethz-c-000788734 https://video.ethz.ch/!v/AMdfbtCtOvq Teaching Architecture Through an Eye-Level Perspective: Examples EMIL HVELPLUND KRISTIANSEN and ANNE ROMME https://doi.org/10.3929/ethz-c-000788738 https://video.ethz.ch/!v/E_FW8yYedhI https://video.ethz.ch/!v/MOQdFlbJsgk https://video.ethz.ch/!v/AII3KaUrTYu Cinematic Urbanism: Examples LORENZO TRIPODI https://doi.org/10.3929/ethz-c-000788749 https://video.ethz.ch/!v/FjH1PqUq0jr https://video.ethz.ch/!v/GA-bRExEClR https://video.ethz.ch/!v/AJ8mR5Uj-9T We Have Extra Lives – Cinema, Gaming, Language, and the Production of Hong Kong Space: Accompaniment ADAM JASPER and PETER NELSON https://doi.org/10.3929/ethz-c-000788744 https://video.ethz.ch/!v/BR8nLSO09Oe Urban-Nature Archives: Fragments JUNIA CAMBRAIA MORTIMER and ROBERTO LUÍS MONTE-MÓR https://doi.org/10.3929/ethz-c-000788732 https://video.ethz.ch/!v/NQYeveOFdBD https://video.ethz.ch/!v/AebcYBoy-VN https://video.ethz.ch/!v/C86DCKISH_v Community Media: Videos CHRISTIAN SCHMID https://doi.org/10.3929/ethz-c-000788750 https://video.ethz.ch/!v/Pjs9WjHu53t https://video.ethz.ch/!v/HYy-qEUrPqy All That Perishes At The Edge Of Land: Excerpts HIRA NABI https://doi.org/10.3929/ethz-c-000788729 https://video.ethz.ch/!v/DlUjDUUFiSS https://video.ethz.ch/!v/MTUykQT6Pwv https://video.ethz.ch/!v/MFhdm2NKbQ6 Homo Urbanus: Trailer LOUISE LEMOINE and ILA BÊKA https://doi.org/10.3929/ethz-c-000788712 https://video.ethz.ch/!v/GO2dwFW7_oi","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"jovis Verlag","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Planetary urbanization","Ethnographic filmmaking","Radical film","Art film","Essay film","Landscape humanities","Environmental humanities","Anthropocene","Extended urbanization","City symphony","Transdisciplinary methods","Creative methods","Planetare Urbanisierung","Ethnografisches Filmemachen","Radikaler Film","Kunstfilm","Essayfilm","Landschaftsbezogene Geisteswissenschaften","Umweltbezogene Geisteswissenschaften","Anthropozän","Erweit