"openlibrary_work":"OL19336182W","openlibrary_edition":"OL60567993M"},"providers":[{"source":"Open Library","source_id":"OL19336182W","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL19336182W","language":"en","formats":[],"access":"metadata_only","license":"","verified_legal":false}]},{"id":"work:65cf75db89ab249e9ab61ac1","title":"Clasificación de algunos suelos de los Andes venezolanos según el método numérico y la 7a. aproximación","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Juan B Castillo"],"language":"es","year":1975,"publisher":"Universidad de Los Andes, Facultad de Ciencias Forestales, Instituto de Geografía y Conservación de Recursos Naturales","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":[],"source":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL28192475W","cover_url":"","formats":[],"access":"metadata_only","license":"","verified_legal":false,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"OL28192475W","openlibrary_work":"OL28192475W","openlibrary_edition":"OL38596594M","open_library_source_id":"OL5235005W","open_library_openlibrary_work":"OL5235005W","open_library_openlibrary_edition":"OL2674971M"},"providers":[{"source":"Open Library","source_id":"OL28192475W","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL28192475W","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"metadata_only","license":"","verified_legal":false},{"source":"Open Library","source_id":"OL5235005W","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL5235005W","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"metadata_only","license":"","verified_legal":false}]},{"id":"work:d258b3c81acaccbe84ff399b","title":"Clean Architecture","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Robert C. Martin"],"language":"it","year":2017,"publisher":"ANAYA MULTIMEDIA","isbn":["9789352865123","8850334397","935286512X","9788850334391","9780134494333","9780134494166","8441539901","0134494164","0134494326","9780134494326","0134494334","9788441539907"],"doi":"","subjects":[],"source":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL19809141W","cover_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8605114-M.jpg","formats":[],"access":"metadata_only","license":"","verified_legal":false,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"OL19809141W","openlibrary_work":"OL19809141W","openlibrary_edition":"OL31838215M"},"providers":[{"source":"Open Library","source_id":"OL19809141W","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL19809141W","language":"it","formats":[],"access":"metadata_only","license":"","verified_legal":false}]},{"id":"work:ba1b1ea3983105e9fc6ba25f","title":"Climate Assemblies","subtitle":"New Civic Institutions for a Climate-changed World","description":"Climate Assemblies are capturing the imagination of people interested in how citizens can participate in decision-making to address the climate and ecological crisis. Traditional institutions are struggling to cope with the challenges of a climate-changed world. Climate Assemblies are new civic institutions that include a cross-section of the public in deliberation to influence environmental policy, governance, public discourse and collective action. With the rapid spread of this approach to public engagement, practice has developed well in advance of research. This book addresses that gap by analysing the internal and external dimensions of climate assemblies and how they interact. It brings together 25 authors to offer novel perspectives, critical insights and practical reflections based on original research about paradigmatic cases at local, national, transnational and global levels. The book investigates the state of the field, reflects on the hope and hype about this growing phenomenon, and proposes ways to improve climate assemblies so that they can make a difference in a climate-changed world.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Climate Assemblies","Environmental Governance","Democratic Innovations","Citizen Participation","Public Deliberation","Bürgerbeteiligung","Bürgerrat","Demokratie","Klima","Regierungsführung","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JP Politics and government::JPH Political structure and processes","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JP Politics and government::JPQ Central / national / federal government::JPQB Central / national / federal government policies","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JB Society and culture: general"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116899","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/dbaa46cf-2e35-4d70-98c3-ca7f5965e228/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/efb33ba5-2ad3-493f-9d61-e5bafab3886f/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116899","handle":"20.500.12657/116899","dspace_uuid":"5fb73558-ed6a-4e28-8ff9-ecce4a13fecf"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116899","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116899","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/efb33ba5-2ad3-493f-9d61-e5bafab3886f/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:f06a5ce7298c38cad342559f","title":"Climate Assemblies","subtitle":"New Civic Institutions for a Climate-changed World","description":"Climate Assemblies are capturing the imagination of people interested in how citizens can participate in decision-making to address the climate and ecological crisis. Traditional institutions are struggling to cope with the challenges of a climate-changed world. Climate Assemblies are new civic institutions that include a cross-section of the public in deliberation to influence environmental policy, governance, public discourse and collective action. With the rapid spread of this approach to public engagement, practice has developed well in advance of research. This book addresses that gap by analysing the internal and external dimensions of climate assemblies and how they interact. It brings together 25 authors to offer novel perspectives, critical insights and practical reflections based on original research about paradigmatic cases at local, national, transnational and global levels. The book investigates the state of the field, reflects on the hope and hype about this growing phenomenon, and proposes ways to improve climate assemblies so that they can make a difference in a climate-changed world.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Climate Assemblies","Environmental Governance","Democratic Innovations","Citizen Participation","Public Deliberation","Bürgerbeteiligung","Bürgerrat","Demokratie","Klima","Regierungsführung","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JP Politics and government::JPH Political structure and processes","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JP Politics and government::JPQ Central / national / federal government::JPQB Central / national / federal government policies","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JB Society and culture: general"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181414","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/de70482f-3806-4a69-9edb-1c6957a3c638/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116899/1/9783111328393.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181414","handle":"20.500.12854/181414","dspace_uuid":"9558fd87-364c-4b56-8140-c97d5bf6d7b0"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181414","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181414","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116899/1/9783111328393.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:067e2104d9b47434883b05d9","title":"Clinical Nursing Skills","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Christy Bowen","Taranee Albert","Mary Anne Bera","Jessica Crockett","Lindsay L. Draper","Sandy Grimm","Alissa Hershberger","Stephanie Hoffmann","Czarina Hounsel","Lindsay Jusino","Lori Kelly","Heather Moore","Amisha Parekh de Campos","Margaret Riley","Susan M. Rouse (Retired)","Leigh A. Waldron"],"language":"en","year":2024,"publisher":"OpenStax, Rice University","isbn":["9781961584501","9781711472836","9781711472829","9781961584853"],"doi":"","subjects":["Nursing","Fundamentals and Skills","{'id': 382, 'meta': {'type': 'books.BookSubjects'}, 'subject_name': 'Nursing', 'subject_page_content': 'Simple to use, simple to adopt. Our nursing textbooks are designed to meet the standard scope and sequence requirements of their respective courses – and are 100% free online. Complete with free resources for educators (like LMS course shells, lecture slides, instructor answer keys, and more), all OpenStax textbooks are fully customizable. Explore our texts below and adopt any and all parts us","{'id': 201, 'meta': {'type': 'books.BookCategories'}, 'subject_name': 'Nursing', 'subject_category': 'Fundamentals and Skills'}"],"source":"OpenStax","source_url":"https://openstax.org/details/books/clinical-nursing-skills","cover_url":"https://assets.openstax.org/oscms-prodcms/media/documents/clinical_nursing_skills_web_card.svg","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://assets.openstax.org/oscms-prodcms/media/documents/Clinical-Nursing-Skills-WEB.pdf"},{"type":"read","url":"https://openstax.org/books/clinical-nursing-skills/pages/1-introduction"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike License 4.0","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"textbook","identifiers":{"source_id":"75dc0490-e1d0-4c96-b05a-d59274e287cc","openstax_slug":"clinical-nursing-skills","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/"},"providers":[{"source":"OpenStax","source_id":"75dc0490-e1d0-4c96-b05a-d59274e287cc","source_url":"https://openstax.org/details/books/clinical-nursing-skills","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://assets.openstax.org/oscms-prodcms/media/documents/Clinical-Nursing-Skills-WEB.pdf"},{"type":"read","url":"https://openstax.org/books/clinical-nursing-skills/pages/1-introduction"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike License 4.0","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:263395224d7e8e2247a78669","title":"Coastal Cities of the Future in Contemporary Literature","subtitle":"Literary and Urban Form in Times of Climate Uncertainty","description":"Focusing on writing about contemporary coastal cities, this open access book demonstrates how literature – in different genres, media, and cultural-geographical contexts – participates in shaping urban imaginaries in the face of climate crisis. The current century has been heralded as the global urban century, a time in which more than half the population of the world is living in urban environments. At the same time, cities and their inhabitants, and coastal cities in particular, are at the forefront of global change, as sites that are particularly vulnerable to climate change and rising sea levels. Coastal cities face an existential crisis that is aligned with the crisis of all life on the planet, in which to imagine a possible future is to acknowledge the possibility of extinction, but also to imagine and work towards more desirable futures. Contemporary literature has long engaged in the framing of these challenges, and this book examines texts by writers such as Ben Lerner and Kim Stanley Robinson, Antti Tuomainen and Annika Luther, Renate Dorrestein and Ramsey Nasr that do just that. Adopting a comparative approach and focusing on cities like New York, Helsinki, Amsterdam and Antwerp, this book shows us a set of ways in which particular cities imagine their future – even their future destruction – but also a set of models, some fraught, others potentially empowering, to think of urban crisis and possible urban form in different contexts. The ebook editions of this book are available open access under a CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 licence on bloomsburycollections.com. Open access was funded by Tampere University.","authors":["Ameel, Lieven"],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"Bloomsbury Publishing (UK)","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["New York","Helsinki","Amsterdam","Literary urban studies","Urban studies","Climate change","Urban form","Rising waters","Kim Stanley Robinson","Antti Tuomainen","Jonathan Lethem","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism::DSM Comparative literature","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism::DSK Literary studies: fiction, novelists and prose writers","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism::DSB Literary studies: general::DSBH Literary studies: c 1900 to c 2000","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism::DSB Literary studies: general"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/117062","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/180daa95-34c2-4466-a940-b2c66df02144/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"creative_commons","