Waves Research","Astrophysical Phenomena and Observations","Astronomy and Astrophysical Research"],"source":"OpenAlex","source_url":"http://arxiv.org/abs/astro-ph/9411032","cover_url":"","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/astro-ph/9411032"}],"access":"open_access","license":"Open Access; license not reported by OpenAlex","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"article","identifiers":{"source_id":"W2078534649","openalex_id":"W2078534649"},"providers":[{"source":"OpenAlex","source_id":"W2078534649","source_url":"http://arxiv.org/abs/astro-ph/9411032","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/astro-ph/9411032"}],"access":"open_access","license":"Open Access; license not reported by OpenAlex","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:3983ec6db5f45f3e2e7ef2b1","title":"Competencias digitales y lenguas extranjeras: Un enfoque formativo para la educación universitaria","subtitle":"","description":"This book presents the results of research conducted at the Enrique Guzmán y Valle National University of Education (Peru), focusing on analyzing the relationship between the development of digital skills and foreign language learning among pre-service teachers. The Foreign Languages program at this institution follows a dual model in which English is required and is complemented by a second foreign language: Italian, French, or German, both with equal curricular weight. The book highlights how the acquisition of digital skills such as information literacy, online collaboration, digital content creation, security, and problem-solving—directly influences the quality of language learning. Based on a theoretical foundation that integrates current pedagogical approaches, it is proposed that mastery of technological tools not only facilitates access to digital resources and environments but also transforms teaching methodologies, fosters student autonomy, and strengthens their role as active agents in the educational process. The work provides empirical evidence on the need to train teachers capable of integrating digital resources into language teaching in a critical, creative, and pedagogically grounded manner. In an interconnected and changing world, this work offers an updated and relevant approach to understanding the challenges and opportunities of university education in the digital age.","authors":["Lavado-Rojas, Betty Marlene","Pomahuacre-Gómez, Walter","Castro-Fernández, Magnolia Anyeli","Castellano-Inga, Alex Fredy","Zárate-Aliaga, Edith Consuelo","López-Torres, Magaly"],"language":"es","year":2025,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/qcvl9663","subjects":["Competencias digitales","Aprendizaje de lenguas extranjeras","Docentes en formación","Alfabetización informacional","Metodologías didácticas","thema EDItEUR::C Language and Linguistics::CJ Language teaching and learning::CJA Language teaching theory and methods::CJAD Language teaching and learning: second or additional languages"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178526.2","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/553a35e0-0e93-4923-9e26-c1ce42f59ae4/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/178526.2","handle":"20.500.12854/178526.2","dspace_uuid":"21c2671c-a9d6-4daa-a5a2-00a685774b23"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/178526.2","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178526.2","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:7676ba22b4217911497f912d","title":"Competencias docentes para la educación en línea en el nivel superior","subtitle":"","description":"In an era in which education has transcended physical classrooms, online teaching has become a fundamental pillar of contemporary higher education. Teaching Competencies for Online Education in Higher Education is an essential work that provides an in-depth analysis of the challenges, transformations, and opportunities faced by university educators in digital environments. The book explores how online education goes beyond the mere use of technology, requiring the development of comprehensive competencies that integrate pedagogical, digital, and socio-emotional dimensions. Throughout its chapters, it offers a complete overview of the evolution of distance education, the characteristics of virtual learning environments, and the regulatory frameworks that support them. Furthermore, it highlights the role of the teacher as a mediator of learning in hybrid contexts, where communication, interaction, and assessment acquire new meanings. The work delves into the use of active methodologies such as problem-based learning, project-based learning, the flipped classroom, case studies, and virtual simulations, demonstrating their practical application in higher education. In addition, it addresses current major challenges, including inclusion, accessibility, continuous teacher training, and the sustainability of constantly evolving digital educational models. More than a theoretical text, this book becomes a strategic guide for understanding and addressing the changes in contemporary education. It is an essential read for those who believe that teaching, even in virtual environments, remains a profoundly human, transformative, and forward-looking endeavor.","authors":["Soria-León, Norma Graciela","Espinoza-Soria, María José"],"language":"es","year":2026,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/myxf4249","subjects":["Competencias docentes digitales","Entornos virtuales de aprendizaje","Metodologías activas (ABP, aula invertida)","Mediación pedagógica en línea","Inclusión y accesibilidad digital","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JN Education::JNT Teaching skills and techniques::JNTC Competence development"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178512.2","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/09a44015-c88d-4f85-aa8b-e1ec6d29425c/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/178512.2","handle":"20.500.12854/178512.2","dspace_uuid":"9e447bb3-3e56-4a78-b603-7882a1a8a200"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/178512.2","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178512.2","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:1ff5965acb0e27a9d4aaa078","title":"Competing Perspectives of Development","subtitle":"","description":"Developmental policies frequently have contradictory effects. These typically play out in different sectors of life and are analyzed in different academic disciplines, using different assumptions, methods and bodies of literature. The results translate into conflicting political demands. This volume argues that keeping two separate narratives distorts reality and prevents a full understanding of development and its challenges. Over the last 200 years, life has become better. People around the world have grown taller and lived longer, benefitting from growing wealth, better nutrition, better housing, better clothing, more tax revenues and better healthcare policies. Life has also become worse: two centuries of industrialization have caused pollution, wasteful consumerism and climate change threatening predominantly the livelihoods of those least responsible, exacerbating global inequality. But these narratives describe different but inseparable elements of the same history. 13 papers explore ways to integrate the \"good\" and \"bad\" narratives into coherent, intertwined histories, using theoretical analyses and case studies from five continents. It is the first publication to centrally focus on this question and its repercussions.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["History of development","Development contradictions","India","Global south_x000D_","Geschichte","Entwicklung","Widersprüche","Indien","Globaler Süden","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History::NHB General and world history","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116825","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/4430f6ce-0933-4029-acfa-07923ab81820/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/b8f0862d-ca6a-4485-a8a0-81e3376e55e6/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116825","handle":"20.500.12657/116825","dspace_uuid":"d1d50bc9-bf12-4037-982d-6321d213954a"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116825","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116825","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/b8f0862d-ca6a-4485-a8a0-81e3376e55e6/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:a685f3bdf94895f3fb179259","title":"Complete Short Works of George Meredith","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Meredith, George"],"language":"en","year":null,"publisher":"Project Gutenberg","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["English fiction -- 19th century","Category: Adventure","Category: British Literature","Category: Romance","Category: Short Stories"],"source":"Project Gutenberg","source_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4499","cover_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/4499/pg4499.co