shells, lecture slides, instructor answer keys, and more), all OpenStax textbooks are fully customizable. Explore our texts below and adopt any and all parts us","{'id': 40, 'meta': {'type': 'books.BookCategories'}, 'subject_name': 'Science', 'subject_category': 'Biology'}"],"source":"OpenStax","source_url":"https://openstax.org/details/books/concepts-biology","cover_url":"https://assets.openstax.org/oscms-prodcms/media/documents/concpets_biology_eZrc8yQ.svg","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://assets.openstax.org/oscms-prodcms/media/documents/Concepts-Biology_-_WEB.pdf"},{"type":"read","url":"https://openstax.org/books/concepts-biology/pages/1-introduction"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike License 4.0","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"textbook","identifiers":{"source_id":"b3c1e1d2-839c-42b0-a314-e119a8aafbdd","openstax_slug":"concepts-biology","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/"},"providers":[{"source":"OpenStax","source_id":"b3c1e1d2-839c-42b0-a314-e119a8aafbdd","source_url":"https://openstax.org/details/books/concepts-biology","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://assets.openstax.org/oscms-prodcms/media/documents/Concepts-Biology_-_WEB.pdf"},{"type":"read","url":"https://openstax.org/books/concepts-biology/pages/1-introduction"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike License 4.0","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:51d08d450efeb5b8870c007f","title":"Concepts of modern mathematics","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Ian Stewart"],"language":"en","year":1975,"publisher":"Dover","isbn":["0486284247","9781306346030","0140218491","1306346037","9780486284248","0486134954","9780486134956","8420621870","9780140218497","9788420621876"],"doi":"","subjects":[],"source":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL175879W","cover_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/311680-M.jpg","formats":[],"access":"digital_lending","license":"","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"OL175879W","openlibrary_work":"OL175879W","openlibrary_edition":"OL21522393M","internet_archive":"conceptsofmodern0000stew_m2t9"},"providers":[{"source":"Open Library","source_id":"OL175879W","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL175879W","language":"en","formats":[],"access":"digital_lending","license":"","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:12c6f53828571777cad65019","title":"Connected Philology","subtitle":"Interdisciplinary Perspectives on Transcultural Encounters","description":"Even though the similarities of philological methods and traditions across various cultures have been the subject of scholarly research, the reasons for these occurrences usually remain obscure. The present volume addresses this obscurity through introducing the concept of 'Connected Philology' from an interdisciplinary perspective. 'Connected Philology' explores underlying causes for similarities in philological practices: in the process of re-textualisation, written and oral traditions are translated, reformulated, and combined; the contact with foreign cultures leads to the expression of unfamiliar concepts in other languages, and the reconceptualisation of word meanings. In addition, such practices are understood in the context of an interplay between politics, society, and individual actors. The contributions focus on transcultural encounters, the subsequent movement of texts, processes of cultural transfer, as well as the history and politics of connected and connecting philology. Connected Philology transcends both national and disciplinary boundaries within philology and establishes connections with history, cultural studies, and linguistics.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Philology","Transculturality","Methodology of Humanties","Cultural connectivity","Philologie","Transkulturalität","Methodologie","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism::DSB Literary studies: general","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116832","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/bdee672d-4ad4-4ec5-ac7e-969513a49192/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/b07a76a7-68f8-4f96-9df5-c06832b2191e/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116832","handle":"20.500.12657/116832","dspace_uuid":"5ece49d7-d9b4-4520-b1cc-508b3e473cce"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116832","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116832","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/b07a76a7-68f8-4f96-9df5-c06832b2191e/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:f1189f49a3b2d1be2ade0fdf","title":"Connected Philology","subtitle":"Interdisciplinary Perspectives on Transcultural Encounters","description":"Even though the similarities of philological methods and traditions across various cultures have been the subject of scholarly research, the reasons for these occurrences usually remain obscure. The present volume addresses this obscurity through introducing the concept of 'Connected Philology' from an interdisciplinary perspective. 'Connected Philology' explores underlying causes for similarities in philological practices: in the process of re-textualisation, written and oral traditions are translated, reformulated, and combined; the contact with foreign cultures leads to the expression of unfamiliar concepts in other languages, and the reconceptualisation of word meanings. In addition, such practices are understood in the context of an interplay between politics, society, and individual actors. The contributions focus on transcultural encounters, the subsequent movement of texts, processes of cultural transfer, as well as the history and politics of connected and connecting philology. Connected Philology transcends both national and disciplinary boundaries within philology and establishes connections with history, cultural studies, and linguistics.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Philology","Transculturality","Methodology of Humanties","Cultural connectivity","Philologie","Transkulturalität","Methodologie","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism::DSB Literary studies: general","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181410","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/92544901-5e0b-4f92-bb5f-775999ed98aa/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116832/1/9783111432861.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181410","handle":"20.500.12854/181410","dspace_uuid":"a0e7e6ee-56d7-482b-9117-b4fe4ed218d7"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181410","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181410","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116832/1/9783111432861.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:76b378f5a942fd1d5f4b35cd","title":"Connecting Deliberation and Voting in Democratic Innovations","subtitle":"Variations and Perspectives on Hybrid Designs","description":"This is an open access title available under the terms of a CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 License. It is free to read, download and share via Elgaronline, thanks to generous funding support from the Dutch Research Council (NWO) Open Access Books grant no. 36.201.114 and the Tilburg University Library Open Access Book Fund. This discerning book examines the promise and practice of hybrid democratic innovations that combine voting and deliberation within a single participatory design while remaining anchored in representative democracy. While traditional scholarship has predominantly focused on either vote-centric or talk-centric forms of participation, this book shifts attention to hybrid models that harness the complementary strengths of both.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"Edward Elgar Publishing","isbn":[],"doi":"10.4337/9781035353323","subjects":["Democratic Innovations; Hybrid Democratic Innovations; Voting; Deliberation; Deliberative Referendum; Citizens' Assembly","JPHV","JPP","JPQB","JPA"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181612","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/3b5d545e-46e9-4138-9a5f-a515e7943229/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"read","url":"https://www.elgaronline.com/edcollbook-oa/book/9781035353323/9781035353323.xml"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181612","handle":"20.500.12854/181612","dspace_uuid":"c02a5df9-89d7-47a2-ad5e-923d7facfc22"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181612","source_url":"https://dire