g/books/contemporary-mathematics/pages/1-introduction"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike License 4.0","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"textbook","identifiers":{"source_id":"7193a423-3ad7-4ac6-98dd-90c70e4724b7","openstax_slug":"contemporary-mathematics","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/"},"providers":[{"source":"OpenStax","source_id":"7193a423-3ad7-4ac6-98dd-90c70e4724b7","source_url":"https://openstax.org/details/books/contemporary-mathematics","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://assets.openstax.org/oscms-prodcms/media/documents/contemporary-mathematics_-_WEB.pdf"},{"type":"read","url":"https://openstax.org/books/contemporary-mathematics/pages/1-introduction"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike License 4.0","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:5c8978149c82ffa24319c0f5","title":"Contemporary Mathematics in Context","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["McGraw-Hill"],"language":"es","year":2002,"publisher":"Schools","isbn":["9780078275371","0078275415","0078275423","0078275466","0078275377","0078307287","0078618193","9780078275401","9780078693007","9780078618208","9780078275388","9780078275418","9780078275494","9780078275463","9780078275500","0078618207","9780078275425","0078275504","9780078618192","0078275407","9780078307287","0078693004","0078275490","0078275385"],"doi":"","subjects":[],"source":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL14996311W","cover_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1089430-M.jpg","formats":[],"access":"digital_lending","license":"","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"OL14996311W","openlibrary_work":"OL14996311W","openlibrary_edition":"OL9263944M","internet_archive":"contemporarymath00mcgr_0"},"providers":[{"source":"Open Library","source_id":"OL14996311W","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL14996311W","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"digital_lending","license":"","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:3fb5a9a37114fb2cbe45e1a3","title":"Contemporary Trends in Sharia","subtitle":"Critical Debates in Historical Contexts","description":"This open access reference book is a critical analysis of sharia for the 21st century. It serves as a critical introduction to a modernist, progressive and neo-traditionalist perspective on Islamic thought and practice regarding sharia. This approach reflects the efforts undertaken by Muslims - particularly those in the diaspora - to forge an alternative Muslim modernity based on creative engagement with both Islamic tradition and modern Western forms of knowledge. The book highlights the ground-breaking work of some of these seminal thinkers in various fields of law. The book is divided into thirteen chapters. It first covers what sharia is, its origins and how it developed in real time for Muslim societies. This discussion is then followed by chapters on each of the most challenging subjects of Islamic law in the contemporary world, including: constitutionalism, human rights, gender justice, biomedical ethics, religious freedom, criminal law, economics and finance and property rights. Each of these themes is discussed by the co-authors in light of the state-of-the-art literature available, each topic’s individual history, and the current debates and diverse global case studies that relate to each theme. The aim is to highlight that there is no monolithic version of sharia. Rather, sharia is an active set of humanistic principles that inspires Muslims around the world to live according to the ethics of their faith. The book is a collaboration by two experts from different professional backgrounds and aims to take a panoramic view of the subject to appeal to a wide audience. Each chapter can be read ‘stand alone’ while contributing to the book’s broader framework. All together, the chapters challenge misconceptions about sharia and showcase the developments surrounding sharia in the Muslim world and within the Muslim diaspora. The ebook editions of this book are available open access under a CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 licence on bloomsburycollections.com. Open access was funded by The Institute of Ismaili Studies.","authors":["Enayat, Hadi","Keshavjee, Mohamed"],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"Bloomsbury Publishing (UK)","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Sharia","Islamic Law","Secularism","Religious Freedom","Criminal Justice","Gender","Bopethics","Property","Fiqh","Ijtihad","Quran","Sunna","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QR Religion and beliefs::QRP Islam::QRPF Islam: sacred texts and revered writings::QRPF1 The Koran (Qur’an)","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QR Religion and beliefs::QRP Islam::QRPB Islam: branches and groups","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JB Society and culture: general::JBS Social groups, communities and identities::JBSR Social groups: religious groups and communities","thema EDItEUR::5 Interest qualifiers::5P Relating to specific groups and cultures or social and cultural interests::5PG Relating to religious groups::5PGP Relating to Islamic / Muslim people and groups","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QR Religion and beliefs::QRP Islam","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QR Religion and beliefs::QRP Islam::QRPP Islamic life and practice","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History::NHG Middle Eastern history"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181539","cover_url":"","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"open access","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181539","handle":"20.500.12854/181539","dspace_uuid":"3b20893f-bd52-45d7-afc2-0ee28ac84b1b"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181539","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181539","language":"en","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"open access","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:aed13c2896c57306f124d739","title":"Contractualist State-building and Economic Freedom in Africa","subtitle":"Reorienting Development Governance","description":"This book examines the necessary political-economic conditions for successful state-building in Africa, developing a contractualist framework that redefines the role of the state and reconfigures the relationship between individuals and state institutions. It bridges the divide between contractarian (liberal) theory and practice by offering case-based insights into the challenges of applying liberal principles in diverse cultural settings in the post-colonial world. Cases on Rwanda, Ethiopia, and Somaliland help illustrate why and how states should prioritize economic freedom and liberal governmentality to enact contractualist transitions. It argues that stable, organic states in Africa can only emerge through institutions that facilitate and codify free, voluntary transactions among autonomous individuals. This book will be of key interest to scholars and students of African Studies, Political Economy, Comparative Politics, and Development Studies.","authors":["Demerew, Kaleb"],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"Taylor & Francis","isbn":[],"doi":"10.4324/9781003639565","subjects":["State fragility","Contractualist transitions","International development","Post-Colonial State-building","Positive sovereignty","Neoliberal Development-Globalization Nexus","Liberal governmentality","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History::NHT History: specific events and topics::NHTQ Colonialism and imperialism","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JP Politics and government"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/117020","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/4b795e31-d3ef-424d-a1ba-de7a6b380d1a/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/117020","handle":"20.500.12657/117020","dspace_uuid":"621d3564-7d25-4e01-8b4c-7a2444b78bc6","doab_source_id":"20.500.12854/181420","doab_handle":"20.500.12854/181420","doab_dspace_uuid":"c095ce49-7331-4b3b-8748-de2a2deb26b8"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/117020","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/117020","language":"en","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true},{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181420","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181420","language":"en","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"open access","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:f2bcdb3f59d3164d04032b55","title":"Control de versiones con Subversion","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Ben Collins-Sussman","Brian W. Fitzpatrick","C. Michael Pilato"],"language":"es","year":null,"publisher":"","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Programación","Subversion"],"source":"Free Programming Books","source_url":"http://svnbook.red-bean.com/nightly/es/index.html","cover_url":"","formats":[{"type":"html","url":"http://svnbook.red-bean.com/nightly/es/index.html"}],"access":"author_free","license":"","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"3bb0aab1d91143ec2894","list_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EbookFoundation/free-programming-books/main/books/free-programming-books-es.md"},"providers":[{"source":"Free Programming Books","source_id":"3bb0aab1d91143ec2894","source_url":"http://svnbook.red-bean.com/nightly/es/index.html","language":"es","formats":[{"type":"html","url":"http://svnbook.red-bean.com/nightly/es/index.html"}],"access":"author_free","license":"","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:280bb7864a76731dfbf6be8f","title":"Control inteligente y eficiencia energética en refrigeración industrial","subtitle":"","description":"The book examines the high energy consumption of refrigeration systems in the food industry, with a particular focus on the Ecuadorian context. The research was conducted in a company located in Valle Hermoso parish, Santo Domingo canton, Santo Domingo de los Tsáchilas province, Ecuador; the company’s name is kept confidential. Challenges were identified related to high energy costs, thermal fluctuations, and premature equipment wear, resulting from the absence of advanced control systems in the refrigeration chambers. The work integrates theoretical and practical foundations on automatic control and mathematical modeling of critical variables such as temperature, humidity, pressure, and airflow, as well as the application of intelligent control strategies, including PID, predictive (MPC), adaptive, and neural controllers. Simulation models were developed in Simulink to evaluate system dynamics and validate closed-loop responses under different conditions. Results showed that neural controllers applied to temperature achieved a stable response with a 7.99% overshoot and a settling time of 378.12 seconds, while the adaptive controller for humidity reached optimal performance with 0% overshoot and 65.39 seconds settling time. Variables such as pressure and airflow also showed significant improvement under adaptive control, demonstrating stability and rapid adjustment. This book represents an academic and technical contribution for students, researchers, and professionals in control, automation, and energy efficiency, illustrating how intelligent control techniques can optimize industrial refrigeration systems, reduce energy consumption, improve environmental sustainability, and ensure the quality of food products.","authors":["Galeas-Rodríguez, Jessica Carolina","Torres-Quijije, Ángel Iván"],"language":"es","year":2025,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/nrck3115","subjects":["Refrigeración industrial","Control inteligente","Eficiencia energética","Controladores neuronales","Modelamiento matemático","thema EDItEUR::P Mathematics and Science::PH Physics::PHD Classical mechanics::PHDY Energy"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178537.2","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/fa444e82-86d0-46e4-b3f2-93636a109bf8/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/178537.2","handle":"20.500.12854/178537.2","dspace_uuid":"b198aec7-0a8d-4b00-adae-70931ec908ce"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/178537.2","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178537.2","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:9a95b22211449869b6ad053e","title":"Convex Optimization","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Stephen Boyd","Lieven Vandenberghe"],"language":"en","year":2004,"publisher":"IEEE RESOURCE CENTERS","isbn":[],"doi":"10.1017/cbo9780511804441","subjects":["Advanced Optimization Algorithms Research","Matrix Theory and Algorithms","Numerical Methods and Algorithms"],"source":"OpenAlex","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.17023/etpt-7q23","cover_url":"","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Open Access; license not reported by OpenAlex","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"W2296319761","openalex_id":"W2296319761"},"providers":[{"source":"OpenAlex","source_id":"W2296319761","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.17023/etpt-7q23","language":"en","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Open Access; license not reported by OpenAlex","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:c43c55299517bd48d3f8ae9a","title":"Copyright's Paradox","subtitle":"","description":"Copyright is at once an engine of free expression and impediment to free expression. Copyright law underwrites much literature, journalism, music, art, and film. Yet copyright often stands in the way of speech that would build upon existing expression to convey new messages and artistic perspectives. In a seminal 1970 article, Melville Nimmer, the leading copyright and First Amendment scholar of his day, aptly termed the copyright‐free speech conflict a “largely ignored paradox.” Yet today that conflict has come virulently to the fore, and copyright is increasingly chastised as a tool of private censorship. Why has that happened? What values and practices does the copyright‐free speech conflict put at stake? How should the conflict be resolved? These are the principal questions this book seeks to answer. This book explores the copyright‐free speech conflict as it cuts across traditional and digital media alike. In so doing, it juxtaposes the dramatic expansion of copyright holders' proprietary control against individuals' newly found ability to digitally cut, paste, edit, remix, and distribute popular sound recordings, movies, TV programs, graphics, and texts the world over. It tests whether, in light of these developments and others, copyright still serves as a vital engine of free expression and assesses how copyright does—and does not—burden speech. Taking First Amendment values as its lodestar, the book argues that copyright should be delimited by how it can best promote robust debate and expressive diversity, and it presents a blueprint for how that can be accomplished.","authors":["Weinstock Netanel, Neil"],"language":"en","year":2008,"publisher":"Oxford University Press","isbn":[],"doi":"10.1093/acprof:oso/9780195137620.001.0001","subjects":["Copyright","Free speech","Free expression","First amendment","Digital","Media","Expressive diversity","Remix","Journalism","Movies","thema EDItEUR::L Law::LN Laws of specific jurisdictions and specific areas of law::LNR Intellectual property law","thema EDItEUR::L Law::LN Laws of specific jurisdictions and specific areas of law::LNR I