: British Literature","Category: Novels"],"source":"Project Gutenberg","source_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/394","cover_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/394/pg394.cover.medium.jpg","formats":[{"type":"html","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/394.html.images"},{"type":"epub","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/394.epub3.images"},{"type":"mobi","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/394.kf8.images"},{"type":"text","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/394.txt.utf-8"}],"access":"public_domain","license":"Public domain in the United States","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"394","gutenberg_id":"394"},"providers":[{"source":"Project Gutenberg","source_id":"394","source_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/394","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"html","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/394.html.images"},{"type":"epub","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/394.epub3.images"},{"type":"mobi","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/394.kf8.images"},{"type":"text","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/394.txt.utf-8"}],"access":"public_domain","license":"Public domain in the United States","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:685056a84f411b9b8981416f","title":"Crime and Punishment","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Dostoyevsky, Fyodor"],"language":"en","year":null,"publisher":"Project Gutenberg","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Crime -- Psychological aspects -- Fiction","Detective and mystery stories","Murder -- Fiction","Psychological fiction","Saint Petersburg (Russia) -- Fiction","Best Books Ever Listings","Category: Classics of Literature","Category: Crime, Thrillers and Mystery","Category: Novels","Category: Russian Literature","Crime Fiction","Harvard Classics"],"source":"Project Gutenberg","source_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/2554","cover_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/2554/pg2554.cover.medium.jpg","formats":[{"type":"html","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/2554.html.images"},{"type":"epub","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/2554.epub3.images"},{"type":"mobi","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/2554.kf8.images"},{"type":"text","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/2554.txt.utf-8"}],"access":"public_domain","license":"Public domain in the United States","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"2554","gutenberg_id":"2554"},"providers":[{"source":"Project Gutenberg","source_id":"2554","source_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/2554","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"html","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/2554.html.images"},{"type":"epub","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/2554.epub3.images"},{"type":"mobi","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/2554.kf8.images"},{"type":"text","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/2554.txt.utf-8"}],"access":"public_domain","license":"Public domain in the United States","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:c13271b68c9b20ee0334142f","title":"Crossing Borders, Advancing Scholarship","subtitle":"Sociologists of Chinese Descent Traversing Diaspora, Ethnic, and Migration Studies","description":"Spanning personal narratives and scholarly inquiry, this volume presents thirteen autobiographical accounts from sociologists of Chinese descent whose research is deeply informed by their lived experiences as immigrants or children and grandchildren of immigrants. This groundbreaking collection offers a rare and illuminating perspective on how migration shapes research trajectories, theoretical frameworks, and knowledge production. Through these intimate reflections, contributors explore the methodological challenges of studying communities in which they occupy the dual position of insider and outsider. Their accounts reveal the intersections of personal history and professional development, highlighting the broader social and political contexts – spanning mainland China, Hong Kong, Taiwan, and migrant host societies such as the United States and Canada – that have influenced their careers. Crossing Borders, Advancing Scholarship offers both a methodological toolkit and a thought-provoking exploration of how diasporic lives shape scholarly work. It not only deepens our understanding of diasporic identity but also serves as an inspiring guide for emerging researchers navigating the complexities of academia and ethnic belonging.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Asian American Studies","Ethnic Studies","Comparative Sociology","Komparative Soziologie","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JH Sociology and anthropology::JHB Sociology","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JH Sociology and anthropology::JHB Sociology::JHBD Population and demography"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116878","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/ec1ee90a-3010-412b-a7d2-74bc9ad945f5/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/8ab0228d-8199-4f03-8613-d57f10ea458a/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116878","handle":"20.500.12657/116878","dspace_uuid":"0370a348-7545-4c8d-8b09-cc63f25c838c"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116878","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116878","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/8ab0228d-8199-4f03-8613-d57f10ea458a/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:a22f8efa970db26a12a6d0ee","title":"Cryptonomicon","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Neal Stephenson"],"language":"de","