"","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"053438f57f69e9aa5197","list_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EbookFoundation/free-programming-books/main/books/free-programming-books-es.md"},"providers":[{"source":"Free Programming Books","source_id":"053438f57f69e9aa5197","source_url":"http://librosweb.es/libro/css_avanzado","language":"es","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://openlibra.com/es/book/download/css-avanzado"},{"type":"html","url":"http://librosweb.es/libro/css_avanzado"}],"access":"author_free","license":"","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:94070a945621eba231c66885","title":"CSS3 y JavaScript avanzado","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Jordi Collell Puig"],"language":"es","year":null,"publisher":"","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Programación","HTML and CSS"],"source":"Free Programming Books","source_url":"https://openlibra.com/es/book/download/css3-y-javascript-avanzado","cover_url":"","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://openlibra.com/es/book/download/css3-y-javascript-avanzado"}],"access":"author_free","license":"","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"4bbdd4a2d231be602c17","list_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EbookFoundation/free-programming-books/main/books/free-programming-books-es.md"},"providers":[{"source":"Free Programming Books","source_id":"4bbdd4a2d231be602c17","source_url":"https://openlibra.com/es/book/download/css3-y-javascript-avanzado","language":"es","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://openlibra.com/es/book/download/css3-y-javascript-avanzado"}],"access":"author_free","license":"","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:2f6f834ce6a5e04ac370285d","title":"Cuando el mundo se siente distinto: nuevas miradas sobre el autismo, la neurodiversidad y la transformación humana","subtitle":"","description":"Autism spectrum disorder represents one of the greatest scientific, clinical, and societal challenges of the twenty-first century. Its remarkable heterogeneity requires moving beyond the fragmented approaches that have traditionally separated genetics, neuroscience, psychology, education, and the behavioral sciences. This book provides an integrative and up-to-date perspective, bringing together the most significant advances from these disciplines to understand autism through a transdisciplinary, evidence-based, and person-centered approach. Across its seven chapters, the book examines the evolution of the neurodiversity paradigm, the neurobiological mechanisms of development, genetics, pharmacogenetics, biomarkers, neuroinflammation, brain connectivity, the gut–brain microbiota axis, metabolism, nutrition, psychopharmacology, and emerging technologies applied to assessment and intervention. It also explores motor impairments, social cognition, empathy, friendship, functional communication, and support strategies that promote autonomy, quality of life, and the social participation of autistic individuals. Rather than presenting a simple compilation of information, this work builds bridges between basic research and clinical practice, between medicine and education, and between scientific evidence and the everyday experiences of autistic individuals and their families. The result is a contemporary reference that integrates the latest knowledge with an ethical and humanistic perspective, providing an essential resource for researchers, healthcare professionals, educators, therapists, university students, and policymakers committed to fostering a deeper, more inclusive, and scientifically grounded understanding of autism.","authors":["García-Cruz, Rubén","Ortiz-Nieto, Fernando"],"language":"es","year":2026,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/nctx1284","subjects":["trastorno del espectro autista","neurodiversidad","neurociencia","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JN Education::JNC Educational psychology"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181621","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/cc49c33f-2f23-4944-9cfa-082b3066440d/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://sophiaeditions.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Ebook978-1-968794-53-8.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-SA","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181621","handle":"20.500.12854/181621","dspace_uuid":"2d974d21-1550-444d-aa3f-f3b945d16ae5"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181621","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181621","language":"es","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://sophiaeditions.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Ebook978-1-968794-53-8.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-SA","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:0eca6f4cf75c3ee4e751f67b","title":"Cuidados de enfermería pediátrica: Manual didáctico médico-quirúrgico","subtitle":"","description":"This book is an essential guide for nursing professionals in training and in practice, designed to strengthen clinical, technical, and humanistic competencies for the comprehensive care of pediatric patients. The work systematically addresses the main medical and surgical conditions and procedures affecting children and adolescents, including neurological disorders, infectious, respiratory, renal, hematologic, endocrine, and dermatological diseases, burns, surgical care, and palliative care. All recommendations and protocols are supported by updated scientific evidence and enriched by the authors’ clinical experience, offering a reliable, practical, and applicable resource for hospital, outpatient, and community settings. Each chapter includes assessment tools, intervention and follow-up strategies, caregiver education guidelines, and recommendations for emotional support, ensuring safe, efficient, and child- and family-centered care. The book integrates theory and practice with human sensitivity, promoting multidisciplinary coordination and the comprehensive management of complex conditions, from seizure syndromes and eating disorders to specialized surgical procedures and grafting techniques. It also provides clear guidelines for palliative care, ensuring quality of life and emotional well-being for pediatric patients. Written in accessible and didactic language, this manual becomes an indispensable resource for academic training and professional development in nursing, empowering practitioners to deliver safe, efficient, and humanized pediatric care.","authors":["Soto-Hilario, Juvita Dina","Torres-Condori, Gladys Maruja","Fabián-Flores, Florián Gualberto","Quispe-Coyla, Mario","Llanos-de Tarazona, Marina Ivercia","Ramírez-Montaldo, Rosalinda"],"language":"es","year":2025,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/qjyk3352","subjects":["Enfermería pediátrica","Atención integral","Cuidados humanizados","Evidencia científica","Procedimientos clínicos","thema EDItEUR::M Medicine and Nursing"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178543.2","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/8fcbfbf8-d397-4315-b7c2-81822cc51494/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/178543.2","handle":"20.500.12854/178543.2","dspace_uuid":"e1ad26d7-54f8-4b65-997c-b4bfefa0b2dc"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/178543.2","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178543.2","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:352768ea643b6dfbea20806b","title":"Cultivo de pepino (Cucumis sativus L.): Respuestas morfoagronómicas y aplicaciones de nanopartículas de quitosano","subtitle":"","description":"This book explores the transformative potential of chitosan nanoparticles in cucumber (Cucumis sativus L.) cultivation, a strategic crop due to its economic, nutritional, and social value worldwide. In the face of current agricultural challenges such as excessive fertilizer use, pest and disease pressure, and the effects of climate change, this research proposes innovative solutions that combine biotechnology and nanotechnology for more efficient and sustainable production. Chitosan, a natural biopolymer with antimicrobial and biostimulant properties, and its nanoparticle versions are presented as key tools to enhance vegetative growth, improve fruit quality, and reduce dependence on chemical inputs. Their application favors nutrient absorption, water retention, and plant resistance to both biotic and abiotic stresses, promoting healthier and more sustainable crops. The study was conducted under controlled greenhouse conditions at the “La María” Experimental Campus of the Technical State University of Quevedo (UTEQ), Ecuador, allowing precise management of agricultural variables such as irrigation, fertilization, and planting density. The results demonstrate that the application of chitosan nanoparticles optimizes vegetative growth, fruit development, and crop quality, offering practical alternatives for a more efficient, resilient, and environmentally responsible agriculture. Furthermore, the research contributes to the academic and professional development of students, consolidating a horticultural production model that integrates science, innovation, and sustainability. This book not only provides scientific evidence but also inspires producers, researchers, and students to adopt innovative practices that merge knowledge, technology, and environmental responsibility, consolidating an agricultural model that is efficient, resilient, and environmentally conscious.","authors":["Tipán-Torres, Hilda Cristhina","Reyes-Pérez, Juan José"],"language":"es","year":2025,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/revy8225","subjects":["Nanopartículas de quitosano","Cultivo de pepino","Biotecnología agrícola","Sostenibilidad","Bioestimulantes","thema EDItEUR::T Technology, Engineering, Agriculture, Industrial processes::TV Agriculture and farming::TVF Sustainable agriculture"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178532.2","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/4559f113-e06c-4f9b-b5b8-a96de6d69498/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/178532.2","handle":"20.500.12854/178532.2","dspace_uuid":"029c8541-4f8e-4806-82cf-30f7386ce594"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/178532.2","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178532.2","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:ef7cc18c7659f30e4274c2f9","title":"Cultura, conocimiento y acción: hacia una gestión educativa eficiente","subtitle":"","description":"This work offers a profound reflection on how knowledge management, organizational culture, and motivation become strategic pillars to improve efficiency and quality in educational institutions. The text is based on an applied analysis at the District Directorate 09D15 Empalme-Educación, located in the province of Guayas, Ecuador, where it is evident that limited knowledge transfer and the low valuation of internal knowledge hinder the effective execution of the Annual Operational Plan, affecting institutional productivity and the quality of educational services. The text articulates three essential dimensions: culture, understood as the set of values and practices that sustain organizational dynamics; knowledge, viewed as a strategic resource that must be shared and applied; and action, which translates that knowledge and values into concrete results. Through an integral approach, the work demonstrates how knowledge management can transform education, generating resilient, innovative organizations capable of responding to contemporary challenges. Beyond a contextual study, this publication provides a replicable theoretical and methodological framework, fostering academic and practical debate on institutional efficiency and continuous improvement. It is a call to leaders, teachers, and managers to transform knowledge into living culture and collective action, showing that efficient educational management can drive progress, justice, and equity, positively impacting communities and contributing to the construction of more sustainable societies aware of their educational development in Ecuador, Latin America, and the Caribbean.","authors":["Moreira-Segovia, Rosa Vanessa","Zambrano-Barros, Nuvia Aurora"],"language":"es","year":2025,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/pgqs1557","subjects":["Gestión del conocimiento","Cultura organizacional","Motivación","Eficiencia institucional","Calidad educativa","thema EDItEUR::K Economics, Finance, Business and Management::KJ Business and Management::KJM Management and management techniques::KJMK Knowledge management"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178538.2","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/28d25bb2-e090-449d-bb5e-d8d66f2058d4/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/178538.2","handle":"20.500.12854/178538.2","dspace_uuid":"7e6f4e69-99fc-4850-853c-ed109b03a658"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/178538.2","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178538.2","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:eb1357e8fc1b95142da57b6c","title":"Cultura de evaluación en prácticas institucionales de acreditación de programas educativos","subtitle":"","description":"The accreditation of educational programs derives from the demands issued by international organizations and the growing interest of Higher Education Institutions (HEIs) in having programs with quality recognition. However, the problem with these processes is that they are carried out from the administrative level, which implies that the participation or perception of the students is not involved. The objective of this book is to base, from the perceptions of the students, the culture of evaluation that is attributed to the institutional practices of accreditation of educational programs, helping to propose actions that contribute to their improvement at the Autonomous University of the State of Hidalgo.","authors":["Cruz Colín, Lucero Quetzall","Cáceres Mesa, Maritza Librada","Veytia Bucheli, María Guadalupe","Hernández Márquez, Jorge"],"language":"es","year":2024,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/tokh2851","subjects":["Acreditación educativa","Percepción estudiantil","Calidad educativa","Evaluación institucional","Mejora continua","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JN Education"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178546.2","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/984e6d80-4178-40d1-bae3-8de79d1ddceb/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/178546.2","handle":"20.500.12854/178546.2","dspace_uuid":"d54fccef-cb6b-4628-b599-f76e3f797e99"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/178546.2","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178546.2","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:4ebf4f7df9a6137e3c4a9aa2","title":"Cultural Game Studies","subtitle":"Critical Approaches","description":"Cultural Game Studies provides a comprehensive framework for understanding games and play as interconnected cultural phenomena, examining their roles as art, entertainment, and human experience within contemporary society. This edited volume delivers a societally and culturally informed critical framework that enables readers to develop a nuanced understanding of game cultures and their scholarship. Rather than studying games or players in isolation, the book contextualises the uses, design, and meanings of play as an interconnected whole. Readers will gain detailed insights into the scholarly history of game studies and its key methodologies, while exploring essential themes including player identities, game production, cultural literacy, and game preservation. The book’s comprehensive approach opens new perspectives for cultural analysis and provides tools for understanding how games increasingly permeate and inform modern society and culture. This book is written for researchers, scholars, and advanced students in game studies, cultural studies, media studies, and digital humanities. It is ideal for academics seeking to deepen their theoretical understanding of game cultures, graduate students conducting research in game-related fields, and instructors teaching courses on digital culture, media theory, or contemporary cultural phenomena. The Open Access version of this book, available at http://www.taylorfrancis.com, has been made available under a Creative Commons Attribution-Non Commercial-No Derivatives (CC BY-NC-ND) 4.0 license.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"Taylor & Francis","isbn":[],"doi":"10.4324/9781003679851","subjects":["Digital humanities","Ludology","Player identity research","Media theory analysis","Transmedia storytelling","Game preservation studies","Critical analysis of game cultures","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JB Society and culture: general::JBC Cultural and media studies::JBCT Media studies::JBCT1 Media studies: internet, digital media and society","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JB Society and culture: general::JBC Cultural and media studies::JBCC Cultural studies","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JB Society and culture: general::JBC Cultural and media studies::JBCT Media studies","thema EDItEUR::A The Arts","thema EDItEUR::U Computing and Information Technology::UG Graphical and digital media applications::UGN Digital animation","thema EDItEUR::K Economics, Finance, Business and Management::KN Industry and industrial studies::KNT Media, entertainment, information and communication industries"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116990","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/110a88c6-737d-4a24-9e99-893f734aca49/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/6d226d7c-83f3-4464-9549-139a910208f7/retrieve"},{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116990/1/9781040750322.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116990","handle":"20.500.12657/116990","dspace_uuid":"4fa0f38a-49be-43c0-97e7-1d364184d19b","doab_source_id":"20.500.12854/181386","doab_handle":"20.500.12854/181386","doab_dspace_uuid":"9f634698-a749-449c-b8ce-96f44ee02c60"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116990","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116990","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/6d226d7c-83f3-4464-9549-139a910208f7/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true},{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181386","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181386","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116990/1/9781040750322.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:52d50daefd6f65bb3d37e1de","title":"Cultural Heritage and Slavery","subtitle":"A Perspective from the Caribbean","description":"The book series of the Bonn Center for Dependency and Slavery Studies publishes monographs and edited volumes that examine different phenomena of slavery and other forms of strong asymmetrical dependencies in societies. The series follows the BCDSS’s research agenda in going beyond the dichotomy of slavery versus freedom by proposing a new key concept, strong asymmetrical dependency, which covers all forms of bondage across time and space. This includes debt bondage, convict labor, tributary labor, servitude, serfdom, and domestic work, as well as forms of wage labor and various types of patronage. Works published in this series will also investigate periods, regions and contexts in world history that have not been directly affected by Western colonization, such as the ancient Near East, pre-modern and modern societies in Asia, Africa, and the pre-colonial Americas. Language Policy Dependency and Slavery Studies With its mission to explore phenomena of asymmetrical dependency, the Bonn Center for Dependency and Slavery Studies (BCDSS) and its book series Dependency and Slavery Studies work against forms of gatekeeping which may put obstacles in the way of scholarly work in English felt to be non-standard. The Center and its book series understand language to be intimately connected to power structures and strive to foster an awareness of epistemic dependencies resulting from linguistic dependencies. Given that language is multiply situated and constantly evolving, the editors of Dependency and Slavery Studies do not insist on conformity to the traditional binary standard Englishes (British and American). Authors are thus encouraged to write in their national or regional variety of English.","authors":[],"language":"es","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Cultural heritage","Slavery","The Carribbean","Kulturerbe","Sklaverei","Karibik","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History::NHK History of the Americas","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History::NHT History: specific events and topics::NHTB Social and cultural history","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181389","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/7541ca95-0b81-4262-8571-cec38939fa25/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116673/1/9783112223055.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181389","handle":"20.500.12854/181389","dspace_uuid":"e529b050-3796-43b7-a5fa-705975797cf3"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181389","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181389","language":"es","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116673/1/9783112223055.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:fea01ac54d6755c14832168d","title":"Cultural stereotypes as gatekeepers: increasing girls’ interest in computer science and engineering by diversifying stereotypes","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Sapna Cheryan","Allison Master","Andrew N. Meltzoff"],"langua