e on water resources demands a transformation in the way irrigation is designed, operated, and managed. In this context, this book presents a comprehensive approach that integrates hydraulic engineering, industrial automation, and digital technologies to develop systems capable of optimizing water use while achieving high levels of efficiency, reliability, and sustainability. The book goes beyond the conventional approach of technical manuals by integrating the scientific foundations of water management with the design, implementation, programming, validation, and maintenance of an automated sprinkler irrigation system developed through an applied research project. Throughout its chapters, the book addresses sustainable water management, the hydraulic principles of sprinkler irrigation, the design and integration of electrical, electronic, and hydraulic components, the programming of Programmable Logic Controllers, system monitoring, fault protection mechanisms, performance evaluation, and maintenance strategies. From an interdisciplinary perspective, it demonstrates how the interaction among sensors, actuators, control systems, and hydraulic networks enables the development of smart infrastructure capable of reducing water and energy consumption, improving operational performance, and enhancing environmental sustainability. Rather than merely documenting a specific project, this publication provides a transferable methodological framework for designing automated systems applicable to agriculture, green spaces, and hydraulic infrastructure. Through its balance of scientific rigor and practical application, it serves as a valuable reference for students, educators, researchers, and professionals in hydraulic, agricultural, environmental, electronic, mechatronics, and industrial engineering, as well as for institutions committed to technological innovation and the efficient management of water resources. In a context shaped by digital transformation, the Internet of Things, and artificial intelligence, this book provides the conceptual and technical foundations needed to advance a new generation of smart irrigation systems aimed at enhancing water security and promoting sustainable development.","authors":["Casimiro-Urcos, Walther Hernán","Quinteros-Osorio, Roger Octavio","Hinojosa-Bautista, Jorge Armando","Tello-Conde, Angel Ricardo","Osorio-Osorio, Adolfo"],"language":"es","year":2026,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/ghhs8237","subjects":["Automatización industrial","riego por aspersión","gestión hídrica","thema EDItEUR::T Technology, Engineering, Agriculture, Industrial processes"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/180565.2","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/b0e61b69-d444-4419-add5-0aa7c89defdf/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://sophiaeditions.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Ebook_978-1-968794-52-1.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-SA","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/180565.2","handle":"20.500.12854/180565.2","dspace_uuid":"0353cade-7c9b-469b-9799-6c85d0b46f0a"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/180565.2","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/180565.2","language":"es","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://sophiaeditions.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Ebook_978-1-968794-52-1.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-SA","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:1e38992e9b5e84abc0cf998a","title":"Dissecting racial bias in an algorithm used to manage the health of populations","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Ziad Obermeyer","Brian W. Powers","Christine Vogeli","Sendhil Mullainathan"],"language":"en","year":2019,"publisher":"eScholarship (California Digital Library)","isbn":[],"doi":"10.1126/science.aax2342","subjects":["Healthcare cost, quality, practices","Health Systems, Economic Evaluations, Quality of Life","Healthcare Systems and Reforms"],"source":"OpenAlex","source_url":"https://escholarship.org/uc/item/6h92v832","cover_url":"","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://escholarship.org/content/qt6h92v832/qt6h92v832.pdf?t=q5l8ac"}],"access":"open_access","license":"Open Access; license not reported by OpenAlex","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"article","identifiers":{"source_id":"W2981869278","openalex_id":"W2981869278"},"providers":[{"source":"OpenAlex","source_id":"W2981869278","source_url":"https://escholarship.org/uc/item/6h92v832","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://escholarship.org/content/qt6h92v832/qt6h92v832.pdf?t=q5l8ac"}],"access":"open_access","license":"Open Access; license not reported by OpenAlex","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:e2d2ffc469239038aea105ff","title":"Distributed Systems","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Andrew S. Tanenbaum","Maarten Van Steen"],"language":"es","year":2001,"publisher":"CreateSpace Independent Publishing Platform","isbn":["9781543057386","9780130888938","0132392275","9781530281756","0130888931","9780136135531","0136135536","1282651315","9780131217867","1543057381","9781282651319","9781292025520","9780132392273","9788120334984","0131217860","9702612802","9789702612803","8120334981","1292025522","153028175X"],"doi":"","subjects":[],"source":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1970672W","cover_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9378755-M.jpg","formats":[],"access":"digital_lending","license":"","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"OL1970672W","openlibrary_work":"OL1970672W","openlibrary_edition":"OL9294557M","internet_archive":"distributedsyste00tane"},"providers":[{"source":"Open Library","source_id":"OL1970672W","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1970672W","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"digital_lending","license":"","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:e106187554ac9692a38fd567","title":"Diversidad, neurodivergencia e inclusión educativa: Aproximaciones teóricas desde la educación contemporánea","subtitle":"","description":"This book offers a comprehensive perspective on how education can be transformed to effectively address student diversity at all levels. It examines the principles of inclusive education, emphasizing its nature as both a right and a process, and analyzes how neurodivergence, learning disorders, autism, attention deficit hyperactivity disorder (ADHD), and giftedness require pedagogical approaches that recognize and value cognitive differences. Additionally, it addresses ethnic and cultural diversity in Latin America and the Caribbean, exploring identity, interculturality, the historical impacts of colonialism, and contemporary struggles for rights recognition, showing that educational inclusion must also consider the cultural and social richness of each context. The work combines theory and practice by presenting concrete strategies such as Universal Design for Learning, curricular adaptations, reasonable accommodations, differentiated instruction, and flexible planning, aiming to ensure access, participation, learning, and well-being for all students. Furthermore, it reflects on school coexistence and the creation of equitable and participatory educational spaces, emphasizing the importance of clear institutional policies, monitoring, and inclusive evaluation. This book is an essential guide for teachers, researchers, and policymakers, inspiring the construction of more just, accessible, and enriching schools capable of fostering inclusive societies that respect human diversity in all its dimensions.","authors":["Rojas-Valladares, Adalia Lisett","Domínguez-Urdanivia, Yideira","Lafita-Frómeta, Roelbis"],"language":"es","year":2026,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/ilnx2136","subjects":["Educación inclusiva","Diversidad","Neurodivergencia","Diseño universal para el aprendizaje (DUA)","Equidad educativa","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JN Education::JNF Educational strategies and policy::JNFK Educational strategies and policy: inclusion"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178505.2","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/19444b32-7c43-432e-ba6a-a4f7343dfa12/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/178505.2","handle":"20.500.12854/178505.2","dspace_uuid":"f7f4a50a-67b7-4689-820e-f8aa4e4d33a9"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/178505.2","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178505.2","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:fc3e235291d9e6412b0a5e2b","title":"Divisions and Definitions","subtitle":"Syriac School Manuals on Aristotle’s Logic (6th–9th C.)","description":"The seven Syriac texts published in this volume are school manuals on logic composed between the 6th and the 9th centuries AD, the time of the decline of the traditional Greek paideia and the rise of Christian education. They explicate and adapt for Christian schools the main terminology of Aristotle’s Categories and Porphyry’s Isagoge . The earliest witness among them is based primarily on Sergius of Reshaina’s commentary on the Categories and Proba’s commentary on the Isagoge , and it presents the subject matters of these treatises in the form of tree diagrams. The collections of tree diagrams and short excerpts from such commentaries served as sources for the new schoolbooks containing philosophical divisions. These schoolbooks in turn became sources for the later manuals on logic published here. Ultimately, these later manuals were more focused on theological polemics than they were on Aristotle’s and Porphyry’s original texts. They thereby grant us insight into the context in which Aristotle and Porphyry were studied within the Christian schools and into the evolving school tradition during the period of transition from late antiquity to the early middle ages.","authors":["Arzhanov, Yury"],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Porphyry","Syriac Christianity","Logic","Porphyrius","Christentum in Syrien","Logik","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QD Philosophy::QDT Topics in philosophy::QDTL Philosophy: logic","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QR Religion and beliefs::QRM Christianity","thema EDItEUR::Y Children’s, Teenage and Educational::YP Educational material::YPJ Educational: Humanities and social sciences, general::YPJH Educational: History"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181503","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/b17ac34e-dab4-4b4b-b720-373aaea011a1/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116768/1/9783112234358.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181503","handle":"20.500.12854/181503","dspace_uuid":"90082ec2-33ff-49b4-879e-c2a101745cf6"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181503","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181503","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116768/1/9783112234358.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:a545ead41b47e89c146329cf","title":"Docentes conectados: Evaluando las competencias digitales en la Educación Superior","subtitle":"","description":"This book offers a comprehensive analysis of the fundamental role that digital competencies play in the contemporary university environment. It examines how the convergence of technology and pedagogy has transformed teaching, establishing a new educational paradigm. Key concepts such as digital competencies for teachers, their dimensions, and their impact on teaching practice are addressed. It also delves into digital literacy as a central element of professional development, highlighting the importance of training in the educational use of Information and Communication Technologies (ICTs), as well as in technology-mediated didactic innovation. The text presents a study conducted in the Peruvian university context, presenting an empirical study. Through the analysis of data collected at five public and three private universities, the digital competencies of teachers are assessed in three main dimensions: digital literacy, ICT teaching, and digital content creation. The findings reveal heterogeneous levels of competency, as well as various structural and training challenges that must be addressed. The book concludes by offering strategic recommendations to strengthen teacher training and promote the effective integration of ICTs in Peruvian higher education. This work is essential for academic administrators, trainers, and teachers interested in improving educational quality in 21st-century digital environments.","authors":["Casimiro-Urcos, Walther Hernán","Casimiro-Urcos, Consuelo Nora","Quinteros-Osorio, Roger Octavio","Tello-Conde, Ángel Ricardo","Casimiro-Guerra, Giorgia"],"language":"es","year":2025,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/addh6859","subjects":["Competencias digitales docentes","Alfabetización digital","Didáctica con TIC","Innovación pedagógica","Educación superior peruana","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JN Education"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178518.2","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/d4caa64b-2a33-44a6-8416-bc647df451ac/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/178518.2","handle":"20.500.12854/178518.2","dspace_uuid":"bc487dac-5202-45a3-b06e-233f80c0e58a"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/178518.2","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178518.2","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:fada3ebd8aca70b736c13fc5","title":"Docker","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Bruno Cascio"],"language":"es","year":null,"publisher":"","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Programación","Misceláneos"],"source":"Free Programming Books","source_url":"https://github.com/brunocascio/docker-espanol","cover_url":"","formats":[],"access":"author_free","license":"","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"915e1303333745f66279","list_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EbookFoundation/free-programming-books/main/books/free-programming-books-es.md"},"providers":[{"source":"Free Programming Books","source_id":"915e1303333745f66279","source_url":"https://github.com/brunocascio/docker-espanol","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"author_free","license":"","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:ed5cea6911a343bf6c6bde7b","title":"Doctor Cupid: A Novel","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Broughton, Rhoda"],"language":"en","year":null,"publisher":"Project Gutenberg","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["English fiction -- Welsh authors","Category: British Literature","Category: Novels","Category: Romance"],"source":"Project Gutenberg","source_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/35548","cover_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/35548/pg35548.cover.medium.jpg","formats":[{"type":"text","url":"https://www.gutenberg.