EN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116895","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/e3b19ee8-5707-497b-9688-3ac3c2c8a994/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/5e86ba76-11d6-43c6-a77c-7dfcb6e76c80/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116895","handle":"20.500.12657/116895","dspace_uuid":"c645e834-1b6d-416e-a8ff-9f40a1983bb8"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116895","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116895","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/5e86ba76-11d6-43c6-a77c-7dfcb6e76c80/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:a83c6554b961d8fd5b2b38f7","title":"Dynamic and Diagnostic Language Assessment","subtitle":"Learning across Frameworks to Support Second/Foreign Language Education","description":"How can assessment shed light on learners’ current abilities and help chart a path for their continued development? Dynamic assessment and diagnostic language assessment are both now well established in the second language (L2) field, and while they emerge from different theoretical traditions, they share a commitment to pursuing this question. The chapters in this volume showcase innovative work in both approaches undertaken by leading scholars around the world. Each chapter also offers insight into the complementary nature of the approaches, ultimately raising the possibility of how they might together form a powerful new assessment framework.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Dynamic assessment","Diagnostic Assessment","Second","Foreign Language (L2)","Sociocultural Theory","SLA","Fremdsprache","Language Assessment","Soziokulturelle Theorie","Zweitsprache","thema EDItEUR::C Language and Linguistics::CF Linguistics","thema EDItEUR::C Language and Linguistics::CJ Language teaching and learning"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181590","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/aaf65b40-7bf7-42d2-9ec8-53ead6b7d2d6/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116895/1/9783111233918.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181590","handle":"20.500.12854/181590","dspace_uuid":"f7ecc573-4e26-4d53-a426-74903395a849"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181590","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181590","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116895/1/9783111233918.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:798ba837e802d772f9a7c5a9","title":"Dynamics at the Lexicon-Syntax Interface","subtitle":"Creativity and Routine in Word-Formation and Multi-Word Expressions","description":"Both word-formation (WF) and the coinage of multi-word expressions (MWE) can be characterised in terms of creativity and routine. Routine in word-formation and multi-word expressions is traditionally described in terms of morphological, lexical, syntactic, and pragmatic rules, but ‘creativity’ is defined in different ways, with definitions ranging from seeing creativity at the heart of human (linguistic) cognition to seeing creativity as precisely beyond ‘regular’ routines, e.g. as an attention-seeking tool or wordplay. In this latter sense, ‘creativity’ is usually sharply distinguished from ‘productivity’, i.e. rule-governed behaviour. Despite these categorisations, the question on what basis patterns are to be defined as ‘creative’ still remains subject to debate. Futhermore, creativity and routine are often studied independently of each other, by different research communities. The volume aims to bring together these different research communities to discuss empirical evidence on the role of creativity and routinization in WF and MWEs.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Creativity","Productivity","Routinisation","Pattern_x000D_","thema EDItEUR::C Language and Linguistics::CF Linguistics","thema EDItEUR::C Language and Linguistics::CJ Language teaching and learning","thema EDItEUR::C Language and Linguistics::CF Linguistics::CFF Historical and comparative linguistics"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116925","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/0da842d9-c1ea-493f-974b-4c269226d80d/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/929c456c-9269-4383-8d66-f9e31a5fe5e1/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116925","handle":"20.500.12657/116925","dspace_uuid":"06538a7d-b2bf-471d-8a05-5e4dce0d1d82"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116925","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116925","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/929c456c-9269-4383-8d66-f9e31a5fe5e1/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:62c784fa194dea67a803b989","title":"Earth System Law","subtitle":"Governing Planetary Transformations in the Anthropocene","description":"Written by leading experts, this open access book provides the first comprehensive and critical exploration of Earth system law. Environmental law, as it stands, does not meet the challenge of governing the many complex planetary transformations of the Anthropocene. Earth system law marks a new legal paradigm—replacing the fragmented, human-centred, state-based approach with an integrated, Earth-centred approach to planetary governance, purpose-built for our turbulent epoch. The book offers innovative proposals for legal principles, actors, institutions, and ethics designed to safeguard the stability and integrity of Earth’s life-support systems. It also delivers the first full stocktake of the Earth system law framework and its scholarship, coupled with a forward-looking research and implementation agenda. Earth System Law is for all those who are frustrated by the persistent inability of environmental law to address the interconnected governance challenges of the Anthropocene—and for those ready to help shape the next legal frontier. Researchers, students, practitioners, and policymakers alike will find here both the vision and the tools to rethink law for a human-dominated planet. The ebook editions of this book are available open access under a CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 licence on bloomsburycollections.com. Open access was funded by the Bloomsbury Open Collections Library Collective.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"Bloomsbury Publishing (UK)","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Earth system governance","Earth system science","Ethics of care","Ecological integrity","Ecological law","Kinship","Legal principles","Planetary boundaries","Planetary justice","Sustainable development","thema EDItEUR::L Law::LB International law::LBB Public international law::LBBP Public international law: environment","thema EDItEUR::L Law::LA Jurisprudence and general issues::LAB Methods, theory and philosophy of law","thema EDItEUR::L Law::LN Laws of specific jurisdictions and specific areas of law::LNK Environment, transport and planning law: general::LNKJ Environment law","thema EDItEUR::L Law::LA Jurisprudence and general issues"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/117063","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/20c13b4d-0ccd-417f-90a3-11ba60643eee/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/6910a903-54b6-4cb3-92ab-d7c1d18f2879/retrieve"},{"type":"epub","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/6c9c5dc1-21c5-412f-8527-b239c57f45a5/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/117063","handle":"20.500.12657/117063","dspace_uuid":"fe71ce64-de17-4302-934a-77a8a53b74d0"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/117063","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/117063","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/6910a903-54b6-4cb3-92ab-d7c1d18f2879/retrieve"},{"type":"epub","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/6c9c5dc1-21c5-412f-8527-b239c57f45a5/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:7563f039c334b7d33733dcc2","title":"Ecce Homo: Complete Works, Volume Seventeen","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Nietzsche, Friedrich Wilhelm"],"language":"en","year":null,"publisher":"Project Gutenberg","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Nietzsche, Friedrich Wilhelm, 1844-1900","Philosophers -- Germany -- Biography","Category: Biographies","Category: Philosophy & Ethics"],"source":"Project Gutenberg","source_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/52190","cover_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/52190/pg52190.cover.medium.jpg","formats":[{"type":"html","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/52190.html.images"},{"type":"epub","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/52190.epub3.images"},{"type":"mobi","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/52190.kf8.images"},{"type":"text","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/52190.txt.utf-8"},{"type":"text","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/files/52190/52190-0.txt"}],"access":"public_domain","license":"Public domain in the United States","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"52190","gutenberg_id":"52190"},"providers":[{"source":"Project Gutenberg","source_id":"52190","source_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/52190","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"html","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/52190.html.images"},{"type":"epub","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/52190.epub3.images"},{"type":"mobi","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/52190.kf8.images"},{"type":"text","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/52190.txt.utf-8"},{"type":"text","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/files/52190/52190-0.txt"}],"access":"public_domain","license":"Public domain in the United States","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:7b304a73061fb04395126582","title":"Echo-Literatur im deutschen 17. Jahrhundert","subtitle":"Diskursivierung, Medialisierung, Vergemeinschaftung","description":"Das Echo ist im 17. Jahrhundert nicht nur im gesamten literarischen Gattungsspektrum anzutreffen, sondern repräsentiert zentrale Aspekte eines modernen dichterischen Selbstverständnisses. Diese Studie macht die Vielfalt der Echo-Symboliken und -Funktionalisierungen im deutschen Barock zugänglich, insbesondere für die Zeit von 1640 bis 1700. Dabei wird das Gebrauchsschrifttum erstmals angemessen berücksichtigt. Der literarische Echo-Dialog schwankt antithetisch zwischen sozialem Ausschluss und kommunikativer Hoffnungssuggestion. In der italienischen und französischen Renaissance-Lyrik dominiert der Ausschluss: Die Echo-Begegnung im einsamen Naturraum ist Signum des isolierten Subjekts. Diese Poetik wird im deutschen 17. Jahrhundert sukzessive in ihr Gegenteil verkehrt. Ausgehend von konsolatorischen Deutungen wandelt sich das Echo zu einem Paradigma der Diskursivität und Vergemeinschaftung. Mit der Einbettung in neue Gattungen und Kontexte wird es zu einer Form des poetischen Diskurses und verkörpert eine Poetik der Sozialität und des Konsens. Als Natursprache und Landschaftsmetonymie schafft es ästhetische, soziale und politische Identitätsräume; und als metaphysische Stimme und raumzeitliche Transgressionsfigur suggeriert es die Verbindung zum Göttlichen.","authors":["Leimgruber, Damaris"],"language":"de","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Early Modern period","Poetry","Echo","Frühe Neuzeit","Barock","Mythos","Lyrik","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism::DSB Literary studies: general::DSBD Literary studies: c 1600 to c 1800","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism::DSC Literary studies: poetry and poets"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181541","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/e2e35712-ddd8-4c43-909f-7007875267b4/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116734/1/9783111664859.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181541","handle":"20.500.12854/181541","dspace_uuid":"c1229c21-ab05-4c88-8024-e186ca2a9fca"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181541","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181541","language":"de","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116734/1/9783111664859.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:a14eb80961239b937ed23130","title":"Ecología Emocional y Aprendizaje en Entornos Digitales Universitarios","subtitle":"","description":"This book explores how managing the socio-emotional skills ecosystem directly influences learning achievement in digital university environments. Through applied research with 200 students from the Faculty of Early Childhood Education at the National University of Education “Enrique Guzmán y Valle” (Peru), the author analyzes how skills such as self-regulation, empathy, self-esteem, assertive communication, and decision-making enable students to function more effectively in virtual learning spaces. The work is based on a solid theoretical foundation on socio-emotional skills in higher education, integrating approaches such as constructivism, connectivism, and social learning, which explain how knowledge is constructed in the digital age. Key dimensions of digital literacy, critical thinking, online problem-solving, and emotional management in technology-mediated contexts are identified. Likewise, the study delves into the levels of digital learning achievement, from basic use to advanced levels of autonomy and academic leadership. The research concludes that, in an increasingly technological educational environment, socio-emotional skills not only complement cognitive development but are essential for sustaining motivation, fostering collaboration, managing stress, and adapting to the diversity of virtual settings. Strengthening this ecosystem represents a key educational strategy for achieving meaningful, humane, and sustainable learning in contemporary universities.","authors":["Montañez-Huancaya de Salinas, Aquila Priscila","Figueroa-Hurtado, Fany Silvana","Montañez Huancaya, Norma Nancy","Roca-Avila, Yovana Connie","Arainga-Blas, Eusebio","Yupanqui-Cueva, Iris Marisol"],"language":"es","year":2025,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/kdye6536","subjects":["Habilidades socioemocionales","Aprendizaje digital","Entornos virtuales","Autorregulación","Educación superior","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JN Education"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178525.2","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/b8719b08-108b-47d2-84b8-410ac58a943b/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/178525.2","handle":"20.500.12854/178525.2","dspace_uuid":"1aa738d0-da37-44a5-8bdf-79e1ba9cf202"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/178525.2","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178525.2","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:15931b76262376c7bfa22d51","title":"Ecological Interdependencies","subtitle":"Strong Asymmetrical Relations and More-than-Human Worlds","description":"This volume interrogates the environmental humanities through the lens of asymmetrical dependencies: it is interested in investigating the relationship between the environment and asymmetrical power dynamics, an approach that sheds light on how historical and contemporary inequalities have shaped and still shape our social, political and cultural realities as they intersect with their respective ecosystems. In an attempt to bridge disciplines, the volume synthesizes diverse perspectives from the humanities and social sciences – anthropology, art history, cultural studies, archaeology, religious studies, political science, and literary studies –, attending to the tangled and often thorny relationships that form human and more-than-human existence. By incorporating ecological viewpoints and recognizing the agency of non-human actors, the book aims to amplify the often-overlooked voices of the marginalized, including those beyond the human realm. Understanding the intersections of power dynamics and human history requires acknowledging our deeply interconnected existence within a broader planetary context and this edited volume’s contributions offer a lens through which to rethink enduring questions of difference and dependency. These considerations are framed not as abstract or theoretical exercises but as deeply grounded in material realities shaped by histories of asymmetry, inequality and exploitation, thus challenging us to critically reframe notions of ecological inter/dependencies beyond the universalizing narratives of the Anthropocene.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Ecology","Dependency","Anthropocene","Relationality","Ökologie","Abhängigkeit","Anthropozän","Relationalität","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History","thema EDItEUR::R Earth Sciences, Geography, Environment, Planning::RN The environment"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116815","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/82b4320b-0e5f-4305-a109-3186e1879504/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/761b6f0b-2216-41fe-a8f8-1b20954197a2/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116815","handle":"20.500.12657/116815","dspace_uuid":"66fe2e3a-d88c-44fa-a2dd-2d1accf7cddb"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116815","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116815","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/761b6f0b-2216-41fe-a8f8-1b20954197a2/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:956d50eadba8dae6b674b2be","title":"Ecological Interdependencies","subtitle":"Strong Asymmetrical Relations and More-than-Human Worlds","description":"This volume interrogates the environmental humanities through the lens of asymmetrical dependencies: it is interested in investigating the relationship between the environment and asymmetrical power dynamics, an approach that sheds light on how historical and contemporary inequalities have shaped and still shape our social, political and cultural realities as they intersect with their respective ecosystems. In an attempt to bridge disciplines, the volume synthesizes diverse perspectives from the humanities and social sciences – anthropology, art history, cultural studies, archaeology, religious studies, political science, and literary studies –, attending to the tangled and often thorny relationships that form human and more-than-human existence. By incorporating ecological viewpoints and recognizing the agency of non-human actors, the book aims to amplify the often-overlooked voices of the marginalized, including those beyond the human realm. Understanding the intersections of power dynamics and human history requires acknowledging our deeply interconnected existence within a broader planetary context and this edited volume’s contributions offer a lens through which to rethink enduring questions of difference and dependency. These considerations are framed not as abstract or theoretical exercises but as deeply grounded in material realities shaped by histories of asymmetry, inequality and exploitation, thus challenging us to critically reframe notions of ecological inter/dependencies beyond the universalizing narratives of the Anthropocene.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Ecology","Dependency","Anthropocene","Relationality","Ökologie","Abhängigkeit","Anthropozän","Relationalität","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History","thema EDItEUR::R Earth Sciences, Geography, Environment, Planning::RN The environment"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181426","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/14c93a02-7720-40ae-9ba3-418d6d6ed5e5/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116815/1/9783112217764.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181426","handle":"20.500.12854/181426","dspace_uuid":"ec2dc0f5-53b0-4981-a267-a137bf7934a8"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181426","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181426","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116815/1/9783112217764.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:14a901e53fde6e893cb477b3","title":"Economía familiar sostenible: cómo convertir la eficiencia en bienestar","subtitle":"","description":"The family economy constitutes the foundation of household wellbeing and, by extension, of society. Efficient management of household resources involves not only controlling income and expenses but also planning, making informed decisions, saving consciously, and investing responsibly. Financial stability allows families to meet basic needs, face unforeseen events, guarantee their children’s education, and generate growth opportunities, while fostering responsible consumption habits and promoting economic sustainability. This book presents the results of a Research and Outreach Project conducted by the authors at the Universidad Metropolitana del Ecuador (UMET), Machala campus. The study identified patterns of income, expenses, savings, credit, and investment among Ecuadorian families and contextualized the financial challenges of the local environment, such as income fluctuations, limited access to financial services, and the need to comply with current regulations. The main objective of the study was to contribute to the development of skills in personal income and expense planning and budgeting, promoting responsible use of financial products among adults aged 18 to 65 living in the urban area of Machala canton and in the parish of La Peaña in Pasaje canton. In this way, practical tools were provided to strengthen financial autonomy, encourage saving habits, and enable more informed and sustainable decision-making in managing family resources. To deepen the practical application of these findings, three families from the community received training focused on three main areas: family financial planning; concepts of simple interest, compound interest, interest rates, amortization, and the time value of money; and the use of financial products within households. The book offers strategies adapted to the local context, promoting financial planning, saving, responsible investing, and proper credit management, transforming economic efficiency into tangible wellbeing and fostering sustainable, autonomous, and resilient households.","authors":["Burgo-Bencomo, Odalys Bárbara","López-Vera, Juan Gabriel","Morán-Molina, Germán Gracian"],"language":"es","year":2025,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Economía familiar","Planificación financiera","Ahorro e inversión","Educación financiera","Autonomía económica","thema EDItEUR::A The Arts::AB The arts: general topics::ABQ Art: financial aspects"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178541.2","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/45866c59-76b6-41a8-b527-11902555f2b5/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/178541.2","handle":"20.500.12854/178541.2","dspace_uuid":"cfe6f253-b180-48fc-87be-55ecae75f0fa"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/178541.2","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178541.2","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:0e63ec4b53efc3e234790ecc","title":"Ecotoxicologia, contaminação e segurança alimentar no sul de Angola: desafios para a saúde ecossistémica regional","subtitle":"","description":"This work analyzes, from an interdisciplinary perspective, the relationships between ecotoxicology, environmental contamination, food security, and socio-environmental sustainability in southern Angola. The study addresses the main ecological challenges faced by the region, including desertification, prolonged droughts, water scarcity, degradation of natural resources, environmental pollution, and the impacts of climate change on ecosystems and human populations. The research is grounded in the integration of environmental sciences, public health, sustainable agriculture, environmental engineering, and ecological governance, enabling a comprehensive understanding of the interdependence between environment, food systems, and quality of life. Throughout the book, the ecotoxicological impacts of contamination on fauna, flora, biodiversity, and food systems are discussed, as well as the effects of water, soil, and food pollution on public health and the nutritional security of communities. The work also examines the socio-environmental vulnerabilities of populations in southern Angola, highlighting the importance of family farming, sustainable natural resource management, and the implementation of public policies aimed at territorial sustainability. In addition, the book emphasizes the importance of ecological technologies, the restoration of degraded ecosystems, integrated water management, and environmental governance in promoting climate resilience and food security. It concludes that regional sustainability depends on the articulation between environmental preservation, human development, sustainable innovation, and the strengthening of ecological strategies capable of ensuring greater ecosystem balance, social justice, and quality of life for present and future generations.","authors":["Cristóvão Mandume, Celso Manuel"],"language":"pt","year":2026,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/bupy3753","subjects":["Ecotoxicologia","Segurança alimentar","Sustentabilidade socioambiental","Mudanças climáticas","Governança ecológica","thema EDItEUR::R Earth Sciences, Geography, Environment, Planning::RN The environment::RNC Applied ecology"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178515.2","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/f52e1446-36e4-4d4a-9d96-66eac9bdf82f/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/178515.2","handle":"20.500.12854/178515.2","dspace_uuid":"8bd5144b-3617-4279-a534-7427e1d988e2"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/178515.2","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178515.2","language":"pt","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:4e984cd45611726a299f5b5c","title":"Edición de textos científicos con LaTeX. Composición, gráficos, diseño editorial y presentaciones beamer","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Walter Mora F.","Alexander Borbón A."],"language":"es","year":null,"publisher":"","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Programación","LaTeX"],"source":"Free Programming Books","source_url":"https://tecdigital.tec.ac.cr/servicios/revistamatematica/Libros/LaTeX/MoraW_BorbonA_LibroLaTeX.pdf","cover_url":"","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://tecdigital.tec.ac.cr/servicios/revistamatematica/Libros/LaTeX/MoraW_BorbonA_LibroLaTeX.pdf"}],"access":"author_free","license":"","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"3dc4ce7687dbd43a9beb","list_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EbookFoundation/free-programming-books/main/books/free-programming-books-es.md"},"providers":[{"source":"Free Programming Books","source_id":"3dc4ce7687dbd43a9beb","source_url":"https://tecdigital.tec.ac.cr/servicios/revistamatematica/Libros/LaTeX/MoraW_BorbonA_LibroLaTeX.pdf","language":"es","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://tecdigital.tec.ac.cr/servicios/revistamatematica/Libros/LaTeX/MoraW_BorbonA_LibroLaTeX.pdf"}],"access":"author_free","license":"","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:89ab6e5ae8c4ba240a45d761","title":"Educación Superior en tiempos de inteligencia artificial: pedagogía, evaluación y bienestar","subtitle":"","description":"This work examines the contemporary challenges of higher education in the face of the emergence of generative artificial intelligence, exploring how these technologies are transforming access to information, knowledge production, and the pedagogical, ethical, and humanistic foundations of the university. It proposes an approach that integrates technological innovation with solid pedagogy, formative assessment, and attention to the holistic well-being of both students and faculty. The book presents findings from studies conducted at universities in Ecuador and Mexico, showing how Latin American contexts, with shared structural challenges, are developing innovative, resilient, and socially committed responses. It explores the application of artificial intelligence in teaching, the semi-automated analysis of occupational profiles, and the ethical management of human talent, highlighting opportunities and challenges for academic and professional education. In addition, the volume addresses instructional design in virtual learning environments, the implementation of active learning methodologies, learning assessment, emotionally intelligent teaching, and neuroeducation, as well as curriculum internationalization and educational inclusion. Case studies on selective mutism, social return, and holistic well-being emphasize the need for personalized and holistic strategies in university education. The work argues that higher education must go beyond the mere transmission of knowledge, promoting students’ holistic development, creativity, critical thinking, autonomy, and social responsibility. This approach articulates technology, pedagogy, assessment, and well-being, offering practical guidance for faculty members, researchers, educational leaders, and public policy decision-makers seeking to transform higher education without losing sight of its human dimension.","authors":[],"language":"es","year":2026,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/hbrd5095","subjects":["Inteligencia artificial generativa","Educación superior","Innovación educativa","Neuroeducación","Evaluación del aprendizaje","thema EDItEUR::4 Educational purpose qualifiers"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178500.2","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/ef0de23c-9d2c-45d6-95ce-0322817eb3ef/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/178500.2","handle":"20.500.12854/178500.2","dspace_uuid":"b47a36a4-5fc0-4f8d-aead-37c0982188cc"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/178500.2","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178500.2","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:0fab79cec13e6dd31b75a69c","title":"Education for Sustainability and Global Citizenship","subtitle":"Intercultural, Ethical, and Justice-Based Approaches","description":"Gold Winner of the Nautilus 2026 Book Awards in Social Sciences & Education Grand Prize Winner of the Nautilus 2026 Book Awards How do we address teaching for sustainability and global citizenship for social-ecological justice based on alternative paradigms? This book addresses the implications of the environmental crisis on formal, non-formal and informal education from a human rights position. The author introduces a pedagogical approach called ‘value-creating global citizenship education’ from a study of selected Asian perspectives, building on the UN sustainable development goals, and beyond. The key focus is to develop resilience and hope through engaged relationships between learners and their environments. Examples are drawn from Indigenous knowledge, diverse ecological worldviews and practices including the Earth Charter, the Soka Amazon Institute, and the United Nations Harmony with Nature Knowledge Network that promotes Earth Jurisprudence. The book offers practical solutions for planetary citizenship for educators and policymakers, including teaching and curriculum guidelines that can be used to integrate intercultural perspectives and develop a global outlook. The ebook editions of this book are available open access under a CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 licence on bloomsburycollections.com. Open access was funded by the Bloomsbury Open Collections Library Collective.","authors":["Sharma, Namrata"],"language":"en","year":2025,"publisher":"Bloomsbury Publishing (UK)","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Education for sustainable development","ESD","Global citizenship education","Sustainability education","thema EDItEUR::J Society and S