3976644","9780613897389","9780312873318","9780765374714","0765342405","5170065000","9780312868604","1857239555","9782841721856","8440698283","1857239989","9785170065004","0765374714","1574534939","0756901537","8498725917","9780792737087","8490708371","9788498725919","284172185X","9788440698285","0748134247"],"doi":"","subjects":[],"source":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL49496W","cover_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12009325-M.jpg","formats":[],"access":"digital_lending","license":"","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"OL49496W","openlibrary_work":"OL49496W","openlibrary_edition":"OL27949004M","internet_archive":"lasombradeender0000card"},"providers":[{"source":"Open Library","source_id":"OL49496W","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL49496W","language":"fr","formats":[],"access":"digital_lending","license":"","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:d2a4ee737292ee01954b50ac","title":"Enfoque metabólico en diabetes: abordaje y educación terapéutica","subtitle":"","description":"This work presents a comprehensive, scientific, and applied perspective on the management of diabetes mellitus, from its pathophysiological foundations to its clinical and educational approaches. The book explores in depth the mechanisms of insulin resistance, metabolic signaling, genetic and epigenetic factors, as well as associated complications and comorbidities, providing a solid conceptual framework for understanding the disease in all its complexity. The text includes academic and research contributions from professionals affiliated with national and international institutions, strengthening its scientific rigor and multidisciplinary perspective. The book integrates practical tools for metabolic assessment, glycemic control, and nutritional management, including structured systems such as exchange lists, carbohydrate counting, and updated dietary guidelines. It also addresses diabetes management in critical contexts, highlighting the importance of glycemic control in hospitalized patients and the optimization of insulin therapy and specialized nutrition. A fundamental axis of the work is therapeutic education, understood as an essential pillar of treatment. Evidence-based strategies are developed to strengthen patient autonomy, prevent hypoglycemia, promote exercise as a metabolic intervention, and prevent chronic complications such as diabetic foot. In addition, the book incorporates the psychosocial dimension and the challenges faced by healthcare systems, promoting a person-centered approach. This work proposes a comprehensive care model that integrates science, clinical practice, and education with the aim of improving metabolic outcomes, preventing complications, and transforming diabetes care through knowledge, strategy, and professional commitment.","authors":["Gordillo-Cortaza, Janet Del Rocío","Gómez-Rutti, Yuliana Yessy"],"language":"es","year":2026,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/ubin6823","subjects":["Diabetes mellitus","Fisiopatología","Educación terapéutica","Manejo nutricional","Atención integral","thema EDItEUR::M Medicine and Nursing::MK Medical specialties, branches of medicine::MKZ Therapy and therapeutics"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178506.2","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/dedfbaa0-5ca1-40d4-9abb-8516ceafa450/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/178506.2","handle":"20.500.12854/178506.2","dspace_uuid":"39538003-3748-4fd9-874f-6129e8cb52c0"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/178506.2","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178506.2","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:97aca6ca46afa565b504c626","title":"Engaged Spirituality","subtitle":"Stories of Religious Resilience, Inspiration, and Pursuing the Common Good","description":"This open access book is a testimony to telling good religion stories to advance vital conversations around some of the most critical issues of our time. Written by reporters and researchers who worked for five years with the University of Southern California’s Center for Religion and Civic Culture, this book focuses on some of the greatest challenges to the current human experience; from education, health care and socioeconomic development to environmental justice, gender and sexual equity, and interreligious dialogue. It draws on compelling profiles of spiritually engaged humanitarians motivated by religious values and spiritual practices to reimagine the ways we engage the tangible, troubling realities of contemporary life. Originating from different traditions and diverse corners of the globe, the power and humanity of these portraits help dispel discouragement about the state of the world and instead inspire readers to take positive action to address shared global challenges. The ebook editions of this book are available open access under a CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 licence on bloomsburycollections.com. Open access was funded by Center for Religion and Civic Culture at the University of Southern California.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"Bloomsbury Publishing (UK)","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Spirituality","Stories","Religious stories","Conversations","Political issues","Social issues","Education","Socioeconomic development","Gender equity","Interreligious dialogue","Humanitarianism","Faith","Contemporary living","Religious values","Global challenges","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QR Religion and beliefs::QRA Religion: general","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QR Religion and beliefs::QRV Aspects of religion::QRVP Religious life and practice::QRVP7 Religious aspects of sexuality, gender and relationships","thema EDItEUR::L Law::LB International law::LBB Public international law::LBBS Public international law: humanitarian law","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JP Politics and government::JPF Political ideologies and movements::JPFA Green politics / ecopolitics / environmentalism","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JP Politics and government::JPF Political ideologies and movements","thema EDItEUR::R Earth Sciences, Geography, Environment, Planning::RN The environment::RNA Environmentalist thought and ideology","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QR Religion and beliefs","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JP Politics and government::JPV Political control and freedoms::JPVH Human rights, civil rights"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/117058","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/7310be8e-733d-4fc1-a9dc-432b8fcaba6f/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/daf93d50-a309-4eda-ae72-670c981a3c90/retrieve"},{"type":"epub","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/d70d3920-def8-4eba-a04e-1764bb0b9fd9/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/117058","handle":"20.500.12657/117058","dspace_uuid":"abbac80b-e89c-4032-b34e-428534b9b2dc"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/117058","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/117058","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/daf93d50-a309-4eda-ae72-670c981a3c90/retrieve"},{"type":"epub","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/d70d3920-def8-4eba-a04e-1764bb0b9fd9/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:168221ba08ba3e95ea467c28","title":"Engineering Desire","subtitle":"Algorithmic Environments and the Promise of Wholeness","description":"Why do technological promises remain so compelling? Artificial intelligence, digital platforms and algorithmic systems continue to attract extraordinary levels of attention, investment and hope. Their transformative promise persists despite visible shortcomings, recurring disappointments and mounting social and environmental concerns. Drawing on Lacanian psychoanalysis, Ciano Aydin offers a new way of understanding this enduring appeal. Shifting attention from behavior to desire and from power to receptivity, he reveals the existential dimensions of our investment in algorithmic environments. Using Tinder as a paradigmatic case, the book shows how these environments increasingly organize desire itself by offering recognition, orientation, certainty and the fantasy of wholeness. But algorithmic environments are not merely sites of illusion. The same systems that sustain fantasies of self-knowledge and completion can also lay bare the structure of desire itself. Engineering Desire offers a distinctive framework for understanding both the risks and possibilities of contemporary technological life, rethinking singular self-formation as a possibility within technological mediation.","authors":["Aydin, Ciano"],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"Taylor & Francis","isbn":[],"doi":"10.4324/9781042010912","subjects":["AI","Desire","Subjectivity","Lacanian psychoanalysis","Algorithmic environments","Intimacy","Fantasy of wholeness","Selfhood","Structural lack","Tinder","Predictive feedback","Digital culture","Existential philosophy","Human subjection","Recognition","Algorithmic design","Self-formation","Unconscious longing","Continental philosophy of technology","Existential uncertainty","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QD Philosophy","thema EDItEUR::U Computing and Information Technology::UY Computer science::UYQ Artificial intelligence","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JP Politics and government::JPA Political science and theory","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JM Psychology::JMA Psychological theory, systems, schools and viewpoints::JMAF Psychoanalytical and Freudian psychology","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JH Sociology and anthropology::JHB Sociology","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JB Society and culture: general::JBC Cultural and media studies::JBCC Cultural studies","thema EDItEUR::M Medicine and Nursing::MK Medical specialties, branches of medicine::MKM Clinical psychology::MKMT Psychotherapy","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QD Philosophy::QDH Philosophical traditions and schools of thought::QDHR Western philosophy from c 1800","thema EDItEUR::P Mathematics and Science::PD Science: general issues::PDR Impact of science and technology on society"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/117015","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/cc9ab7aa-e321-42b7-87fa-93c221bfbf4d/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/117015","handle":"20.500.12657/117015","dspace_uuid":"15c96ccc-ac9f-4f48-ba1f-e7aa25497c5e"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/117015","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/117015","language":"en","formats":[],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:830092cb444b9bdfe217c23e","title":"Entendiendo Angular","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Jorge Cano"],"language":"es","year":null,"publisher":"","isbn":[],"doi":"