s/7889/7889-8.txt"}],"access":"public_domain","license":"Public domain in the United States","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:052de7b5bdbe1e8e25a2e626","title":"Errant Letters: Jacques Rancière and the Philosophy of Literature","subtitle":"Studies in Culture, Literary Theory, and History","description":"Jerzy Franczak comprehensively presents Jacques Rancière’s thought by emphasizing the relationship between politics and literature. This detailed analysis takes into account the context of modern aesthetics and political philosophy, as a result, the book introduces further protagonists such as Louis Althusser, Michel Foucault, Pierre Bourdieu, or Jean-François Lyotard. Franczak first reconstructs Rancière’s original philosophy of literature and subsequently apply it in readings of select world literature masterpieces by Gustav Flaubert, Max Jacob, Bertold Brecht, Vladimir Nabokov, and Philip Roth.","authors":["Franczak, Jerzy"],"language":"en","year":2023,"publisher":"Peter Lang International Academic Publishers","isbn":[],"doi":"10.3726/b21035","subjects":["Errant","Franczak","Golubiewski","Jacques","Jerzy","Krzysztof","Letters","Literature","Mikołaj","Modern aesthetics and political philosophy","Nycz","Philosophy","Philosophy of literature","Rancière","Relationship between politics and literature","Ryszard","Smólski","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JP Politics and government::JPA Political science and theory","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism::DSB Literary studies: general","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism::DSM Comparative literature","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QD Philosophy::QDT Topics in philosophy::QDTN Philosophy: aesthetics","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QD Philosophy::QDT Topics in philosophy::QDTS Social and political philosophy","thema EDItEUR::A The Arts::AB The arts: general topics::ABA Theory of art","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism::DSA Literary theory","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JP Politics and government::JPV Political control and freedoms::JPVC Civics and citizenship","thema EDItEUR::A The Arts::AB The arts: general topics","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QD Philosophy","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QR Religion and beliefs::QRA Religion: general::QRAB Philosophy of religion","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JP Politics and government::JPP Public administration","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JP Politics and government::JPR Regional, state and other local government","thema EDItEUR::K Economics, Finance, Business and Management::KC Economics::KCP Political economy","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JP Politics and government::JPQ Central / national / federal government::JPQB Central / national / federal government policies"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116980","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/1c433258-6363-4ac3-bbf7-169587cc9b7f/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/f3710d4b-b264-41a4-836d-61ef27ac49f1/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116980","handle":"20.500.12657/116980","dspace_uuid":"2e8ef259-14af-4c25-a4f1-62e880d687ba"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116980","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116980","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/f3710d4b-b264-41a4-836d-61ef27ac49f1/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:11808dcfa1fab435b611b39d","title":"Escuchar sin palabras: Guía práctica para la intervención en el autismo infantil","subtitle":"","description":"This book offers a comprehensive guide to intervention in autism spectrum disorder, focusing on understanding child development as a unique, dynamic, and contextual process. It acknowledges the diversity of clinical, functional, and communicative profiles within the spectrum and emphasizes the importance of individualized, evidence-based interventions that promote functional communication, self-regulation, social participation, and the child’s overall well-being. The text addresses the crucial role of family and educational environments, highlighting that ongoing interaction between both contexts, together with structured supports, peer mentoring, and adapted strategies, strengthens learning, autonomy, and inclusion in school and social life. The work presents a multidimensional approach that integrates neuroscience, developmental psychology, pedagogy, and behavioral, sensory, and augmentative and alternative communication strategies, enabling learning to be generalized to everyday situations. It also underscores the importance of continuous assessment, planning curricular adaptations, reinforcement systems, and developmental follow-up to ensure sustainable and effective interventions. The guide recognizes the central role of the family as an active agent, promoting empowerment, training, and participation in the application of strategies. Finally, the book provides practical tools, concrete examples, and clear implementation steps for professionals and caregivers, establishing itself as an essential resource that combines theory and practice while fostering a humane, inclusive, and respectful approach to the abilities and needs of every child with autism.","authors":["Sanabria-Boudri, Fanny Miriam","Cerrón-Lliempe, Hans Peter","Quispe-Quispe, Denisse Angela","Razuri-Gamarra, Maritza Yolanda","Orosco-Naveros, Aida Beatriz","Pajares-Briones, Jorge Alberto"],"language":"es","year":2026,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/wszk1361","subjects":["Trastorno del Espectro Autista","Intervención temprana","Inclusión educativa","Comunicación aumentativa y alternativa","Desarrollo infantil","thema EDItEUR::Y Children’s, Teenage and Educational"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178495.2","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/c3f4a0f0-18f2-4855-85b8-9950cd541bf5/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/178495.2","handle":"20.500.12854/178495.2","dspace_uuid":"41454341-1f94-405a-bf69-7579d5ae4c12"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/178495.2","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178495.2","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:09a6cc2b748f18f371443609","title":"Estrategia y competitividad: claves para la gestión de las microempresas","subtitle":"","description":"This work presents the results of a comprehensive study on the influence of strategic management on the competitiveness of manufacturing microenterprises in the Southern Zone of Manabí, Ecuador. The book addresses a highly relevant topic, as microenterprises form the backbone of the local and regional economy but face significant challenges in remaining competitive in an environment marked by volatility, constant innovation, and global market pressures. The study highlights how the lack of a clear vision, limited environmental analysis, inadequate implementation of support policies, and weak adaptation of organizational culture are structural problems that affect microenterprises’ ability to formulate and execute effective strategies. Using a quantitative methodological approach with validated and reliable surveys applied to 62 individuals from 31 companies, the book analyzes strategy formulation, implementation, and evaluation, as well as the relationship between these practices and business competitiveness. As a proposal, it emphasizes the need to strengthen strategic management through clear, customized, and sustainable processes tailored to the characteristics and resources of each microenterprise. The results reveal significant correlations between organizational culture, performance evaluation, motivating vision, and customer knowledge, along with differentiated strategic profiles identified through principal component and cluster analyses. The work concludes that strategic management is not a luxury but an essential factor for achieving sustainable competitive advantages, improving efficiency, optimizing resources, and fostering economic development. This book offers a valuable guide for both researchers and entrepreneurs seeking to transform microenterprises into resilient and competitive organizations.","authors":["Figueroa-Soledispa, Martha Lorena","Jiménez-Chinga, Regina","Zeta-Vite, Adolfo","Suárez-Carrasco, Fernando","Albañil-Ordinola, Guillermina Isabel"],"language":"es","year":2025,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/qwma4693","subjects":["Dirección estratégica","Competitividad","Microempresas","Cultura organizacional","Gestión empresarial","thema EDItEUR::K Economics, Finance, Business and Management"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178540.2","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/b4dfd5ed-4465-4446-be28-3c01ce00e939/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/178540.2","handle":"20.500.12854/178540.2","dspace_uuid":"f3553cf1-7b6f-4bbe-bf2a-08baf6970d5d"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/178540.2","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178540.2","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:57cc9073be09b76d5b471480","title":"Estructura con CSS","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Greg Smith","Isaac Durazo, `trl.:` Isaac Durazo"],"language":"es","year":null,"publisher":"","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Programación","HTML and CSS"],"source":"Free Programming Books","source_url":"http://es.learnlayout.com","cover_url":"","formats":[{"type":"html","url":"http://es.learnlayout.com"}],"access":"author_free","license":"","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"fb82ce8b16493c2e9c71","list_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EbookFoundation/free-programming-books/main/books/free-programming-books-es.md"},"providers":[{"source":"Free Programming Books","source_id":"fb82ce8b16493c2e9c71","source_url":"http://es.learnlayout.com","language":"es","formats":[{"type":"html","url":"http://es.learnlayout.com"}],"access":"author_free","license":"","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:26ed201e43c583482d2a339f","title":"Ethical Perspectives on Artificial Intelligence in Biomedical Engineering","subtitle":"","description":"Artificial intelligence (AI) is currently considered a disruptive key technology in the field of biomedical engineering. However, there is more to it than just the applications, advantages and challenges of AI in this field. The book takes a closer look at various additional aspects and provides a more comprehensive view of AI in healthcare. The first part provides introductory considerations from a historical, technical, socio-scientific, legal and ethical perspectives. Complementing this, the second part illustrates these topics using various applications in the field of biomedical engineering. These cannot be covered exhaustively, but a broad overview is provided and the relevant challenges are addressed. Finally, the last part deals with questions relating to the framework conditions, the regulation of AI and the associated business models. Last but not least, brief introductory statements from the Federal Ministry of Research, Technology and Space and the DGBMT on the topic of AI in biotechnology and healthcare underscore the relevance of the contributions.","authors":["Manzeschke, Prof. Dr. theol. habil. Arne","Wittenberg, Dr.-Ing. Thomas"],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Artificial Intelligence","Ethics","Biomedical Engineering","Responsibility","Digital Sovereignty","thema EDItEUR::U Computing and Information Technology::UY Computer science::UYQ Artificial intelligence"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181418","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/306259e0-4447-45bb-a1bf-d8c1d56757fd/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116765/1/9783111586458.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181418","handle":"20.500.12854/181418","dspace_uuid":"7f3bac7e-ff79-4de8-8169-bfaa38504159"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181418","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181418","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116765/1/9783111586458.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:54eb32a20600d1fd827f8276","title":"Ethik in Seelsorge und Spiritual Care","subtitle":"","description":"The interdisciplinary book series Studies in Spiritual Care (SCC) publishes international research ranging from studies on specific aspects of Spiritual Care to programmatic contributions to the self-understanding of this new practice and research area. The series is of interest to professionals working in the field as well as to students, researchers, and scholars from the fields of medicine, pastoral care, psychotherapy, and social work.","authors":[],"language":"de","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Pastoral Care","Spiritual Care","Ethics","Health Care","Seelsorge","Ethik","Gesundheitswesen","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QR Religion and beliefs::QRV Aspects of religion::QRVG Theology","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QR Religion and beliefs::QRV Aspects of religion::QRVP Religious life and practice::QRVP5 Religious counselling","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QR Religion and beliefs::QRA Religion: general::QRAM Religious issues and debates::QRAM1 Religious ethics","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QR Religion and beliefs::QRA Religion: general::QRAB Philosophy of religion","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QD Philosophy::QDT Topics in philosophy::QDTQ Ethics and moral philosophy","thema EDItEUR::M Medicine and Nursing::MB Medicine: general issues::MBX History of medicine","thema EDItEUR::M Medicine and Nursing::MF Pre-clinical medicine: basic sciences","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QR Religion and beliefs::QRM Christianity"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116872","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/d745aa0c-14b1-4e70-92b6-3e8f7faf2122/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/04d67589-c05b-4d29-8250-331cbdf128de/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116872","handle":"20.500.12657/116872","dspace_uuid":"36cbcd9a-dc02-4645-872f-7b07d24492f4"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116872","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116872","language":"de","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/04d67589-c05b-4d29-8250-331cbdf128de/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:1c274f4049932dcaf8735a78","title":"Ethische Code Oral History","subtitle":"15 principes voor het werken met mondelinge bronnen","description":"Oral histories enrich our understanding of historical developments by fore­grounding the memories and inter­pretations of individuals and groups who experienced these events first­hand. They broaden and deepen the context and meaning of written sources and other forms of heritage, including voices that were previously unheard. The purpose of this Ethical Code for Oral History Netherlands is to advance the further professionalisation of oral history as a discipline. The Code supports creators, custodians and users of oral history interviews in making choices that strengthen participants’ trust in the respectful handling of their recorded interview, while ensuring the findability, accessibility and FAIR­ compliant reuse of interview collections.","authors":[],"language":"nl","year":2026,"publisher":"VU University Press","isbn":[],"doi":"10.66742/eaxg2398","subjects":["Oral history","Interviewen","Archiveren","FAIR","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JH Sociology and anthropology","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JH Sociology and anthropology::JHB Sociology::JHBC Social research and statistics"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/117092","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/3885f17f-47b8-4cd4-89e9-28ae428ba9fe/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/c1c9c9ff-7680-47bd-b0e9-0d7a39f92900/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/117092","handle":"20.500.12657/117092","dspace_uuid":"28fd3203-0ff6-4850-992a-d9271bae477b"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/117092","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/117092","language":"nl","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/c1c9c9ff-7680-47bd-b0e9-0d7a39f92900/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:3d381bff2599877e3187e94b","title":"EU International Insolvency Law and Third Countries","subtitle":"Which Way(s) Forward?","description":"Cross-border insolvencies between EU and third countries are a common phenomenon in business, but only marginally addressed by EU law. Is it time for the EU to adopt a regulatory instrument to address this topic? Which role might UNCITRAL play in this context? The present volume provides structured insights, exploring classic cross-border insolvency topics such as universality and territoriality, recognition of foreign proceedings, rules for domestic proceedings etc.), but also addresses frontier issues like ADR and new technologies in cross-border insolvency. The book gathers the reflections of 32 top global experts in international insolvency law from 19 EU and non-EU countries and develops reflections for further legislative action.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"Nomos Verlagsgesellschaft mbH & Co. KG","isbn":[],"doi":"10.5771/9783748957072","subjects":["LN"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181604","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/0eee9505-48ed-4999-9b48-5d80b21a1a00/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"read","url":"https://doi.org/10.5771/9783748957072"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/ · CC-BY-SA","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181604","handle":"20.500.12854/181604","dspace_uuid":"6aa69694-0db4-4fa2-b08a-8bf1228a042c"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181604","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181604","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"read","url":"https://doi.org/10.5771/9783748957072"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/ · CC-BY-SA","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:ff8220fdb59442543e8079b1","title":"Europe’s Favourite Dictatorships","subtitle":"Southern Authoritarianism, Tourism, and the “Free West”, 1945–1975","description":"In the decades following the Second World War, the existence of authoritarian regimes on the Iberian Peninsula undermined the idea of a \"free West.\" At the same time, Spain and Portugal were emerging as ever more popular holiday destinations for West European tourists. This book analyzes how tourism shaped the relations between West European democracies and the Iberian regimes: Government officials and entrepreneurs established touristic infrastructures, travel writers addressed the tension between visitors’ leisure and locals’ oppression, activists called for a boycott of tourism to the authoritarian regimes. In a period shaped by the Cold War, tourism turned the Iberian regimes into Europe’s favourite dictatorships.","authors":["Hertel, Patricia"],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Tourism","Portugal","Spain","Dictatorship","Diktatur","Spanien","Tourismus","thema 