","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://publikationen.bibliothek.kit.edu/39594/2047"}],"access":"open_access","license":"Open Access; license not reported by OpenAlex","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:6bdfd5063bc8ca8c22a9c19f","title":"Expressways 3 Test Package","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Steven J. Molinsky"],"language":"es","year":1986,"publisher":"Prentice Hall Regents","isbn":["9780131899223","0133856844","0133853861","9780132986885","9780132984492","0132977222","013297763X","0132984237","0132977303","9780133856842","0131899228","0137905858","0132983737","9780132977630","0132984725","9780133863680","9780132977227","9780137905850","0132984490","0133863689","9780132984720","9780132983730","0132984318","9780132984232","9780132984317","9780132977302","9780133853865","0132986884","9780137942312","9780133853780","0133853780","0137942311"],"doi":"","subjects":[],"source":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL14854188W","cover_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/10867013-M.jpg","formats":[],"access":"digital_lending","license":"","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"OL14854188W","openlibrary_work":"OL14854188W","openlibrary_edition":"OL7340503M","internet_archive":"expresswayslevel0000stev"},"providers":[{"source":"Open Library","source_id":"OL14854188W","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL14854188W","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"digital_lending","license":"","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:62e808eae32adc5cd7012fc2","title":"Family Medicine in the Undergraduate Curriculum","subtitle":"Preparing medical students to work in evolving health care systems","description":"It has been recognised by governments and healthcare organisations worldwide that for Universal Healthcare in pursuit of Health for All under the Sustainable Development Goals to be achieved, effective primary care that is integrated, accessible, and affordable for everyone is essential. This practical guide is the first designed specifically to support those planning and conducting family medicine/primary care education within medical schools around the world. It offers medical educators a collection of concise easy to follow chapters, guiding the reader through the curriculum requirements with key references for further detail. Plain English and practical, deliverable advice, adaptable to different contexts, ensures the content is accessible to those educating medical students in any country, while the structure within sections ensures that family medicine doctors and educators can dip into chapters relevant to their roles, for example curriculum design for academic educators or teaching methods for those educating in clinical practice. Key Features ■ The first “how-to” guide dedicated to effective integration of family medicine teaching into medical school curricula ■ Offers a strong evidence-based framework for integrating family medicine into medical schools ■ Wide in scope, for academics and educationalists at all levels and in all geographies, reflecting and embracing the experience and variation in family medicine across the globe to produce pragmatic and effective information on which medical schools can base change ■ Step-by-step introduction to the processes of literature review (establishing the existing knowledge base), choosing a topic, research questions, and methodology, conducting research, and disseminating results ■ Supported by the WONCA Working Party on Education The book is edited and authored by members of the World Organization of Family Doctors (WONCA) Working Party on Education, which is ideally placed to offer a strong platform for medical schools to integrate family medicine whatever the local context, enabling all future doctors, whatever their career aspiration, to understand the importance of family medicine to health systems and holistic medicine and encourage family medicine doctors to inspire students to consider a career in the field. The Open Access version of this book, available at http://www.taylorfrancis.com, has been made available under a Creative Commons [Attribution-NonCommercial (CC BY-NC) 4.0 International license.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2023,"publisher":"CRC Press","isbn":[],"doi":"10.1201/9781003325734","subjects":["Medical curriculum design","Competency-based education","Clinical reasoning skills","Interprofessional learning","Assessment tools in medicine","Faculty development strategies","Undergraduate medical education integration","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JN Education::JNU Teaching of a specific subject","thema EDItEUR::M Medicine and Nursing::MB Medicine: general issues::MBP Health systems and services::MBPA Primary care medicine, primary health care","thema EDItEUR::M Medicine and Nursing::MR Medical study and revision guides and reference material","thema EDItEUR::M Medicine and Nursing::MB Medicine: general issues::MBN Public health and preventive medicine","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JN Education::JNT Teaching skills and techniques","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JN Education::JNM Higher education, tertiary education","thema EDItEUR::M Medicine and Nursing::MB Medicine: general issues::MBP Health systems and services","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JN Education::JND Educational systems and structures::JNDG Curriculum planning and development"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/117088","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/6632da3f-af9e-4327-ac9d-b001f7abc774/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/f4f55015-e311-4dc8-b215-315d91d7bd52/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/117088","handle":"20.500.12657/117088","dspace_uuid":"a0070452-1bda-46ff-b9b7-368f62654f7f"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/117088","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/117088","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/f4f55015-e311-4dc8-b215-315d91d7bd52/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:b55629b8699fa13d91a87391","title":"Famous Affinities of History: The Romance of Devotion. Vol 1-4, Complete","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Orr, Lyndon"],"language":"en","year":null,"publisher":"Project Gutenberg","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Biography","Love","Women -- Biography","Biographies","Category: History - Other","Category: Romance"],"source":"Project Gutenberg","source_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4693","cover_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/4693/pg4693.cover.medium.jpg","formats":[{"type":"html","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4693.html.images"},{"type":"epub","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4693.epub3.images"},{"type":"mobi","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4693.kf8.images"},{"type":"text","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4693.txt.utf-8"},{"type":"text","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/files/4693/4693.txt"}],"access":"public_domain","license":"Public domain in the United States","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"4693","gutenberg_id":"4693"},"providers":[{"source":"Project Gutenberg","source_id":"4693","source_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4693","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"html","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4693.html.images"},{"type":"epub","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4693.epub3.images"},{"type":"mobi","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4693.kf8.images"},{"type":"text","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4693.txt.utf-8"},{"type":"text","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/files/4693/4693.txt"}],"access":"public_domain","license":"Public domain in the United States","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:200a8701c19e78731efa4832","title":"Fashioning Immortality","subtitle":"Comparative Studies in Three Pindaric Odes","description":"The book is an interdisciplinary study on P ythian Three, Nemean Three and Nemean Five , three Pindaric epinicians, which share a special use of the word τέκτων, ‘fashioner’. In these victory odes, the term τέκτων refers to creators of immaterial objects and occurs close to the first and/or the final words of the poems, in connection with key themes, namely: health, poetry, choral performance, movement as opposed to stasis. The study shows that structures in which Pindaric metaphors are found have parallels in Indo-European languages of ancient attestation: Old Indic and Avestan. In doing so, the book casts new light on Pindar’s language and the stylistic features of his odes, which are in a relation of historical continuity with phraseological and structural characteristics of religious hymns of Ancient India and Iran. The study reveals that * tetƙ- metaphors and “* tetƙ- compositions”, i.e. metaphors and ring-compositions built by means of repetitions of “* tetƙ- words” (Vedic takṣ , Avestan taš , and Greek τέκτων), have a deep meta-thematic relevance in three linguistically related traditions and are an inherited phraseological stylistic feature common to Ancient Greek and Indo-Iranian poetic creations.","authors":["Massetti, Laura"],"language":"en","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Pindar","Stylistics","Ring-composition","Comparative Linguistics","Stilistik","Ringkomposition","Komparative Linguistik","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DB Ancient, classical and medieval texts::DBS Ancient Sagas and epics::DBSG Ancient Greek and Roman literature","thema EDItEUR::C Language and Linguistics::CF Linguistics::CFG Semantics, discourse analysis, stylistics","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism::DSB Literary studies: general::DSBB Literary studies: ancient, classical and medieval"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181483","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/758f6dd5-b4e8-45a8-a91b-489017827a0b/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116739/1/9783112208243.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181483","handle":"20.500.12854/181483","dspace_uuid":"7f7f6ccf-93ed-4c9d-afea-cf4bc4ae7d12"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181483","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181483","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116739/1/9783112208243.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:556a6112e44902751a2bf28f","title":"Fast algorithm for detecting community structure in networks","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["M. E. J. Newman"],"language":"en","year":2004,"publisher":"arXiv (Cornell University)","isbn":[],"doi":"10.1103/physreve.69.066133","subjects":["Complex Network Analysis Techniques","Bioinformatics and Genomic Networks","Opinion Dynamics and Social Influence"],"source":"OpenAlex","source_url":"http://arxiv.org/abs/cond-mat/0309508","cover_url":"","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/cond-mat/0309508"}],"access":"open_access","license":"Open Access; license not reported by OpenAlex","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"article","identifiers":{"source_id":"W2089458547","openalex_id":"W2089458547"},"providers":[{"source":"OpenAlex","source_id":"W2089458547","source_url":"http://arxiv.org/abs/cond-mat/0309508","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/cond-mat/0309508"}],"access":"open_access","license":"Open Access; license not reported by OpenAlex","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:d4cdfa1a05141bcbfe81a9e5","title":"Femicidio y violencia doméstica: Perspectivas psicológicas para la comprensión y prevención","subtitle":"","description":"This book offers an in-depth and multidimensional analysis of one of the most serious and persistent social problems: violence against women and its most extreme manifestation, femicide. The work proposes addressing these phenomena not only from a legal perspective, but by integrating psychology, sociology, and criminology to understand the emotional, cognitive, and cultural roots of perpetrators, as well as the profound consequences for victims. From emotion regulation and the influence of stress on the immune system to the exploration of repressed traumatic memories and emotional resilience, the book enables the identification of risk factors, mechanisms that perpetuate abuse, and effective intervention strategies. Through an interdisciplinary approach, the author examines domestic violence in Ecuador, demonstrating how patriarchal cultural norms, power dynamics, and intergenerational transmission sustain patterns of abuse, while highlighting the resilience of victims in hostile environments. The book also delves into misogyny as a psychological, social, and cultural phenomenon, whose irrational hatred of women constitutes a central factor in explaining femicide and calls for rigorous forensic psychological assessments to prevent and adequately punish these crimes. Integrating theory, empirical research, and case studies, this work provides conceptual and methodological tools for psychologists, legal professionals, educators, and public policymakers. More than an academic analysis, it is an urgent call to action, toward prevention, victim protection, and the construction of societies in which the dignity, equality, and lives of women are respected and valued.","authors":["Mosquera-Zambrano, Silvia (Kaunas)"],"language":"es","year":2026,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/lbjn4083","subjects":["Violencia contra las mujeres","Femicidio","Psicología forense","Violencia de género","Resiliencia emocional","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178502.2","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/9a4bd2e3-9779-4f86-b6df-f8744d4de5b2/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/178502.2","handle":"20.500.12854/178502.2","dspace_uuid":"b0b7d8fa-55ca-4932-a3bc-f9a877582879"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/178502.2","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178502.2","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:b20f4fcf9b66c9703740ff4f","title":"Fermat's Last Theorem","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Simon Singh"],"language":"es","year":1997,"publisher":"Grupo Editorial Norma","isbn":["3423195185","9780001054639","9654484129","9788408023753","8408046799","9780008553821","2012789218","0140268693","0007790228","9758434365","0007381999","0802713319","0008553823","9783446193130","9580448655","9780007241811","9789172636880","9780385493628","3446193138","1857025210","9781857025217","9874682736","9780802713315","9788408046790","8817112917","2709618540","9783423330527","9783423195188","9789758434367","9780613181051","9788817112918","9784105393014","9780965593199","9781857026696","9780007790227","0001054635","4105393014","000724181X","185702669