s":["Ivan Bulloch"],"language":"es","year":1992,"publisher":"World Book","isbn":["0716649004","9781587289699","9780716649014","1568472315","9781854341921","0716649012","9780716649007","9781568472317","1587289695","1854341928"],"doi":"","subjects":[],"source":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1884844W","cover_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/3860574-M.jpg","formats":[],"access":"digital_lending","license":"","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"OL1884844W","openlibrary_work":"OL1884844W","openlibrary_edition":"OL1082836M","internet_archive":"games00bull"},"providers":[{"source":"Open Library","source_id":"OL1884844W","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1884844W","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"digital_lending","license":"","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:51b97cdaee960bbe9e3f1a69","title":"Gamificación universitaria: Una experiencia sobre su impacto en el rendimiento académico","subtitle":"","description":"This work examines the potential of gamification as an innovative pedagogical strategy to strengthen academic performance in the field of higher education. This study focuses on an applied experience with students from the Faculty of Early Childhood Education at the Enrique Guzmán y Valle National University of Education (Peru), specifically in the subject of Applied Didactics for the 1st cycle, during the year 2024. Gamification, understood as the incorporation of game elements in non-game educational contexts, is presented here as a methodology capable of energizing the learning experience, enhancing student motivation, and generating a more participatory environment. Throughout the text, its theoretical foundations, its links with active learning, and the challenges associated with its implementation in real university environments are analyzed. In addition, various technological tools and applications are examined that allow for the design of gamified content tailored to student needs and the specifics of the teaching context. The documented experience demonstrates that, beyond the playful component, gamification offers new forms of educational interaction that foster both academic engagement and pedagogical reflection. This work constitutes a relevant reference for teachers, researchers, and educational administrators interested in innovating teaching-learning processes in initial vocational training. Its approach combines theoretical analysis with practical evidence, providing useful input for understanding, applying, and evaluating the impact of gamification in higher education.","authors":["Casimiro-Urcos, Consuelo Nora","Casimiro-Urcos, Walther Hernán","Tobalino-López, Donatila","Pareja-Pérez, Lourdes Basilia","Vegas-Palomino, Elizabeth Mercedes","Montañez-Huancaya, Aquila Priscila"],"language":"es","year":2025,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/uawf6106","subjects":["Gamificación","Rendimiento académico","Motivación estudiantil","Aprendizaje activo","Educación superior","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JN Education"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178523.2","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/d4def2ee-7cdc-47f8-abc4-8e951fb4ff2c/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/178523.2","handle":"20.500.12854/178523.2","dspace_uuid":"d0172e4e-2fbb-499f-bba0-8d752dd36502"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/178523.2","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178523.2","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:13e7cde79252b19210b4f7a1","title":"Gamification for Engaging Computer Science Students in Learning Activities: A Case Study","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Maria-Blanca Ibanez","Ángela Di Serio","Carlos Delgado Kloos"],"language":"en","year":2014,"publisher":"IEEE Transactions on Learning Technologies","isbn":[],"doi":"10.1109/tlt.2014.2329293","subjects":["Educational Games and Gamification","Online Learning and Analytics","Teaching and Learning Programming"],"source":"OpenAlex","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/tlt.2014.2329293","cover_url":"","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/ielx7/4620076/6901341/06827214.pdf"}],"access":"open_access","license":"Open Access; license not reported by OpenAlex","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"article","identifiers":{"source_id":"W2083289268","openalex_id":"W2083289268"},"providers":[{"source":"OpenAlex","source_id":"W2083289268","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/tlt.2014.2329293","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/ielx7/4620076/6901341/06827214.pdf"}],"access":"open_access","license":"Open Access; license not reported by OpenAlex","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:af1fc59d3029ef39e103f7d2","title":"Ganadería sostenible en Tenango de Doria: Guía Técnica para el Control Sanitario en bovinos","subtitle":"","description":"This book constitutes a fundamental contribution to improving health and sustainability in cattle production in grazing systems, specifically in the Tenango de Doria region of Hidalgo. Developed within the framework of the project “Strategies for Combating Cattle Diseases in Tenango de Doria, Hidalgo” at the Autonomous University of Chapingo, this work offers a rigorous analysis and a comprehensive technical proposal to address the main health challenges affecting animal productivity and well-being. Throughout the work, knowledge on strategic mineral supplementation, sustainable management of forage resources and soils, and agroecological and zootechnical practices aimed at effective disease prevention are integrated. The guide emphasizes the implementation of health protocols adapted to local environmental and epidemiological conditions, including vaccination programs, deworming, and comprehensive ectoparasite control, all of which are crucial factors for ensuring herd health. It also addresses strategic water resource management and comprehensive pasture management, key elements for optimizing productivity in a context of adverse climatic and geographic conditions. The proposed innovative regenerative livestock approach promotes ecosystem restoration, generating a dynamic balance between production and environmental conservation. Aimed at producers, technicians, and specialists, this text is positioned as an indispensable resource for informed decision-making and the implementation of sustainable practices that ensure the profitability and resilience of cattle farming in Tenango de Doria.","authors":["Mojica-Zárate, Héctor Tecumshé","Lezama-Juárez, Dulce María","Partida-Sedas, José Gervasio","López-García, Francisco Javier","Antonio-Hurtado, Sebastián"],"language":"es","year":2025,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/cdii3740","subjects":["Ganadería bovina","Sanidad animal","Sostenibilidad","Manejo de pastoreo","Ganadería regenerativa","thema EDItEUR::T Technology, Engineering, Agriculture, Industrial processes::TV Agriculture and farming"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178524.2","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/fc8f13d5-4e21-4d44-bf6b-ca235050146a/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/178524.2","handle":"20.500.12854/178524.2","dspace_uuid":"d1d0c91a-ab70-4479-8cf3-56495b18ab28"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/178524.2","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178524.2","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:24e80cbf13c7b0d7ddc0e145","title":"Gender and Power in a Nazi Concentration Camp","subtitle":"The Ravensbrück Female Medical Personnel","description":"Drawing on a rich corpus of contemporary and post-war sources – including personal letters and legal documentation – this open access book illuminates the roles of eleven female doctors and nurses at a camp for female prisoners in Nazi Germany. While it may seem unthinkable that medical staff worked in a place of death and suffering, Kate Docking looks at how female medical personnel were hired to work at Ravensbrück concentration camp from September 1939 until its liberation by the Allies in April 1945, highlighting why many women sought jobs there. Examining the experiences of these women from a gendered perspective, Gender and Power in a Nazi Concentration Camp sheds new light on the role of female medical personnel during the Nazi era. Though the Ravensbrück female medical personnel committed atrocities, the majority were not brought to justice. Docking underscores how stereotypes of femininity as ‘naturally innocent’ helped to allow women involved in Nazi crimes to continue their lives peacefully after the war. This ground-breaking book demonstrates the need for gender to be considered in explanations of how Nazi persecution was able to happen. The ebook editions of this book are available open access under a CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 licence on bloomsburycollections.com. Open access was funded by the Centre for the Study of Health, Ethics, and Society, University of Hamburg, Germany.","authors":["Docking, Kate"],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"Bloomsbury Publishing (UK)","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Gender history","Women's history","Holocaust","German history","European history","Second World War","World War Two","History of medicine","Justice","Femininity","Innocence","Doctors","Nurses","Survivor memoirs","Third Reich","Nazism","Atrocities","Human experiments","Nazi crimes","Stereotypes","Victimisation narrative","Postwar Germany","Gender studies","Fear","Terror","Power dynamics","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History::NHD European history","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History::NHT History: specific events and topics::NHTZ Genocide and ethnic cleansing::NHTZ1 The Holocaust","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JB Society and culture: general::JBS Social groups, communities and identities::JBSF Gender studies, gender groups::JBSF1 Gender studies: women and girls","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History::NHW Military history::NHWR Specific wars and campaigns::NHWR7 Second World War","thema EDItEUR::1 Place qualifiers::1D Europe","thema EDItEUR::3 Time period qualifiers::3M c 1500 onwards to present day::3MP 20th century, c 1900 to c 1999::3MPB Early 20th century c 1900 to c 1950::3MPBL c 1940 to c 1949","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JB Society and culture: general::JBS Social groups, communities and identities::JBSF Gender studies, gender groups"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/117054","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/42c79c0c-e66c-422e-9be7-4b5c5ad1572a/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/117054","handle":"20.500.12657/117054","dspace_uuid":"00f7d3cd-8e21-4140-9b15-730cae6e2d32"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/117054","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/117054","language":"en","formats":[],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:f36924a324b5b2508ceecef6","title":"Generación automática de reportes con R y LaTeX","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Mario Alfonso Morales Rivera"],"language":"es","year":null,"publisher":"","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Programación","R"],"source":"Free Programming Books","source_url":"http://cran.r-project.org/doc/contrib/Rivera-Tutorial_Sweave.pdf","cover_url":"","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"http://cran.r-project.org/doc/contrib/Rivera-Tutorial_Sweave.pdf"}],"access":"author_free","license":"","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"276a77134d3aa977d4e6","list_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EbookFoundation/free-programming-books/main/books/free-programming-books-es.md"},"providers":[{"source":"Free Programming Books","source_id":"276a77134d3aa977d4e6","source_url":"http://cran.r-project.org/doc/contrib/Rivera-Tutorial_Sweave.pdf","language":"es","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"http://cran.r-project.org/doc/contrib/Rivera-Tutorial_Sweave.pdf"}],"access":"author_free","license":"","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:54cca39034890273e8225b43","title":"Geometría en movimiento: exploraciones didácticas con GeoGebra. Tomo 1","subtitle":"","description":"This book presents a proposal for strengthening the teaching of school geometry through the integration of theoretical foundations, didactic guidelines, and learning activities designed with GeoGebra. It is based on the premise that learning geometry should not be limited to identifying shapes or mechanically applying procedures but should instead foster the development of geometric thinking, visualization, representation, mathematical reasoning, and the construction of meaningful understanding. From this perspective, the book examines the main challenges students encounter, including dependence on prototypes, confusion between geometric drawings and geometric objects, and difficulties in coordinating multiple systems of representation. Drawing on the contributions of Van Hiele, Duval, Laborde, Fischbein, and other leading scholars in mathematics education, the authors provide criteria for designing learning experiences aligned with levels of geometric reasoning and the mediating role of representations. The book also analyzes the potential and limitations of GeoGebra, emphasizing that its educational value depends on intentional teaching practices that promote exploration, conjecture formulation, validation of mathematical relationships, and mathematical argumentation. The second part translates these theoretical foundations into classroom proposals organized around lines, angles, triangles, congruence, similarity, Thales’ theorem, quadrilaterals, polygons, the circumference, and the circle. Each chapter includes didactic sequences, reflective questions, and lesson-planning guidelines, making the book a valuable resource for teachers, teacher educators, and researchers interested in promoting a more dynamic, meaningful, and evidence-based approach to geometry instruction.","authors":["Abad-Peña, Graciela","Fernández-Rodríguez, Katia Lisset","Castro-Muñoz, Joel Alberto","Briones-Franco, Johanna Graciela","Ayoví-Vanegas, Marlene"],"language":"es","year":2026,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/sczc1503","subjects":["Geometry Education","GeoGebra","Geometric Reasoning","Mathematics Didactics","Mathematical Visualization","thema EDItEUR::P Mathematics and Science"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/180364.2","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/bec20ce4-e6c3-4596-a02b-95727bd1ba3c/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/180364.2","handle":"20.500.12854/180364.2","dspace_uuid":"e1479423-0dd7-4280-8e27-197168380bde"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/180364.2","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/180364.2","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:103b6dbec5d92a6b46cb6139","title":"George's Secret Key to the Universe","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Stephen Hawking","Lucy Hawking","Hugh Dancy"],"language":"es","year":1998,"publisher":"Turtleback Books","isbn":["3570132846","6050924937","9781407047867","8804591897","9783570132845","0606373756","9788382020908","9722339052","2266219189","5437003447","9781644736739","9781410406385","1442430109","8936024911638","9780743571616","9788484414216","0552559814","9782266219181","9784265820115","9788381165006","9781407047850","164473673X","9789722339056","8310114036","0385612702","0385614039","1407047841","9785437003442","9788484414223","0743571614","9788499083728","140704785X","9788310114037","8484414221","9781407047843","1416985840","8382020909","9780385612708","9780552559584","9783570219539","055255958X","8484414213","9786050924930","1407047868","9780385611817","2266179357","8499083722","9782266179355","4265820115","8381165008","9788804591894","2266176455","9781442430105","9782266176453","9781416985846","9780606373753","9780385614030","9781416954620","0385611811","3570219534","1416954627","1410406385","9788925518701","8925518708","9780552559812"],"doi":"","subjects":[],"source":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL5714585W","cover_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6681655-M.jpg","formats":[],"access":"digital_lending","license":"","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"OL5714585W","openlibrary_work":"OL5714585W","openlibrary_edition":"OL38186871M","internet_archive":"laclavesecretade0000lucy"},"providers":[{"source":"Open Library","source_id":"OL5714585W","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL5714585W","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"digital_lending","license":"","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:ed6da13d860b159855e4e22a","title":"Germany’s History Wars","subtitle":"Contesting Memory and Identity Today","description":"Like no other country’s Germany’s identity is shaped by its history or rather by the critical engagement with this history. The book traces the most important public debates on history since the new millennium thereby adding a mosaic of topics and perspectives to the memorial landscape of the Berlin Republic. The book is divided into five parts, \"German Empire and the question of continuity\", \"National Socialism and World War II\", \"The Holocaust and Multidirectional Memory\", \"GDR/BRD/Unification\" to \"The Berlin Republic. Marginalization and new Master Narratives\", and addresses them from different biographical backgrounds, thereby creating a mosaic of topics and perspectives.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Memory politics","Culture wars","History wars","German history_x000D_","Erinnerung","Globalgeschichte","Kolonialismus","Vergangenheitsbewältigung","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History::NHD European history","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History::NHB General and world history"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181427","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/204fcaf1-a5e6-4073-b9f3-05023b8fd341/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116724/1/9783111588551.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181427","handle":"20.500.12854/181427","dspace_uuid":"b085c067-77e2-4925-869c-2ea77b56237e"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181427","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181427","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116724/1/9783111588551.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:3b2e8802b104a3d68372af86","title":"Geschichte auf Instagram und TikTok","subtitle":"Perspektiven auf Quellen und Praktiken","description":"","authors":[],"language":"de","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Public history","Digital history","Social media","Science communication","Wissenschaftskommunikation","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History::NHB General and world history"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116937","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/ff81d5f2-4074-42df-9d28-f6421284b7a5/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/abe1b694-76c0-40c2-96f5-12872de762c7/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116937","handle":"20.500.12657/116937","dspace_uuid":"3fe5ffae-d504-4795-96d4-ec0cf0c9f857"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116937","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116937","language":"de","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/abe1b694-76c0-40c2-96f5-12872de762c7/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:8b1876270e40687045f026d2","title":"Geschichtslyrik, 1850–1918","subtitle":"Quantitative und qualitative Untersuchungen zur Geschichte einer Gattung","description":"Die Arbeit widmet sich der Geschichte der deutschsprachigen Geschichtslyrik von 1850 bis 1918. Obwohl Geschichtslyrik im 19. und frühen 20. Jahrhundert eine wichtige Rolle spielte, wurde die Gattung bislang noch nicht umfassend untersucht. Ein wichtiges Ergebnis der Arbeit besteht darin, dass die in früheren Forschungsbeiträgen angedeutete These eines ‚Niedergangs‘ der Geschichtslyrik in der literarischen Moderne stark relativiert werden muss. Um die Gattungsgeschichte zu erhellen, wird ein über 1800 Texte umfassendes, auf Geschichtslyrikanthologien basierendes Korpus untersucht. Dabei kommen neben qualitativen Einzeltextanalysen und -interpretationen auch digitale, quantitative Verfahren zum Einsatz, womit hier vor allem die manuelle Annotation sämtlicher Korpustexte und die statistische Auswertung der Annotationsdaten gemeint ist. Jenseits der eigentlichen Texte setzt sich die Arbeit auch mit der Rezeption und Vermittlung von Geschichtslyrik im Untersuchungszeitraum auseinander. Beansprucht wird, nicht nur einen Beitrag zur Geschichte der Geschichtslyrik zu leisten, sondern auch am Beispiel dieser Gattung zu demonstrieren und zu reflektieren, wie sich Gattungsgeschichtsschreibung im Allgemeinen sinnvoll betreiben lässt.","authors":["Kröncke, Merten"],"language":"de","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Historical poetry","Literary genre","Corpus linguistics","Geschichtslyrik","Literaturgattung","Korpuslinguistik","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism::DSB Literary studies: general","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism::DSB Literary studies: general::DSBF Literary studies: c 1800 to c 1900","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism::DSC Literary studies: poetry and poets","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116817","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/f8fc1ab4-f149-4b79-960a-6b339bd0583f/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/a2661adf-3ae5-402f-9cbd-764915ce509e/retrieve"},{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116817/1/9783112221594.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116817","handle":"20.500.12854/181580","dspace_uuid":"5ed97683-ad44-4126-aded-3dc7171e145c","oapen_library_source_id":"20.500.12657/116817","oapen_library_handle":"20.500.12657/116817","oapen_library_dspace_uuid":"c0b4bba9-c5a1-46a5-ba41-49338d8d7bfa","doab_source_id":"20.500.12854/181580"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116817","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116817","language":"de","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/a2661adf-3ae5-402f-9cbd-764915ce509e/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY · Other open license","verified_legal":true},{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181580","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181580","language":"de","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116817/1/9783112221594.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:92877ca1db411d019c2e3b39","title":"Gestão da aprendizagem organizacional no Ensino Superior: Um modelo estratégico para universidades em contextos emergentes","subtitle":"","description":"In a world marked by rapid technological transformations, environmental crises, the globalization of knowledge, and profound social inequalities, universities face the challenge of reinventing themselves in order to remain relevant, innovative, and socially committed. The book offers a deep and contemporary reflection on the role of organizational learning as a fundamental strategy for the transformation and strengthening of contemporary higher education institutions. Drawing on the theoretical contributions of both classical and contemporary authors in the field of organizational learning, the book presents an integrated strategic model based on four fundamental pillars: knowledge management, competency development, strategic monitoring, and a learning-oriented organizational culture. These elements are analyzed in an articulated manner, demonstrating how they can contribute to institutional innovation, the improvement of academic quality, the strengthening of scientific research, and university sustainability. The book pays special attention to universities operating in emerging contexts, recognizing the challenges associated with structural limitations, digital transformation, environmental sustainability, and the need for stronger connections between universities and society. Throughout its chapters, the work discusses concrete strategies for applying organizational learning to the essential functions of the university: teaching, research, university extension, and institutional management. With an interdisciplinary approach focused on the contemporary reality of higher education, this work serves as a valuable reference for researchers, university managers, academics, and students interested in institutional innovation, academic leadership, and sustainable development. More than a book about university management, this work presents a strategic vision of universities as learning organizations capable of transforming knowledge into innovation, human development, and sustainable social impact.","authors":["Sarmento dos Santos-da Silva, Ana Paula"],"language":"pt","year":2026,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/zfxs7567","subjects":["Aprendizagem organizacional","Gestão do conhecimento","Inovação institucional","Sustentabilidade universitária","Vinculação universidade-sociedade","thema EDItEUR::K Economics, Finance, Business and Management::KJ Business and Management::KJM Management and management techniques::KJMK Knowledge management"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178514.2","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/c58e49bb-87a2-4e2d-b5fb-05658b89cb62/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/178514.2","handle":"20.500.12854/178514.2","dspace_uuid":"8dec522b-1618-491a-8e74-277d6333961f"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/178514.2","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178514.2","language":"pt","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:06072fd7a1e9aeee54bd0f00","title":"Gestión administrativa y atención de calidad: Claves para la mejora de servicios en centros de terapia física","subtitle":"","description":"This book offers a comprehensive analysis of the interrelationship between administration and quality of care in healthcare services, with a particular focus on physical therapy centers. The text addresses the theoretical foundations of administration applied to the healthcare environment, highlighting its strategic role in service efficiency. It delves into essential administrative functions—such as planning, organization, direction, and control—as well as the impact that professionals and organizations have on the continuous improvement of patient care. It also examines quality standards in healthcare services, with an emphasis on the specific context of physical therapy centers. The book presents an evaluation focused on the district of Surquillo, Lima, Peru, conducted during the year 2023. The main physical therapy care centers in the area are profiled, specifically the Casa Hogar Santa Luisa de Marillac, Fisiocentro, and the Villa Victoria Porvenir Health Center. The book analyzes the quality of the services provided and their direct impact on patient satisfaction, using relevant indicators from the healthcare field. Finally, it presents the relationship between administrative management and quality of care, highlighting how proper organization of resources, processes, and personnel positively impacts user perception and experience. This work seeks to be a useful tool for both academics and healthcare professionals interested in improving the management and quality of therapeutic services.","authors":["Casimiro-Guerra, Giorgia","Casimiro-Urcos, Walther Hernán","Casimiro-Urcos, Javier Francisco","Orosco-Naveros, Aida Beatriz"],"language":"es","year":2025,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/kyml7642","subjects":["Administración sanitaria","Calidad de atención","Terapia física","Gestión de recursos","Satisfacción del paciente","thema EDItEUR::M Medicine and Nursing::MK Medical specialties, branches of medicine::MKZ Therapy and therapeutics"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178522.2","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/c74329b8-b7e7-4ea2-ade1-d46a7121c641/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/178522.2","handle":"20.500.12854/178522.2","dspace_uuid":"d8eefc42-b9ae-41b8-b089-b0a282aaecb7"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/178522.2","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178522.2","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:0115165fb8455e2c3eb3615d","title":"Gestión, auditoría y estrategias empresariales para el desarrollo sostenible","subtitle":"","description":"This book brings together applied studies conducted at the Universidad Católica de Cuenca (Ecuador) with the objective of strengthening organizational management, process auditing, and strategic decision-making across various productive sectors. The work integrates contemporary theoretical and methodological approaches with real case studies that highlight problems, opportunities, and solutions in areas such as finance, internal control, inventory, purchasing, sales, digital marketing, auditing, and territorial development. The text begins with a financial evaluation and expense control in a vehicle inspection company, followed by the proposal of a questionnaire for audit in procurement processes and the implementation of the Balanced Scorecard in commercial management. Inventory processes in gastronomic businesses, expense control in small enterprises, and operational risks in service companies are analyzed, demonstrating how management auditing optimizes efficiency and transparency. The book also incorporates a communicational and strategic dimension through studies on branding, rebranding, and digital marketing in SMEs, hair salons, and dental clinics, highlighting their influence on positioning, competitiveness, and sustainable economic growth. Finally, food sovereignty and subjective poverty in rural communities are addressed, expanding the scope of auditing toward social and territorial dimensions and showing how applied analysis can contribute to sustainable and equitable public policies. This work constitutes a comprehensive reference for professionals, academics, and students interested in the intersection of management, auditing, and business strategies, combining methodological rigor, practical applicability, and a commitment to the economic and social development of Ecuador.","authors":["Ordoñez-Parra, Janice Licenia","Vásquez-Erazo, Edwin Joselito"],"language":"es","year":2026,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/nlhc3877","subjects":["Auditoría de gestión","Gestión organizacional","Control interno","Toma de decisiones","Desarrollo empresarial","thema EDItEUR::K Economics, Finance, Business and Management"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178499.2","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/648b279b-075e-4bdf-9045-f002d3b6b093/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/178499.2","handle":"20.500.12854/178499.2","dspace_uuid":"96e7cf80-f5dd-49f2-9a86-2cbcec9f08f6"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/178499.2","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178499.2","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:3781bbafdbf61195a5349040","title":"Gestión educativa en la Educación Superior","subtitle":"","description":"This work addresses with depth and rigor the contemporary challenges facing universities in a context marked by the globalization of knowledge, digital transformation, and the growing demand for quality, equity, and innovation. Far from conceiving management as a simple technical-administrative process, this book proposes a strategic, human, and contextualized vision in which the university is understood as a complex, dynamic, and learning-oriented system. Educational management is presented here as a fundamental tool for promoting continuous improvement, strengthening institutional quality, and responding appropriately to the needs of a constantly changing society. The text analyzes the academic, social, technological, and ethical dimensions that shape effective management, with an emphasis on pedagogical leadership, collaborative organizational culture, student well-being, values formation, and the professional development of human talent. The work also highlights the importance of building more inclusive, sustainable, and student-centered universities, capable of integrating reliable assessment processes, making informed decisions, and generating institutional policies that promote access, retention, and academic success. Through a comprehensive approach, it invites us to rethink the university as a space for transformation, innovation, and social commitment. This book constitutes a valuable tool for managers, teachers, researchers, and decision-makers committed to quality, people-centered, and future-oriented higher education.","authors":["Soria-León, Norma Graciela"],"language":"es","year":2025,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/ibga9354","subjects":["Gestión educativa","Calidad institucional","Liderazgo pedagógico","Transformación digital","Inclusión y equidad","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JN Education::JNK Educational administration and organization"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178529.2","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/223b5c2a-4e60-4213-ac0c-245b58884807/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/178529.2","handle":"20.500.12854/178529.2","dspace_uuid":"8ab7d7c7-9ab8-4e2d-a4b0-2a256b5254f8"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/178529.2","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178529.2","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:399969fa26f29bd3ceaa1aaa","title":"Ghost Stories of an Antiquary","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["James, M. R. (Montague Rhodes)"],"language":"en","year":null,"publisher":"Project Gutenberg","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Ghost stories, English","Horror tales, English","Short stories, English","Category: British Literature","Category: Crime, Thrillers and Myste