tion":"How do you design and build a good school? The question of how pedagogy can be translated into contemporary, high-quality school architecture is central to the guide, as is that of how joint planning can succeed. New typologies and developments in school design are described in detail, with attention paid to the implementation of a pre-planning phase in school design. The volume provides exciting insights into the fundamentals and processes of school design in Germany for all relevant professions and interested stakeholders. First published in 2012 and reissued in 2017, this standard work on designing new school buildings is now available in an updated handbook format.","authors":[],"language":"de","year":2025,"publisher":"jovis Verlag","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Architecture","Pedagogy","Teaching","Schools","School buildings","Interdisciplinary","Participatory planning","Educational spaces_x000D_","Schulbau","Phase Null","Partizipation","Lernräume","Pädagogische Architektur","Interdisziplinär","thema EDItEUR::A The Arts::AM Architecture::AMB Individual architects and architectural firms"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116940","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/22025862-7edf-44a4-997e-478682752e9e/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/b1d930e5-96fb-4144-800e-8c0b3f3fa20d/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116940","handle":"20.500.12657/116940","dspace_uuid":"4d0f2103-f962-4f56-a708-34ecdf424624"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116940","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116940","language":"de","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/b1d930e5-96fb-4144-800e-8c0b3f3fa20d/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:d86819112c23e1069248b1aa","title":"Handbuch Soziale Arbeit und Digitalisierung","subtitle":"","description":"Mit welchen Fragen, Herausforderungen und Umbrüchen ist die Soziale Arbeit im Kontext von Digitalität und Digitalisierungsprozessen konfrontiert? Das Handbuch behandelt das allgegenwärtige Thema Digitalität und Digitalisierung als Standardwerk umfassend mit Bezug auf Disziplin und Praxis der Sozialen Arbeit. Beleuchtet werden unterschiedliche disziplinäre Perspektiven, gesellschaftliche Entwicklungen und Diskurse, digitalisierte Formen der Dienstleistungserbringung, Digitalität und Digitalisierung im Kontext von Profession, Organisation und in verschiedenen Handlungsfeldern. In jedem der über 50 Beiträge wird der aktuelle Wissensstand zusammengefasst und seine Bedeutung für Soziale Arbeit herausgearbeitet. Mit Perspektive auf Organisation, Fachkräfte, Adressat*innenund Erbringungsformen wird der Stand des Wissens vorgestellt und Möglichkeiten, Risiken und offene Fragestellungen diskutiert. Die Analysen informieren sowohl Entscheidungsträger*innen als auch Fachkräfte und Studierende der Sozialen Arbeit und anderer sozialer Berufe.","authors":[],"language":"de","year":2026,"publisher":"Beltz Juventa","isbn":["9783779990291"],"doi":"","subjects":["Digitale Technik","Digitalisierung","Sozialpädagogik","Lebenswelt","Mediatisierung","Teilhabe","Open Access","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JK Social services and welfare, criminology::JKS Social welfare and social services"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181599","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/c92c7d6c-6a3a-4f1e-8d1d-d856c7cd40bc/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116567/1/9783779990291.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181599","handle":"20.500.12854/181599","dspace_uuid":"c7cc3d68-a802-4e52-980d-5660da959362"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181599","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181599","language":"de","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116567/1/9783779990291.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:929cd63e562514f4cbfca566","title":"Handbuch Wirtschaft und Religion","subtitle":"Deutschland im 19. und 20. Jahrhundert","description":"Das Handbuch bietet eine interdisziplinäre, systematische und historische Perspektive auf die vielfältigen Zusammenhänge zwischen Religion und Wirtschaft. Die zentrale Frage lautet: Wie entwickelt sich das Verhältnis von Religion und Wirtschaft im historischen Zeitverlauf und insbesondere in der deutschen Gesellschaft seit dem 19. Jahrhundert? Die deutschen Entwicklungen werden epochenübergreifend eingeordnet, um die langen Linien des Wechselverhältnisses von Religion und Wirtschaft nachzuzeichnen. Das Handbuch ist problemorientiert angelegt: Es stellt den Forschungsstand dar und benennt zugleich Desiderate und aussichtsreiche Felder zukünftiger Forschung. Es greift große Narrative wie die Säkularisierungstheorie kritisch auf und führt die Diskussion dabei über Klassiker wie Max Weber hinaus. 29 ausgewiesene Expertinnen und Experten erörtern aktuelle Themen wie die Migrationsgesellschaft und präsentieren neue Paradigmen wie Religionsökonomie und Verhaltensökonomik. Fünf thematisch gegliederte Abschnitte bieten einen zielgerichteten Überblick über Ideengeschichte, Theorien, Methoden, religiöse Traditionen und zentrale Themenbereiche. Aus verschiedenen Perspektiven zeigt sich: Auch in der modernen Gesellschaft bleiben Religion und Wirtschaft eng miteinander verwoben und beeinflussen sich gegenseitig.","authors":[],"language":"de","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Business ethics","Religious enterprise","Prosperity","Moral economy","Moralische Ökonomie","Religiöse Unternehmen","Wirtschaftsethik","Wohlstand","thema EDItEUR::K Economics, Finance, Business and Management::KC Economics::KCZ Economic history","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QR Religion and beliefs::QRA Religion: general::QRAX History of religion"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181399","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/a496431c-246e-481b-ae17-1a31238770cf/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116659/1/9783110982152.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181399","handle":"20.500.12854/181399","dspace_uuid":"6d59c99f-8011-42ec-9d2d-a9033d15865d"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181399","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181399","language":"de","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116659/1/9783110982152.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:a5c831390769b33ffc7991eb","title":"Harmonizing language data","subtitle":"Standards for linguistic resources","description":"Standards function as safeguards to ensure that data remains interpretable, uniformly queryable, and archivable over time – a critical challenge for digital humanists working with complex linguistic resources. This book provides an overview of essential standards for ensuring the sustainability of data in the Digital Humanities (DH). It addresses the selection of data encoding formats, methods of annotating primary data, and approaches to making resources findable and accessible. The focus is on various forms of linguistic data, such as texts, lexicons, or parallel arrangements (e.g., translations or transcribed recordings). The work explains the role of annotations and metadata in structuring and contextualizing data and examines the influence of diverse data formats, shaped by local academic or industrial practices. In contrast to neural language models, which often yield impressive but opaque results, DH projects aim for transparency, reproducibility, and sustainability. Achieving these goals requires interoperability – the seamless interaction between data and tools. The book demonstrates how clear guidelines and best practices help ensure the long-term usability of data. It offers digital humanists practical approaches and well-founded standards to sustainably archive and efficiently utilize their data, making it an indispensable resource for the field.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Data Sustainability","Interoperability","Metadata and Annotations","Data Standards","Datennachhaltigkeit","Interoperabilität","Metadaten und Annotationen","Datennormen","thema EDItEUR::C Language and Linguistics::CF Linguistics::CFX Computational and corpus linguistics","thema EDItEUR::U Computing and Information Technology::UX Applied computing::UXA Computer applications in the arts and humanities","thema EDItEUR::C Language and Linguistics::CF Linguistics","thema EDItEUR::U Computing and Information Technology::UY Computer science","thema EDItEUR::C Language and Linguistics::CJ Language teaching and learning"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116801","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/