ion","description":"This is an open access title available under the terms of a CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 License. It is free to read, download and share via Elgaronline, thanks to generous funding support from Riksbankens Jubileumsfond (grant no: P21-0235). This topical book explores whether virtual meetings can enable the creation of common ground when colleagues are not meeting in person daily. It shows how common ground is created and maintained through different practices and demonstrates that technology is an actor playing a role in the meeting alongside the participants.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"Edward Elgar Publishing","isbn":[],"doi":"10.4337/9781035395217","subjects":["Virtual Meetings; Communing; Common Ground; Collaboration; Coordination; Coorientation","KNTX","KJD","KJU","KJWX"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181610","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/05383467-b8c4-46b4-98e1-679d14aee80f/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"read","url":"https://www.elgaronline.com/monobook-oa/book/9781035395217/9781035395217.xml"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181610","handle":"20.500.12854/181610","dspace_uuid":"a87c89b1-648d-415e-bd80-f2e604e21dd1"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181610","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181610","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"read","url":"https://www.elgaronline.com/monobook-oa/book/9781035395217/9781035395217.xml"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:2b46ff3c0e8f410d7feb2b5d","title":"HTML5","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Arkaitz Garro"],"language":"es","year":null,"publisher":"","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Programación","HTML and CSS"],"source":"Free Programming Books","source_url":"https://openlibra.com/es/book/html5","cover_url":"","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://openlibra.com/es/book/html5"}],"access":"author_free","license":"","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"22a9f358777469195ae4","list_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EbookFoundation/free-programming-books/main/books/free-programming-books-es.md"},"providers":[{"source":"Free Programming Books","source_id":"22a9f358777469195ae4","source_url":"https://openlibra.com/es/book/html5","language":"es","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://openlibra.com/es/book/html5"}],"access":"author_free","license":"","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:96141f4d6ef0613e715720ab","title":"Humanistische Lebensbegleitung in Krisenzeiten","subtitle":"","description":"Jede Zeit hat ihre Krisen, jedes Leben seine Erschütterungen. In dieser Zeit bedrängen uns antidemokratische und autokratische Bewegungen, neue Kriege, soziale Ungleichheit und Klimawandel. Zudem ist kein menschliches Leben gefeit vor existenziellen Widerfahrnissen: Gewalt und Krankheit, Unfälle und Unglücke, Verlust und Tod, Einsamkeit und Sinnlosigkeit. Der Sammelband untersucht die Potentiale von Philosophie, Psychologie und humanistischer Weltanschauung, Menschen beim Umgang mit schwierigen Herausforderungen zu unterstützen. Neben wissenschaftlichen Beiträgen enthält das Buch Praxisreflexionen eines Psychotherapeuten, von Lehrer:innen und einer humanistischen Beraterin. Ob Lebenskunst, heitere Melancholie, Resilienz, Dialektik der Hoffnung, Helfen ohne Heil oder das Philosophieren mit Kindern: Die vorgestellten Strategien und Konzepte bieten Umgangs- und Auswegsoptionen, ohne doch mögliche Grenzen zu verschweigen. Kurzum: eine Fundgrube kritischer Zuversicht für professionell in sozialen, pädagogischen oder psychologischen Berufen Tätige wie für uns alle in den kleinen und großen Schlamasseln der Welt.","authors":