ast Europe, a cultural, ecclesiastical and educational history emerged, as well as a politically recognizably differentiated living environment, which differed from that of the West and is currently the subject of great interest. The series focuses on the contribution of a differentiating Christianity to this process.","authors":[],"language":"de","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["DG Title","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QR Religion and beliefs::QRM Christianity","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QR Religion and beliefs::QRM Christianity::QRMB Christian Churches, denominations, groups"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181497","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/691ff451-e351-40ae-aa7a-67905f4b9cd3/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116874/1/9783111376530.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181497","handle":"20.500.12854/181497","dspace_uuid":"b4d0a787-7fbd-49e1-931d-14f3cc500c1e"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181497","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181497","language":"de","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116874/1/9783111376530.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:f5f704e3ae519e3b3da4a8b4","title":"Initia Reformationis Transsilvaniae","subtitle":"Vielfalt, Aufbrüche, Rezeptionsräume in der Frühen Neuzeit","description":"In the early modern period, Central Europe was a dynamic region, interconnected with its neighbors in many ways and characterized by ethnic and religious diversity. In the geographically broadly defined area of contact between north and south-east, west and east Europe, a cultural, ecclesiastical and educational history emerged, as well as a politically recognizably differentiated living environment, which differed from that of the West and is currently the subject of great interest. The series focuses on the contribution of a differentiating Christianity to this process.","authors":[],"language":"de","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["DG Title","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QR Religion and beliefs::QRM Christianity","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QR Religion and beliefs::QRM Christianity::QRMB Christian Churches, denominations, groups"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116874","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/6f823139-da4b-46a1-b3b4-e4c6fe646500/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/2673eafa-544f-4d69-b905-9259227fb176/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116874","handle":"20.500.12657/116874","dspace_uuid":"976eb269-3a29-4fe8-8888-49ee404a1424"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116874","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116874","language":"de","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/2673eafa-544f-4d69-b905-9259227fb176/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:7f58ad34be8de34320a12057","title":"Initiation im höfischen Roman","subtitle":"Ein ritualtheoretischer Beitrag zur historischen Narratologie insbesondere des Artusromans","description":"Open-Access-Transformationspaket 2026 The study examines the relationship between historical rites of passage (knighting, coronation, marriage) and 12th- and 13th-century courtly narrative traditions. It analyzes how French and German courtly romances render these transitional rituals in narrative form, reflect upon them, and subject them to critical inquiry. In doing so, it uncovers the ritual logics that are essential for understanding the romances in their historical context.","authors":["Barton, Ulrich"],"language":"de","year":2026,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Chivalric romance","Historical narratology","Initiation","Rites of passage","Höfischer Roman","Historische Narratologie","Übergangsrituale","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism::DSB Literary studies: general::DSBB Literary studies: ancient, classical and medieval","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism::DSA Literary theory","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116889","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/e09da694-5362-4661-849b-05b93ee7f04e/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/8115849a-e6a0-4f3d-9253-17b79df376a0/retrieve"},{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116889/1/9783112242636.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116889","handle":"20.500.12657/116889","dspace_uuid":"83a39d3d-9df2-424e-9251-140560efeedf","doab_source_id":"20.500.12854/181462","doab_handle":"20.500.12854/181462","doab_dspace_uuid":"9be1dfea-d2ba-4517-bc2e-a173b0cc4f47"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.1265