tion that allowed us to determine that the complexity of society is directly reflected in the school, which, as a mirror, observes how the foundations of knowledge and wisdom have to share ideological spaces with practical aspects and social conflicts. In this framework, school mediation and restorative practices are conceived as tools that contribute to preventing escalation towards situations of violence and at the same time constitute an opportunity to train adolescents and young people for life in democracy, peace and human rights.","authors":["Ramón-Pineda, Miguel Ángel","Espinoza-Freire, Eudaldo Enrique"],"language":"es","year":2024,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/vedl8370","subjects":["Conflictos estudiantiles","Mediación escolar","Prácticas restaurativas","Convivencia escolar","Derechos humanos","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JN Education"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178547.2","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/245ebd4e-ae7d-4983-92ee-e9bdb4698646/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/178547.2","handle":"20.500.12854/178547.2","dspace_uuid":"342da58d-55c0-4f6b-847f-4033b9aab4d7"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/178547.2","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178547.2","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:c3a693418d186787409aab09","title":"La science et l'hypothèse","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Henri Poincaré"],"language":"fr","year":1900,"publisher":"Bloomsbury Publishing Plc","isbn":["9781440063701","0344896366","9798524272577","9780344896361","1602065055","9781980881421","9781521336533","1652606084","9781980376088","1522034765","9780486602219","9781522034766","1350026778","9782080810564","9798753026392","9781723766947","048678617X","9780342852604","1521336539","9780486143484","1798157470","0486602214","0344318184","9780344318177","1723766941","9781387888078","135002676X","1980881421","1976861047","1720244391","1440063702","9788467001433","9781350026766","1350355577","9780486786179","9781350026759","1980376085","0342852604","9780344318184","9781350026773","0344318176","2080810561","9798537140900","1717999123","9798810954958","9781798157473","9798656493581","9781652606086","8467001437","1387888072","9781350355576","9781976861048","1350026751","9798548764935","9781717999122","9780557321407","9781720244394","9780342852611","9798534149487","9798546421021","9798355476571","0486143481","0557321409","9798535001647","0342852612","9781602065055","9798732509441"],"doi":"","subjects":[],"source":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL708894W","cover_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5702803-M.jpg","formats":[{"type":"read","url":"https://archive.org/details/b21641031_0"}],"access":"open_access","license":"","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"OL708894W","openlibrary_work":"OL708894W","openlibrary_edition":"OL13276247M","internet_archive":"b21641031_0"},"providers":[{"source":"Open Library","source_id":"OL708894W","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL708894W","language":"fr","formats":[{"type":"read","url":"https://archive.org/details/b21641031_0"}],"access":"open_access","license":"","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:1b053560b21ae3582b814415","title":"La última ilusión","subtitle":"La crisis de la revolución en América Latina, 1979-1991","description":"La última ilusión. La crisis de la revolución en América Latina, 1979-1991 analiza el ocaso de los proyectos revolucionarios latinoamericanos a partir de la experiencia del sandinismo en Nicaragua. Por medio de fuentes periodísticas de la época y un trabajo crítico, este ensayo examina cómo la izquierda latinoamericana transitó de la esperanza transformadora a la crisis ideológica y política que marcó el final del siglo XX.A través de enclaves históricos como las tensiones entre revolución y democracia, el impacto de la Guerra Fría y la influencia del imperialismo estadounidense en la desestabilización de los movimientos revolucionarios, Valeria Manzano centra su eje analítico en el triunfo y posterior derrota electoral del Frente Sandinista de Liberación Nacional, símbolo de una generación que buscaba reconciliar la utopía con la práctica democrática.Esta obra es una reflexión sobre la persistencia de las ideas y la nostalgia del cambio. Con un enfoque interdisciplinario contribuye a la comprensión de la política, la memoria y los desafíos contemporáneos de América Latina.","authors":["Manzano (0009000049389553), Valeria"],"language":"es","year":2026,"publisher":"Bielefeld University Press","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64136/mmlh4594","subjects":["Revolución","América Latina","Nicaragua","Revolución Sandinista","Izquierda política","Movimientos revolucionarios","Historia","Política","Gobierno","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History::NHT History: specific events and topics::NHTV Revolutions, uprisings, rebellions","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JP Politics and government::JPF Political ideologies and movements::JPFC Far-left political ideologies and movements","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JP Politics and government::JPF Political ideologies and movements::JPFF Left-of-centre democratic ideologies","thema EDItEUR::1 Place qualifiers::1K The Americas::1KL Latin America – Mexico, Central America, South America"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181516","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/046448b6-3773-4201-a5cd-655342963c82/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116590/1/9783691290479.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-ND","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181516","handle":"20.500.12854/181516","dspace_uuid":"a623d331-4d8d-432b-ace1-71233636fc4b"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181516","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181516","language":"es","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116590/1/9783691290479.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-ND","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:76a6b6750cd2bb5652defe10","title":"Lady Audley's Secret","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Braddon, M. E. (Mary Elizabeth)"],"language":"en","year":null,"publisher":"Project Gutenberg","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Bigamy -- Fiction","Deception -- Fiction","Domestic fiction","England -- Fiction","Married women -- Fiction","Psychological fiction","Category: British Literature","Category: Crime, Thrillers and Mystery","Category: Novels"],"source":"Project Gutenberg","source_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/8954","cover_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/8954/pg8954.cover.medium.jpg","formats":[{"type":"html","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/8954.html.images"},{"type":"epub","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/8954.epub3.images"},{"type":"mobi","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/8954.kf8.images"},{"type":"text","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/8954.txt.utf-8"},{"type":"text","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/files/8954/8954-8.txt"}],"access":"public_domain","license":"Public domain in the United States","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"8954","gutenberg_id":"8954"},"providers":[{"source":"Project Gutenberg","source_id":"8954","source_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/8954","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"html","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/8954.html.images"},{"type":"epub","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/8954.epub3.images"},{"type":"mobi","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/8954.kf8.images"},{"type":"text","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/8954.txt.utf-8"},{"type":"text","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/files/8954/8954-8.txt"}],"access":"public_domain","license":"Public domain in the United States","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:9a6fe23823d61b42f8522e75","title":"Language and Reason in Islamic Thought","subtitle":"Faḫr al-Dīn al-Rāzī’s Reconciliation of Manṭiq and Bayān","description":"This study delves into Fakhr al-Dīn al-Rāzī's (1149–1210) theory of language, a pivotal yet underexplored facet of his intellectual legacy. Moving beyond his interactions with the Avicennian tradition, it positions al-Rāzī as an independent thinker. The work examines two often misinterpreted dimensions of his thought: his assertion that all concepts are self-evident, challenging traditional epistemology on conceptualization ( taṣawwur ) as advanced by Abū Naṣr al-Fārābī (870–950) and Ibn Sīnā (980–1037), and his refinement of ʿAbd-l-Qāhir al-Ğurğānī’s (1009–1078) theory of linguistic composition ( naẓm ), emphasizing language’s expressive capacity ( bayān ) and the Qurʾān’s unique linguistic structure. By analyzing these facets, the study reconstructs al-Rāzī’s comprehensive framework for understanding linguistic phenomena, bridging the Greek-inspired falsafa tradition and the rich Arabic linguistic heritage. This exploration offers scholars and students a nuanced perspective on Islamic intellectual history, highlighting al-Rāzī’s role in harmonizing diverse traditions and advancing a profound theory of linguistic understanding. This theory is essential for engaging with al-Rāzī’s extensive written heritage.","authors":["najafi, mostafa"],"language":"en","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Faḫr l-Dīn al-Rāzī","Bayān","Manṭiq","Language Theory","Logik","Sprachtheorie","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QR Religion and beliefs::QRP Islam::QRPP Islamic life and practice"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181477","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/343d8acc-7682-4e3b-b3e5-71d82cdf55a4/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116675/1/9783112205983.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181477","handle":"20.500.12854/181477","dspace_uuid":"17f516a5-294f-4812-bd44-8c486db3df42"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181477","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181477","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116675/1/9783112205983.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:ac4f10671040dc5e06828ea1","title":"LAS CUATRO ESPOSAS","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["vaddy1307"],"language":"es","year":1989,"publisher":"","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["vaddy"],"source":"Internet Archive","source_url":"https://archive.org/details/LASCUATROESPOSAS","cover_url":"https://archive.org/services/img/LASCUATROESPOSAS","formats":[],"access":"creative_commons","license":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"LASCUATROESPOSAS","internet_archive":"LASCUATROESPOSAS"},"providers":[{"source":"Internet Archive","source_id":"LASCUATROESPOSAS","source_url":"https://archive.org/details/LASCUATROESPOSAS","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"creative_commons","license":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:10c120bc1c80e913d192fac8","title":"Las tecnologías disruptivas: vía para la transformación del aprendizaje","subtitle":"","description":"Current technological transformations are redefining the ways of teaching, learning, and constructing knowledge within educational systems. Disruptive Technologies: A Pathway to the Transformation of Contemporary Learning analyzes this process from a critical and forward-looking perspective, focusing on the potential of educational robotics and generative artificial intelligence as drivers of pedagogical innovation. The book explores how these technologies, when integrated through coherent didactic and methodological approaches, strengthen active, interdisciplinary, and contextualized learning. Drawing on conceptual frameworks such as TPACK and STEM, the text proposes a balanced articulation among pedagogical knowledge, disciplinary expertise, and technological resources, highlighting the importance of intentional and reflective teacher mediation. One of the central contributions of the work is the design of a professional teacher training model aimed at developing competencies for formative management with disruptive technologies. This model takes shape in a structured, flexible, and assessable strategy that promotes continuous improvement in educational practice and its adaptation to diverse institutional contexts. Additionally, the book presents active methodologies, gamification dynamics, simulation, and collaborative work, along with educational experiences that demonstrate the impact of these technologies on motivation, creativity, and problem-solving. From an ethical and humanistic perspective, the book invites readers to rethink the teacher’s role as a designer of innovative and meaningful learning experiences. Addressed to teachers, researchers, and educational leaders, this text stands as an academic reference for those seeking to understand, plan, and implement transformative educational processes aligned with the demands of the present and the future.","authors":["Baute-Rosales, Mireya","Espinoza-Soria, María José","Soler-McCook, Jorge Miguel","Chávez-Cárdenas, María del Carmen"],"language":"es","year":2026,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/dovj2960","subjects":["Tecnologías disruptivas","Inteligencia artificial generativa","Robótica educativa","Formación docente","Innovación pedagógica","thema EDItEUR::U Computing and Information Technology"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178503.2","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/ac622e37-94c7-4768-bbad-4432b5d89601/retrieve","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/178503.2","handle":"20.500.12854/178503.2","dspace_uuid":"c232b2b4-05ad-4a90-8e6f-f9fd5a0d09bc"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/178503.2","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/178503.2","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:1e4c588e032716b47dcaa5c6","title":"Laserstrahlschweißen von Metallen mit niedrigsiedenden Legierungselementen","subtitle":"","description":"Themengebiete selektive Verdampfung und Kapillarinstabilitäten untersucht. Die Untersuchungen werden zum Großteil mit magnesium- und zinklegierten Aluminiumlegierungen durchgeführt, da diese Werkstoffe bereits für geringe Legierungsgehalte deutlich reduzierte Verdampfungstemperaturen aufweisen. Durch einen Abgleich von Stofftransportmodellen mit experimentellen Ergebnissen und der Anpassung von Materialkennwerten können die Modelle zur Vorhersage des Legierungselementverlustes und des Verdampfungsstroms niedrigsiedender Elemente genutzt werden. Als das wesentliche Ergebnis der Untersuchungen kann Blasensieden als Ursache von Kapillarinstabilitäten identifiziert werden. Das Phänomen wird umfassend charakterisiert und ein Entstehungsmechanismus vorgeschlagen, der die Erkenntnisse aus den Untersuchungen zur selektiven Verdampfung aufgreift. Darüber hinaus wird ein Kriterium für das Blasensieden formuliert.","authors":["Hugger, Florian"],"language":"de","year":2026,"publisher":"FAU University Press","isbn":[],"doi":"10.25593/978-3-96147-934-4","subjects":["Laserstrahlschweißen","Verdampfung","Legierungen","Niedrigsiedende Legierungselemente","Legierungsverlust","Blasensieden","thema EDItEUR::T Technology, Engineering, Agriculture, Industrial processes::TG Mechanical engineering and materials::TGP Production and industrial engineering"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116945","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/ec4a6ffd-de3b-4610-a560-ccbbae1dacb3/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/cdcdfe2d-83de-4eca-bfe8-88456eee0f37/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116945","handle":"20.500.12657/116945","dspace_uuid":"dc95bf76-5850-4afe-b74a-8abac47eb092"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116945","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116945","language":"de","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/cdcdfe2d-83de-4eca-bfe8-88456eee0f37/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:e2827ce1865261e7a3aa3790","title":"Lattanzio e la ›virtus‹","subtitle":"La critica a Lucilio e Cicerone nel VI libro delle ›Divinae Institutiones‹","description":"This volume assesses how the Satirist Lucilius (2nd century BC) and the statesman and orator Cicero (1st century BC), in their attempt at integrating mos maiorum and Greek virtue (ἀρετή), give the opportunity for the apologist Lactantius (3rd-4th century AD) to confront two witnesses of Roman cultural history in the field of “military” and “ethical” virtus : he remoulds their assertions through a strongly biased, but deeply conceived reenactment. In Div. inst. 6.5.1 ̶ 6.24, Lactantius rejects both the definitions of virtus exposed by Lucilius (vv. 1326 ̶ 1338 Marx) and Cicero’s reflections upon the officia vivendi and his notion of honestum (Off. 1.34 ̶ 41): one after the other, they are accordingly involved by the apologist in a vehement attack against the Roman empire. By regarding the pre-Christian empire as one based on injustice, Lactantius claims a demand for a restored virtus , grounded in agnitione Dei . After contrasting Lucilius’s stance about commoda patriai (v. 1337) as the peak of traditional Roman virtue, the apologist stigmatizes its underlying utilitarian ethics, and argues with the interplay between politics, law, and philosophy, on which Cicero allegedly founded the legitimacy of Roman expansionist imperialism.","authors":["Perruccio, Andrea"],"language":"it","year":2026,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Lucilius on Virtue","Cicero's orations","Lactantius's ideology","Lucilius und Tugend","Ciceros Reden","Lactantius' Ideologie","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DB Ancient, classical and medieval texts::DBS Ancient Sagas and epics::DBSG Ancient Greek and Roman literature","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QD Philosophy::QDH Philosophical traditions and schools of thought::QDHA Ancient Greek and Roman philosophy","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History::NHG Middle Eastern history","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism::DSB Literary studies: general::DSBB Literary studies: ancient, classical and medieval"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116903","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/e5d8112d-8ccc-4552-a93e-d05a78ba8dd0/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/710decf3-20f3-4e5d-a80a-ef504701a268/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116903","handle":"20.500.12657/116903","dspace_uuid":"473fd39c-0fc6-48a6-ae42-515b4313fc6e"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116903","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116903","language":"it","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/710decf3-20f3-4e5d-a80a-ef504701a268/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:4db0a83c496e754c78de979d","title":"Law, Nature and the Ecosystem Approach","subtitle":"Modelling a Transcultural Eco-Legal Framework across Europe and Latin America","description":"This book argues that, beyond the apparent fracture between humans and nature that defines the Anthropocene crisis, there exists a shared cultural foundation in legal traditions, converging on the recognition of the intrinsic value of Nature and of the ecosystem interconnections between human and non-human life. The legal innovations explored here—particularly from Latin America—embody a holistic, integrated view coherent with the ecosystem approach. It is proposed that these ideas offer potential not only within their own legal systems but also as models for Western legal frameworks. Divided into five parts, the book maintains a balance between theoretical and empirical, combining foundational legal and philosophical discussions with practical case studies and applications. Part 1 establishes the theoretical foundation, setting the conceptual framework of the volume. Part 2 builds on this by addressing the methodological implications and laying the groundwork for a transition from anthropocentric to ecocentric governance. Parts 3 and 4 bridge theory with practice, exploring participatory tools, bottom-up initiatives, and challenges to traditional environmental law, illustrating how theoretical advancements are applied in specific legal and policy contexts. Part 5 focuses on jurisprudence and the role of the judiciary, providing an empirical analysis of how legal principles are interpreted and enforced in judicial settings. This progression ensures that the book effectively integrates theory with empirical research, underscoring its interdisciplinary and practical significance. The volume will be of interest to those working in the areas of Legal Philosophy, Environmental Law, Constitutional Law, Comparative Law, Human Rights, Anthropology and Environmental Studies. The Open Access version of this book, available at http://www.taylorfrancis.com, has been made available under a Creative Commons Attribution- Non Commercial-Share Alike (CC-BY-NC-SA)] 4.0 license.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"Taylor & Francis","isbn":[],"doi":"10.4324/9781003686682","subjects":["Environmental constitutionalism","Ecocentric governance","Rights of nonhuman animals","Decolonising property law","Participatory environmental policy","Indigenous legal traditions","Judicial enforcement of nature rights","thema EDItEUR::L Law::LN Laws of specific jurisdictions and specific areas of law::LNK Environment, transport and planning law: general::LNKJ Environment law","thema EDItEUR::L Law::LA Jurisprudence and general issues::LAM Comparative law","thema EDItEUR::L Law::LN Laws of specific jurisdictions and specific areas of law::LND Constitutional and administrative law: general::LNDC Law: Human rights and civil liberties","thema EDItEUR::L Law::LA Jurisprudence and general issues::LAB Methods, theory and philosophy of law","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JH Sociology and anthropology::JHM Anthropology","thema EDItEUR::R Earth Sciences, Geography, Environment, Planning::RN The environment::RNC Applied ecology","thema EDItEUR::L Law::LN Laws of specific jurisdictions and specific areas of law::LND Constitutional and administrative law: general","thema EDItEUR::L Law::LB International law::LBB Public international law::LBBR Public international law: human rights","thema EDItEUR::L Law::LA Jurisprudence and general issues","thema EDItEUR::L Law::LN Laws of specific jurisdictions and specific areas of law::LNC Company, commercial and competition law: general::LNCR Energy and natural resources law","thema EDItEUR::L Law::LN Laws of specific jurisdictions and specific areas of law","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QD Philosophy::QDT Topics in philosophy::QDTQ Ethics and moral philosophy"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/117014","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/233e43df-e366-487b-a658-c367f6af341d/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/85ac389d-3970-4033-8bc3-6abda7b7d957/retrieve"},{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/117014/1/9781040923184.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-SA · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/117014","handle":"20.500.12657/117014","dspace_uuid":"ac0c5583-cb32-4d83-8890-bcd2684df999","doab_source_id":"20.500.12854/181540","doab_handle":"20.500.12854/181540","doab_dspace_uuid":"6c31b4f9-e0b6-4c7b-99dd-a669f0255062"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/117014","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/117014","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/85ac389d-3970-4033-8bc3-6abda7b7d957/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-SA · Other open license","verified_legal":true},{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181540","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181540","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/117014/1/9781040923184.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-SA","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:d7e3a6d87c2d96ce1708b4e6","title":"Lawyers, Gatekeeping and Access to Justice","subtitle":"A Critical Analysis","description":"Lawyers face increasing pressure from clients, politicians, prospective hires and international and civil society organisations to act as gatekeepers: to reject certain clients or cases or mitigate their involvement. This can be at variance with the traditional role of lawyers to provide access to justice. This volume presents a systematic exploration of the gatekeeping debate. It discusses the key dimensions of gatekeeping, the risk of abuse of identifying lawyers with their clients in authoritarian regimes, the limits of partisan lawyering and the legal boundaries to representation. It also discusses the question of representation that may be in line with professional duties but still be considered controversial based on soft law or moral or societal expectations. A key takeaway is that the gatekeeping discussion would benefit from the differentiation between whether a client deserves representation and how a lawyer should represent the client. The contributions are written by high-profile academics and professionals from various jurisdictions around the globe, aiming to provide solid, multifaceted, balanced and comprehensive guidance 