ps://openstax.org/details/books/lifespan-development","cover_url":"https://assets.openstax.org/oscms-prodcms/media/documents/lifespan_development_lifespan_development_web_card.svg","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://assets.openstax.org/oscms-prodcms/media/documents/Lifespan_Development_-_WEB.pdf"},{"type":"read","url":"https://openstax.org/books/lifespan-development/pages/1-what-does-psychology-say"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike License 4.0","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"textbook","identifiers":{"source_id":"03481f82-baf1-407d-9bac-e614dae0a694","openstax_slug":"lifespan-development","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/"},"providers":[{"source":"OpenStax","source_id":"03481f82-baf1-407d-9bac-e614dae0a694","source_url":"https://openstax.org/details/books/lifespan-development","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://assets.openstax.org/oscms-prodcms/media/documents/Lifespan_Development_-_WEB.pdf"},{"type":"read","url":"https://openstax.org/books/lifespan-development/pages/1-what-does-psychology-say"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike License 4.0","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:53902d37b53611851031ed6c","title":"Light Verb Constructions from a Cross-Linguistic Perspective","subtitle":"","description":"Light verb constructions are complex predicates consisting of a semantically reduced verb and an additional often phrasal element contributing the main predicational content. Although light verb constructions have been identified for various (genetically unrelated) languages, a comparative concept which allows identifying light verb constructions across languages is still missing. The present volume approaches this issue from the perspective of the analysis of individual languages. The basic research question underlying the formation of the volume is: Which properties manifest light verb constructions cross linguistically? The papers collected in the volume investigate a large range of languages from different languages families which includes Indo-European languages like Aheli, Italian, Scottish Gaelic and Old West Norse but also non-Indo-European languages such as Tibetan (Sino-Tibetan), Kina Rutul (Nakh-Dagestanian) and Gĩkũyũ (Bantu). The present volume fills a gap in the cross-linguistics discussion of light verb constructions and seeks to provide novel insights concerning a widely recognized type of complex predicate construction.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Light Verb Constructions","Complex Predicates","Cross-Linguistic Comparison","Light-Verb-Konstruktionen","Komplexe Prädikate","Sprachübergreifender Vergleich","thema EDItEUR::C Language and Linguistics::CF Linguistics","thema EDItEUR::C Language and Linguistics::CF Linguistics::CFK Grammar, syntax and morphology","thema EDItEUR::C Language and Linguistics::CF Linguistics::CFG Semantics, discourse analysis, stylistics","thema EDItEUR::C Language and Linguistics::CF Linguistics::CFF Historical and comparative linguistics"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116816","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/f2311f00-e349-41eb-a12d-b366f7218ae2/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/53140c3f-bf3d-43be-a628-afa7a4e7840b/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116816","handle":"20.500.12657/116816","dspace_uuid":"9dad7201-a4fe-4d5f-a309-89db7aff8dad"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116816","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116816","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/53140c3f-bf3d-43be-a628-afa7a4e7840b/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:c5febb66bf66a6e51304a8ec","title":"Light Verb Constructions from a Cross-Linguistic Perspective","subtitle":"","description":"Light verb constructions are complex predicates consisting of a semantically reduced verb and an additional often phrasal element contributing the main predicational content. Although light verb constructions have been identified for various (genetically unrelated) languages, a comparative concept which allows identifying light verb constructions across languages is still missing. The present volume approaches this issue from the perspective of the analysis of individual languages. The basic research question underlying the formation of the volume is: Which properties manifest light verb constructions cross linguistically? The papers collected in the volume investigate a large range of languages from different languages families which includes Indo-European languages like Aheli, Italian, Scottish Gaelic and Old West Norse but also non-Indo-European languages such as Tibetan (Sino-Tibetan), Kina Rutul (Nakh-Dagestanian) and Gĩkũyũ (Bantu). The present volume fills a gap in the cross-linguistics discussion of light verb constructions and seeks to provide novel insights concerning a widely recognized type of complex predicate construction.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Light Verb Constructions","Complex Predicates","Cross-Linguistic Comparison","Light-Verb-Konstruktionen","Komplexe Prädikate","Sprachübergreifender Vergleich","thema EDItEUR::C Language and Linguistics::CF Linguistics","thema EDItEUR::C Language and Linguistics::CF Linguistics::CFK Grammar, syntax and morphology","thema EDItEUR::C Language and Linguistics::CF Linguistics::CFG Semantics, discourse analysis, stylistics","thema EDItEUR::C Language and Linguistics::CF Linguistics::CFF Historical and comparative linguistics"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181511","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/46e2284b-578e-4b12-a799-5844ea19144d/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116816/1/9783112229330.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181511","handle":"20.500.12854/181511","dspace_uuid":"7dc39c06-88bd-431f-981e-c0918e767dbe"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181511","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181511","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116816/1/9783112229330.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:ce3083fb6b4220fcac95a845","title":"Linguistische Wissenschaftsforschung","subtitle":"Zur sprachlichen Hervorbringung von Wissenschaft am Beispiel der Germanistischen Linguistik","description":"The German Linguistic Studies Series is a comprehensive and outstanding forum in its field. It has borne the name of its subject in its title since the foundation of the series in the eighth decade of the last century. The series is comprehensive in the broad spectrum of topics covered (language levels, varieties, communication forms, epochs) in the range of research perspectives (theoretical and empirical studies, fundamental research and applications, interdisciplinarity with psychology, the social sciences etc.) and methodologies (the sole criterion is quality), in the rhythm of research (trends are perceived and also set, achievements are secured) and in the forms of presentation (monographs, textbooks, collected volumes, dictionaries). Professorial theses, outstanding doctoral theses, pioneering research findings from wider contexts, but also the surprising ‛stroke of genius’ set the standards for inclusion in the series. Call for Book Proposals: https://blog.degruyter.com/call-for-book-proposals-reihe-germanistische-linguistik/","authors":["Kalwa, Nina"],"language":"de","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Science studies","Practices","Constructivism","Culture","Wissenschaftsforschung","Praktiken","Konstruktivismus","Kultur","thema EDItEUR::C Language and Linguistics::CF Linguistics","thema EDItEUR::C Language and Linguistics::CJ Language teaching and learning"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116842","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/530dbd11-8675-4337-847d-76ffa4ac810d/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/c1e7f815-948d-4a43-841d-36adde04e9ec/retrieve"},{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116842/1/9783112223154.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116842","handle":"20.500.12657/116842","dspace_uuid":"98e63905-498f-49f4-86b3-2de4be1f0936","doab_source_id":"20.500.12854/181502","doab_handle":"20.500.12854/181502","doab_dspace_uuid":"b491138c-0669-4f28-b4d7-87f41290b6b1"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116842","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116842","language":"de","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/c1e7f815-948d-4a43-841d-36adde04e9ec/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY · Other open license","verifie