1347","007860091X","0078296358","007860169X","9780078601293","9780078601699","9780078296314","9780028343143","0078228662","9780078652639","9780078601378","9780078610578","9780078600869"],"doi":"","subjects":[],"source":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL14996338W","cover_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1089515-M.jpg","formats":[],"access":"digital_lending","license":"","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"OL14996338W","openlibrary_work":"OL14996338W","openlibrary_edition":"OL9973916M","internet_archive":"mathematicsappli0000mcgr_s7z4"},"providers":[{"source":"Open Library","source_id":"OL14996338W","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL14996338W","language":"en","formats":[],"access":"digital_lending","license":"","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:c451bdd19daaae330004d369","title":"Matrix of Work","subtitle":"Through a Dark Valley – On the Road to Prosperity and Freedom?!","description":"The “Matrix of Work” provides an interdisciplinary “big picture” of the global history of human work from its beginnings to the end of the 21st century. In the sense of a matrix, the book encompasses both an in-depth analysis of the essential structural elements of the epochs of work and an examination of overarching dimensions across epochal boundaries. Empirical research forms the core of the matrix materials. It includes an extensive compilation of data from the disciplines of economic and social statistics, archaeology, ethnology and global historical research on productivity, working and living hours, domestic and family work, consumption baskets and their distribution, and much more. These findings are presented in the form of timelines, tables and informative graphics. Based on this data and knowledge of the current state of research in these fields, theses are formulated to understand the big picture. Anyone with an interest in the history and future of work will find new insights, thought-provoking arguments, and distinctive set of long-term data highly valuable.","authors":["Zukunft der Arbeit, Institut für die Geschichte und"],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Global history","Labor history","Productivity","Globalgeschichte","Geschichte der Arbeit","Produktivität","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History::NHT History: specific events and topics::NHTB Social and cultural history","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JH Sociology and anthropology::JHB Sociology::JHBL Sociology: work and labour","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History::NHB General and world history","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116910","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/7a853ec1-7eb1-475b-87f7-d4d324ceeffc/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/423c9e30-d23a-4975-826b-d2f1a3c64274/retrieve"},{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116910/1/9783112212301.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116910","handle":"20.500.12657/116910","dspace_uuid":"92c78975-0a27-4757-ac8e-4bc9b46184bf","doab_source_id":"20.500.12854/181495","doab_handle":"20.500.12854/181495","doab_dspace_uuid":"c8aeddb5-d1a7-4e2b-9206-38c21bf995ca"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116910","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116910","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/423c9e30-d23a-4975-826b-d2f1a3c64274/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY · Other open license","verified_legal":true},{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181495","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181495","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116910/1/9783112212301.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:d5dccc1623e68479ba7fbb66","title":"Measuring the Unmeasurable","subtitle":"Social Love in Citizens and Institutions Across the Globe","description":"This book argues that love is not just a fleeting emotion, but rather an action that can bring tangible benefits to people. Its practical approach to love reveals a public dimension that makes love important in a co-governance perspective, as it contributes to citizens’ well-being and institutional guidance. Rooted in the debate of how well-being can be operationalized by integrating classic indicators of progress and wealth with other relational dimensions, this book proposes a new measurement: The World Love Index, a transnational secondary data analysis, measures how much people from different countries care for others and the world. In the current post-pandemic context, marked by conflicts and identity issues, the proposed new index aims to signal the transition toward a new social ecology. It can be considered a complementary of alternative measure to the GDP. The book provides the theoretical framework supporting the usage of the World Love Index and it presents the Index’s results, focusing on the tole of citizens and institutions, and analyzing methods, social capital, and policies such as migration and welfare policies. The volume also identifies open challenges for a more supportive and inclusive world.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Social Love","Well-being","Solidarity","Transnational Index","Secondary data analysis","Bürger","Liebe","Solidarität","Wohlbefinden","Wohlfahrt","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JM Psychology"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116822","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/94616b74-adbf-4c22-8767-988286cd4219/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/75250c51-387d-4cc9-97e0-90ef1a12aeed/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116822","handle":"20.500.12657/116822","dspace_uuid":"e9a29ecd-7a6c-403a-ac62-878a051cbce4"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116822","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116822","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/75250c51-387d-4cc9-97e0-90ef1a12aeed/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:d91d8e416a8f1c964ca07485","title":"Media Accountability and Corruption in Africa","subtitle":"Contestations and Controversies","description":"Gathering scholarly voices and case studies from 10 sub-Saharan African countries, Media Accountability and Corruption in Africa is an open access look at how media influences governance, accountability, and public perceptions of corruption on the continent. The book offers an outline of the media's role in corruption in sub-Saharan Africa, then guides readers along as it examines specific countries and issues in depth via four thematic sub-sections: these explore media representations of corruption; media corruption and accountability; social media and corruption; and media capture and journalistic safety. Both editors and all contributors are based in sub-Saharan Africa, and their real-world, lived experiences of the contexts they write about enable new and critical insights into how media sometimes aids corruption and sometimes helps to expose and fight it. For its fresh theoretical interventions and detailed examples, this collection is valuable resource for scholars, practitioners, and policymakers interested in development, media accountability, and political transparency in Africa. The ebook editions of this book are available open access under a CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 licence on bloomsburycollections.com. Open access was funded by the Bloomsbury Open Collections Library Collective.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"Bloomsbury Publishing (UK)","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["African politics","International development","Media accountability","Corruption","Media farming","Media capture","thema EDItEUR::G Reference, Information and Interdisciplinary subjects::GT Interdisciplinary studies::GTP Development studies","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JB Society and culture: general::JBC Cultural and media studies::JBCT Media studies::JBCT1 Media studies: internet, digital media and society","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JP Politics and government::JPZ Corruption in politics, government and society","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JB Society and culture: general::JBF Social and ethical issues::JBFV Ethical issues and debates","thema EDItEUR::K Economics, Finance, Business and Management::KN Industry and industrial studies::KNT Media, entertainment, information and communication industries","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JB Society and culture: general::JBC Cultural and media studies::JBCT Media studies","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JB Society and culture: general::JBF Social and ethical issues::JBFV Ethical issues and debates::JBFV5 Ethical issues: scientific, technological and medical developments","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JP Politics and government::JPH P