e":"Scriba di nessuna causa apparente","description":"Love, politics, and knowledge are the conceptual fires through which Carlo Montaleone attempts to capture the highly controversial figure of Michel de Montaigne. He who had defined himself as the observer without knowledge, the magistrate without jurisdiction and the jester of comedy is the author of a book, the Essays, which from the end of the sixteenth century did not cease to arouse admiration and dismay. His way of writing – in leaps and trippings, as he himself admits – and his choice not to offer answers carved in marble under any circumstances, represent the ingredients of a discourse on reality that the very different conditions of today do not prevent us from feeling as profoundly ours.","authors":["Montaleone, Carlo"],"language":"it","year":2026,"publisher":"Milano University Press","isbn":[],"doi":"10.54103/fsu.324","subjects":["Love","Atoms","Mal de la pierre","Language","Fallibilism","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QD Philosophy"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181628","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/ea840232-9c05-431a-955b-a88fa8a84e7c/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"read","url":"https://libri.unimi.it/index.php/fsu/en/catalog/view/324/1445/3499"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181628","handle":"20.500.12854/181628","dspace_uuid":"eb5ce898-cd89-42a1-a5ae-47eba0ebb24f"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181628","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181628","language":"it","formats":[{"type":"read","url":"https://libri.unimi.it/index.php/fsu/en/catalog/view/324/1445/3499"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"