97M","internet_archive":"moremathematical00gard"},"providers":[{"source":"Open Library","source_id":"OL459993W","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL459993W","language":"de","formats":[],"access":"digital_lending","license":"","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:8a669f98b245beabf5a277b4","title":"Mots en jeu(x) – expériences, réflexions et découvertes","subtitle":"","description":"This volume showcases the multiple dimensions of wordplay in contemporary Francophone contexts by bringing academic approaches into dialog with practical reflections and experiences. The authors explore the various possibilities offered by words and language, highlighting the significance of wordplay across diverse fields, for various groups of people, and in a range of different usage contexts. Wordplay emerges both as a shared cultural resource and as a medium through which a great variety of topics and issues can be articulated.","authors":[],"language":"fr","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Frankophonie","Wortspiel","thema EDItEUR::G Reference, Information and Interdisciplinary subjects::GT Interdisciplinary studies::GTC Communication studies"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116836","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/f18c3996-459a-4013-9988-72337d9717a0/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/04c985a6-25ef-4f57-b3a0-c6adb4b0f18a/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116836","handle":"20.500.12657/116836","dspace_uuid":"467969b4-6013-4ade-b6fd-a84f2f3bec3a"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116836","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116836","language":"fr","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/04c985a6-25ef-4f57-b3a0-c6adb4b0f18a/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:9cc563c76851f790c2d78aa3","title":"Mr. Standfast","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Buchan, John"],"language":"en","year":null,"publisher":"Project Gutenberg","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Hannay, Richard (Fictitious character) -- Fiction","Intelligence service -- Great Britain -- Fiction","Spy stories","War stories","World War, 1914-1918 -- Fiction","Adventure","Category: Adventure","Category: British Literature","Category: Crime, Thrillers and Mystery","Category: Historical Novels","Category: Novels","Contemporary Reviews","Movie Books","World War I"],"source":"Project Gutenberg","source_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/560","cover_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/560/pg560.cover.medium.jpg","formats":[{"type":"html","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/560.html.images"},{"type":"epub","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/560.epub3.images"},{"type":"mobi","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/560.kf8.images"},{"type":"html","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/files/560/560-h.zip"},{"type":"text","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/560.txt.utf-8"},{"type":"text","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/files/560/560.txt"}],"access":"public_domain","license":"Public domain in the United States","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"560","gutenberg_id":"560"},"providers":[{"source":"Project Gutenberg","source_id":"560","source_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/560","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"html","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/560.html.images"},{"type":"epub","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/560.epub3.images"},{"type":"mobi","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/560.kf8.images"},{"type":"html","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/files/560/560-h.zip"},{"type":"text","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/560.txt.utf-8"},{"type":"text","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/files/560/560.txt"}],"access":"public_domain","license":"Public domain in the United States","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:3adcfc728fc01ab8e0841321","title":"Multilingualism, Migration, and Domestic Work","subtitle":"On the Sociolinguistic Situation of Filipina Domestic Migrant Workers in Madrid","description":"How do Filipina domestic workers experience multilingualism in their daily lives? To whom do they ascribe or deny agency in their narratives of language and migration? This study explores the intersection of multilingualism and transnational migration in the global sector of domestic work in Spain, the second largest labor market in the EU. Over the course of three years, a corpus of field notes, narrative interviews, focus groups, language portraits and language maps was built with 25 Filipina domestic workers (FDWs) in Madrid, partly collected through participatory approaches. The analysis focuses on three main aspects: first, spatial repertoires; second, the multilingual everyday life and lived experiences of languages; and third, the agency of FDWs. The aim of this study is to better understand the dynamics that emerge from inequalities of multilingualism in the feminized sector of transnational domestic work. The book expands our understanding of multilingualism and transnational migration in the feminized sector of paid domestic work. It is a pioneering contribution to the growing field of language and migration, offering new insights into the sociolinguistic aspects of migration from Spain’s only former colony in Asia to Spain. Theoretically, the study adds a postcolonial and critical approach to language and migration, using a variety of methodological techniques.","authors":["Issel-Dombert, Sandra"],"language":"en","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Migration","Care","Spain","The Philippines","thema EDItEUR::C Language and Linguistics::CF Linguistics","thema EDItEUR::C Language and Linguistics::CJ Language teaching and learning","thema EDItEUR::C Language and Linguistics::CF Linguistics::CFB Sociolinguistics","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JB Society and culture: general::JBF Social and ethical issues::JBFH Migration, immigration and emigration"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116798","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/a61e0121-d2a5-4146-94c4-78e5dfe6001f/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/ff52990f-e73c-4872-a5bb-3ece13863509/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116798","handle":"20.500.12657/116798","dspace_uuid":"4328efd7-8ea5-46d6-842b-3c0273ebf5d9"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116798","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116798","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/ff52990f-e73c-4872-a5bb-3ece13863509/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:44ef1c221fe385c9649e4c25","title":"Multilingualität in der Stadt","subtitle":"Eine sprachhistorische und soziokommunikative Untersuchung zu Lviv/Lemberg 1848–1918","description":"The German Linguistic Studies Series is a comprehensive and outstanding forum in its field. It has borne the name of its subject in its title since the foundation of the series in the eighth decade of the last century. The series is comprehensive in the broad spectrum of topics covered (language levels, varieties, communication forms, epochs) in the range of research perspectives (theoretical and empirical studies, fundamental research and applications, interdisciplinarity with psychology, the social sciences etc.) and methodologies (the sole criterion is quality), in the rhythm of research (trends are perceived and also set, achievements are secured) and in the forms of presentation (monographs, textbooks, collected volumes, dictionaries). Professorial theses, outstanding doctoral theses, pioneering research findings from wider contexts, but also the surprising ‛stroke of genius’ set the standards for inclusion in the series. Call for Book Proposals: https://blog.degruyter.com/call-for-book-proposals-reihe-germanistische-linguistik/","authors":["Ptashnyk, Stefaniya"],"language":"de","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Multilingualism","Urban linguistic history","Nineteenth century","Press and education","Mehrsprachigkeit","Urbane Sprachgeschichte","19. Jahrhundert","Pressewesen","Schulwesen","thema EDItEUR::C Language and Linguistics::CF Linguistics","thema EDItEUR::C Language and Linguistics::CJ Language teaching and learning","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History::NHD European history","thema EDItEUR::C Language and Linguistics::CF Linguistics::CFF Historical and comparative linguistics","thema EDItEUR::C Language and Linguistics::CF Linguistics::CFB Sociolinguistics"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116884","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/55a2b86f-a949-4239-ad73-9f2ebd89c330/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/4e104622-2948-4c39-988b-2ecb151e229c/retrieve"},{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116884/1/9783111624495.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116884","handle":"20.5