domain in the United States","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"23","gutenberg_id":"23"},"providers":[{"source":"Project Gutenberg","source_id":"23","source_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/23","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"html","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/23.html.images"},{"type":"epub","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/23.epub3.images"},{"type":"mobi","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/23.kf8.images"},{"type":"text","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/23.txt.utf-8"}],"access":"public_domain","license":"Public domain in the United States","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:ca726a997dbd1d263da4c657","title":"Navigating Contested Perspectives in Special Education","subtitle":"Promoting Dialogue for the Benefit of Pupils and Students","description":"Bringing together researchers with different approaches to special education on ideological, theoretical and ethical levels, this book provides a multifaceted approach to practice, policy and theory to foster dialogue and meaningful discussion towards best practices in special education. Chapters explore key themes such as the nature and identity of special education, the differences at both local and national levels between special and inclusive education practices, and the issue of contested terminology, acknowledging how a lack of consensus can dilute meaning or cause confusion within different educational settings. Case study chapters report from a rich wealth of international settings such as Norway, Nepal, Denmark, Britain, and Finland, using research gathered from autoethnographies, qualitative interviews and questionnaires from primary, secondary and higher educational contexts. Demonstrating how different perspectives can support organised and more coherent special education that benefits a diversity of children and young people, both socially and academically, this book will be of interest to scholars, researchers and postgraduate students in the fields of inclusion and special education, childhood education and education policy and politics.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"Taylor & Francis","isbn":[],"doi":"10.4324/9781003652656","subjects":["Special education","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JN Education::JNS Teaching of students with different educational needs","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JN Education::JNF Educational strategies and policy::JNFK Educational strategies and policy: inclusion","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JN Education::JND Educational systems and structures","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JN Education::JNL Schools and pre-schools::JNLA Pre-school and kindergarten","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JN Education::JNF Educational strategies and policy","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JN Education::JNA Philosophy and theory of education::JNAM Moral and social purpose of education","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JN Education::JNL Schools and pre-schools::JNLB Primary and middle schools","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JN Education::JNL Schools and pre-schools::JNLC Secondary schools","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JN Education::JNS Teaching of students with different educational needs::JNSG Teaching of students with learning difficulties","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JN Education"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/117000","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/e7ffa333-aa40-4a4c-bd78-6d1ca858c845/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/00ff776e-117d-420a-8334-aa3f92d54465/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/117000","handle":"20.500.12657/117000","dspace_uuid":"2e93cde8-de7e-48d0-ab8c-b6e6d223e578"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/117000","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/117000","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/00ff776e-117d-420a-8334-aa3f92d54465/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-ND · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:4570d36fb622366c50287a22","title":"Navigating the Labyrinth","subtitle":"A Cross-Cultural Analysis of Workplace Bullying from a Central Asian Perspective","description":"While research on workplace bullying has expanded globally, its theoretical foundations remain largely rooted in Western societies. Navigating the Labyrinth - A Cross-Cultural Analysis of Workplace Bullying from a Central Asian Perspective provides a vital corrective to this trend by offering a cross-cultural analysis of workplace mistreatment through the specific socio-historical lens of Central Asia, with a primary focus on Uzbekistan. This book deconstructs universalist assumptions and examines how unique cultural dimensions, such as high power distance and in-group collectivism, fundamentally alter perceptions, enactments, and reports of bullying. Essential for scholars, practitioners, and organizational leaders, this work bridges the gap between global theory and local practice, offering a nuanced guide to fostering psychological safety and protecting human dignity in a rapidly globalizing workforce.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"IntechOpen","isbn":[],"doi":"10.5772/intechopen.115636","subjects":["Industrial psychology","Organizational psychology","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JM Psychology::JMJ Occupational and industrial psychology"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181616","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/d66783a9-eb89-471c-9489-67fff20123d8/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://intech-files.s3.amazonaws.com/a04Tc00000HAZnVIAX/0017053_Authors_Book (2026-06-03 13:44:18).pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181616","handle":"20.500.12854/181616","dspace_uuid":"eaf9c929-d7db-4759-86b4-f00590829ac1"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181616","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181616","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://intech-files.s3.amazonaws.com/a04Tc00000HAZnVIAX/0017053_Authors_Book (2026-06-03 13:44:18).pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:6bc3017af5a67c9e1a44b384","title":"Navigating Transitions to Sustainable Human Development","subtitle":"Frameworks, Evidence and Policies","description":"This is an open access title available under the terms of a CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 License. It is free to read, download and share on Elgaronline.com. This book introduces an innovative framework for Sustainable Human Development, highlighting how achieving a balance between human wellbeing and planetary boundaries requires moving beyond growth-focused horizons. Leading experts present integrated approaches, mapping a clear path for future transition processes.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"Edward Elgar Publishing","isbn":[],"doi":"10.4337/9781035390670","subjects":["Sustainable Human Development; Sustainability Transition; Sustainable And Inclusive Well-Being; Beyond-Gdp; Theoretical Framework; Evidence-Based Policies","RNA","RNT","RNU"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181614","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/c8d46614-6925-4704-a75a-f08d5b9b1ef4/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"read","url":"https://www.elgaronline.com/edcollbook-oa/book/9781035390670/9781035390670.xml"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181614","handle":"20.500.12854/181614","dspace_uuid":"3222552a-f7fa-4c79-9b49-2e996b7e3468"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181614","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181614","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"read","url":"https://www.elgaronline.com/edcollbook-oa/book/9781035390670/9781035390670.xml"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:51d79eadfc15ab1b536f6561","title":"Necrodialogues and Media","subtitle":"Communicating with the Dead in the Twentieth and Twenty-First Centuries","description":"This volume is an original contribution to the understanding of the various forms of communication with the dead. Terming them \"necrodialogues\", it examines these forms of communication in relation to cultural and ritual practices of necromancy and mediumism on the one hand, and to the development of technologies for establishing contact with the beyond on the other. While recent scholarship in media and cultural studies rejects the narrative that technological progress in modernity eclipsed religious experiences and occult practices, twentieth- and twenty-first-century literary studies, holding on to the secularization paradigm, still largely dismiss practices of communication with the dead as anti-modern. By bringing together perspectives from different disciplines, this volume emphasizes the interconnectedness of literary necrodialogues and other cultural and media practices of communicating with the dead. The main aim of the collection is to explore the cultural, historical, anthropological, and media contexts in which modern necrodialogues are produced and invested with different meanings.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Communication","Necrodialogues","Talking Dead","Mediumism","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JB Society and culture: general","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JB Society and culture: general::JBC Cultural and media studies::JBCT Media studies","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QR Religion and beliefs","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116850","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/8db00b1e-54aa-44ed-867f-80a50ac5f850/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/72e1238e-71c3-4c3e-831c-0014cfa73f2d/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116850","handle":"20.500.12657/116850","dspace_uuid":"6e3badef-5b49-440d-bedf-411ab76e8c42"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116850","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116850","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/72e1238e-71c3-4c3e-831c-0014cfa73f2d/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:6004ed1b1e7629fece1029f2","title":"Necrodialogues and Media","subtitle":"Communicating with the Dead in the Twentieth and Twenty-First Centuries","description":"This volume is an original contribution to the understanding of the various forms of communication with the dead. Terming them \"necrodialogues\", it examines these forms of communication in relation to cultural and ritual practices of necromancy and mediumism on the one hand, and to the development of technologies for establishing contact with the beyond on the other. While recent scholarship in media and cultural studies rejects the narrative that technological progress in modernity eclipsed religious experiences and occult practices, twentieth- and twenty-first-century literary studies, holding on to the secularization paradigm, still largely dismiss practices of communication with the dead as anti-modern. By bringing together perspectives from different disciplines, this volume emphasizes the interconnectedness of literary necrodialogues and other cultural and media practices of communicating with the dead. The main aim of the collection is to explore the cultural, historical, anthropological, and media contexts in which modern necrodialogues are produced and invested with different meanings.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Communication","Necrodialogues","Talking Dead","Mediumism","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JB Society and culture: general","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JB Society and culture: general::JBC Cultural and media studies::JBCT Media studies","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QR Religion and beliefs","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181435","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/712ecff9-0c04-4e0f-9b74-b1fb8b75c190/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116850/1/9783110733457.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181435","handle":"20.500.12854/181435","dspace_uuid":"00e0fb37-dc5b-431b-a3f1-4ecca1b71504"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181435","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181435","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116850/1/9783110733457.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:49004f3a057ed0cd657a94e9","title":"NET FORCE HIDDEN AGENDAS","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Tom Clancy","Steve R. Pieczenik"],"language":"es","year":1999,"publisher":"Headline","isbn":["1101002441","9781439519516","9781101002445","9780606204217","0425171396","9788408048954","0747261156","0606204210","9783453171831","9780747261155","9780425171394","3453171837","8408048953","143951951X","0727856898","9780727856890"],"doi":"","subjects":[],"source":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL8409305W","cover_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/485722-M.jpg","formats":[],"access":"digital_lending","license":"","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"OL8409305W","openlibrary_work":"OL8409305W","openlibrary_edition":"OL43608346M","internet_archive":"tomclancysnethid00clan"},"providers":[{"source":"Open Library","source_id":"OL8409305W","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL8409305W","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"digital_lending","license":"","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:2de0e86a60f00310581d588e","title":"Network Security Assessment","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Chris McNab"],"language":"en","year":2004,"publisher":"Anaya Multimedia","isbn":["8441517517","9780596006112","9781306817455","9780596520809","9781306816878","1306817455","0596510306","9780596519339","9780596510305","059600611X","0596520808","0596519338","149191095X","9781491910955","9788441517516","1306816874"],"doi":"","subjects":[],"source":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL5752477W","cover_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/388870-M.jpg","formats":[],"access":"digital_lending","license":"","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"OL5752477W","openlibrary_work":"OL5752477W","openlibrary_edition":"OL26836814M","internet_archive":"networksecuritya0000mcna"},"providers":[{"source":"Open Library","source_id":"OL5752477W","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL5752477W","language":"en","formats":[],"access":"digital_lending","license":"","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:cd85d4354323fff1e30e9e18","title":"Neurodiversity and the Contemporary in the 21st-Century Novel","subtitle":"","description":"Offering a provocative analysis of neurodivergent and 21st century perspectives on time and some of its cultural expressions, this open access book is the first comparative study of the intersections between neurodiversity and the evolving field of Contemporary Studies. Blending literary close reading and sociological discourse analysis, the book turns to fiction for the strategic insights it can offer into cultural imaginaries of neurodiversity and time. With a focus on 21st century novels from authors such as Jonathan Safran Foer, Lisa Genova, John Wray, and Julie Dachez, it interrogates the entanglements between categories of crip time and the contemporary, examines the processes of exclusion governing neurodivergence construction, and advocates for a new vocabulary demonstrating the role of contemporary neuroinclusive perspectives in 21st century epistemological processes. The ebook editions of this book are available open access under a CC BY 4.0 licence on bloomsburycollections.com. Open access was funded by the Wellcome Trust.","authors":["Simonetti, Nicola"],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"Bloomsbury Publishing (UK)","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Neuronovel","Crip theory","Disability studies","Crip time","Critical neurodiversity studies","Lisa Genova","Olivia Rosenthal","Joanna Cannon","Nathan Filer","Neal Shusterman","Henry Bauchau’s","John Wray","– Mark Haddon","Reif Larsen","Jonathan Safran Foer","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism::DSB Literary studies: general::DSBJ Literary studies: from c 2000","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism::DSK Literary studies: fiction, novelists and prose writers","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism::DSB Literary studies: general::DSBH Literary studies: c 1900 to c 2000","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism::DSB Literary studies: general"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181529","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/bf524ba3-1c61-431d-a0ec-3ddb9afec664/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116618/1/9781350587427.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181529","handle":"20.500.12854/181529","dspace_uuid":"20e09a60-cf75-43f0-a8b1-6f15f94bacb9","doab_source_id":"20.500.12854/181463","doab_handle":"20.500.12854/181463","doab_dspace_uuid":"914ddf36-8e42-4af7-92b3-084152f72192"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181529","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181529","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116618/1/9781350587427.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true},{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181463","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181463","language":"en","formats":[],"access":"open_access","license":"open access","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:c13fe81feda9ba3d85b99f35","title":"Neuromancer","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["William Gibson"],"language":"es","year":1984,"publisher":"Time Warner AudioBooks","isbn":["9029042478","8445072897","9787539951331","0006480411","9788585887902","0002252325","8790136292","9781399607773","9788445070840","9780575034709","7539951338","6055532662","9788445009444","9780613922517","9781473217386","0441012035","0441007465","9788445015254","9780932096418","8445076620","057503470X","9780002252324","9780007119585","9781004055050","1473217377","9783453056657","8804516445","9783453313897","9788790136291","0586066454","9788445072899","3453056655","0441569560","9780006480419","9788203203329","0441569595","8576571919","110114646X","8842910686","0007491522","9788445075951","9780007491520","9780441007462","0007119585","9783608504880","8445070843","3453313895","1570420599","0932096417","1004055056","229030820X","0143111604","2277223255","0441000681","9780307969941","8203203329","9781473217379","9780441569588","9782277223252","9781101146460","8445015257","0613922514","9789752103672","9781570421563","0441569587","9780143111603","9780007383290","9780441012039","9752103677","9780441569571","8842907464","9786055532666","1473217385","9780441569595","0007383290","9780441000685","8758804110","9788758804118","3608504885","9780441569564","9788804752233","1570421560","1399607774","9788842907466","0736638369","9781570420597","9782290308202","8445009443","9788804516446","8804752238","8445075950","9788445076620","9788576571919","9789029042475","0307969940","0441569579","9510172049","9780586066454","9789510172049","8585887907","9788842910688","9780736638364"],"doi":"","subjects":[],"source":"Open Library","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL27258W","cover_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/283860-M.jpg","formats":[],"access":"digital_lending","license":"","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"OL27258W","openlibrary_work":"OL27258W","openlibrary_edition":"OL60610680M","internet_archive":"neuromancer0000gibs_b5r9"},"providers":[{"source":"Open Library","source_id":"OL27258W","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL27258W","language":"es","formats":[],"access":"digital_lending","license":"","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:d59eb5bc784901db7a0935c8","title":"Neuroscience of Attention","subtitle":"Attentional Control and Selection","description":"The ability to attend selectively to events in the world around us is a core cognitive function. It prevents distraction and enables humans and animals to dedicate perceptual, cognitive, and motor resources to deal with the most pressing current challenges. When attention systems of the brain are damaged by disease or trauma, the impact for the individual and society can be significant, and therefore, understanding the neural mechanisms of attention is a central goal in neuroscience. In addition, understanding how attention mechanisms operate is critical for advancing the important mission of developing the most effective training regimes for a wide range of duties, as well as for creating new methods for educating the world's growing population. This book addresses the basic neuroscience of how the brain controls the focus of attention, and how this focused attention influences sensory and motor processes. This book provides a selection of the models, mechanisms and findings in the neuroscience of attentional control and selection from leading authorities working in human and animal models, and incorporating an array of neuroscience methods from single neuron recordings to functional brain imaging, and advanced modeling. The book begins with chapters that describe attentional selection, relying largely on evidence from attention in vision. Subsequent chapters address attentional control mechanisms in cortical and subcortical brain networks. Finally, the role of attention in action, short-term memory, and emotion are discussed.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2012,"publisher":"Oxford University Press","isbn":[],"doi":"10.1093/acprof:oso/9780195334364.001.0001","subjects":["Cognitive function","Perceptual resources","Cognitive resources","Motor resources","Disease","Trauma","Attention mechanisms","Attentional control","Attentional selection","Emotion","thema EDItEUR::P Mathematics and Science::PS Biology, life sciences::PSA Life sciences: general issues::PSAN Neurosciences","thema EDItEUR::P Mathematics and Science::PS Biology, life sciences::PSA Life sciences: general issues::PSAN Neurosciences::PSAN5 Cognitive and behavioural neuroscience","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JM Psychology::JMM Physiological and neuro-psychology, biopsychology","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JM Psychology::JMR Cognition and cognitive psychology"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116969","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/afd10c09-315a-4a18-a54e-dfd1d323adca/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/74fa86a2-2cf7-4ba3-ac91-57755c28c2ed/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC · Other open license","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12657/116969","handle":"20.500.12657/116969","dspace_uuid":"ee05f195-2ad3-415d-a312-954b80935f84"},"providers":[{"source":"OAPEN Library","source_id":"20.500.12657/116969","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/116969","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/74fa86a2-2cf7-4ba3-ac91-57755c28c2ed/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC · Other open license","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:7bf5bc57546025816b176417","title":"New Algorithms and Methods to Estimate Maximum-Likelihood Phylogenies: Assessing the Performance of PhyML 3.0","subtitle":"","description":"","authors":["Stéphane Guindon","Jean-François Dufayard","Vincent Lefort","Maria Anisimova","Wim Hordijk","Olivier Gascuel"],"language":"en","year":2010,"publisher":"Systematic Biology","isbn":[],"doi":"10.1093/sysbio/syq010","subjects":["Genomics and Phylogenetic Studies","Bioinformatics and Genomic Networks","Genetic diversity and population structure"],"source":"OpenAlex","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/sysbio/syq010","cover_url":"","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://academic.oup.com/sysbio/article-pdf/59/3/307/24207259/syq010.pdf"}],"access":"open_access","license":"Open Access; license not reported by OpenAlex","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"article","identifiers":{"source_id":"W2111211467","openalex_id":"W2111211467"},"providers":[{"source":"OpenAlex","source_id":"W2111211467","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/sysbio/syq010","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://academic.oup.com/sysbio/article-pdf/59/3/307/24207259/syq010.pdf"}],"access":"open_access","license":"Open Access; license not reported by OpenAlex","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:47d565bd9c931168f93412b7","title":"New Approaches to Phrynichus’ ›Praeparatio Sophistica‹","subtitle":"","description":"Phrynichus’ Praeparatio sophistica ranks not last among the most importat works of ancient scholarly literature which we wish we could read in its original, full redaction. It was Phrynichus’ magnum opus , and the high status of this work was still acknowledged in Byzantine intellectual circles. This volume brings some new light to the Praeparatio sophistica and its history, focusing on three areas of interest: (1) its context of production and linguistic theorisation; (2) its stylistic theorisation and interpretative framework; (3) the direct and indirect transmission from antiquity, through Late Antiquity, and down to the Byzantine era. The volume will be of interest to Classicists working on the linguistic theories of Atticism and the literary practice of the Second Sophistic.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Atticism","Classical antiquity","Lexicography","Phrynichus","Arabius","Antike","Attizismus","Lexikografie","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History::NHG Middle Eastern history","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History::NHC Ancient history","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism::DSB Literary studies: general::DSBB Literary studies: ancient, classical and medieval","thema EDItEUR::Q Philosophy and Religion::QD Philosophy::QDH Philosophical traditions and schools of thought::QDHA Ancient Greek and Roman philosophy"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181544","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/9ec454cb-ecc1-4380-a92b-e1dcdf597023/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116660/1/9783111580319.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181544","handle":"20.500.12854/181544","dspace_uuid":"53cdf71c-308a-4639-b86a-303310b9091a"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181544","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181544","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116660/1/9783111580319.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:f9aa2f280730ab00940fa1c1","title":"New Approaches to Transcodification","subtitle":"Literature, Arts, and Media","description":"This collection aims to renew our perspective on adaptation and intermedial processes by thinking of them in terms of codes rather than media. As a result, the notion of transcodification emerges as a crucial tool in order to study the circulation of semiotic and aesthetic resources across disciplines, knowledge systems, and cultures. Defined as the transfer of meaning-making potential from one semiotic domain to another, transcodification both includes and transcends intermediality, thus dramatically expanding the scope and research potential of adaptation and intermedial studies. The essays collected here apply this framework to an incredibly wide variety of objects and issues, from the relationship between art and historiography to the visual culture of finance, from contemporary approaches to ekphrasis to the hidden labor of screenwriters, from modern surveillance to digital comics, from fansubbing to the reception of the classical world in the digital age, from medieval theater to the role of videogames in the “war on terror”. By fostering dialogue between radically different disciplines, the book offers a unique approach to the study of semiotic interrelations across the most diverse aspects of human culture.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Adaption","Intermediality","Semiotics","Transcodification","Intermedialität","Semiotik","Transkodierung","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History::NHG Middle Eastern history","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History::NHC Ancient history","thema EDItEUR::G Reference, Information and Interdisciplinary subjects::GT Interdisciplinary studies::GTC Communication studies","thema EDItEUR::D Biog