countries through increased research, funding initiatives, policy development, teacher support, and media interest. These developments are presented in the book through case studies from each of the five countries. The volume also introduces contemporary research on gifted education from both theoretical and empirical perspectives and includes international contributions that reflect on the opportunities and challenges facing Nordic policy, research, and educational practice today. The book serves as an up-to-date resource on Nordic approaches to gifted education in research, teaching, and policymaking.","authors":[],"language":"en","year":2026,"publisher":"Stockholm University Press","isbn":[],"doi":"10.16993/bdo","subjects":["Child rights","Education policy","High ability","Nordic perspectives","Talent development","Gifted","thema EDItEUR::1 Place qualifiers::1D Europe::1DN Northern Europe, Scandinavia","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JB Society and culture: general::JBF Social and ethical issues::JBFA Social discrimination and social justice","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JN Education::JNF Educational strategies and policy::JNFK Educational strategies and policy: inclusion","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JN Education::JNS Teaching of students with different educational needs::JNSP Teaching of gifted or talented students","thema EDItEUR::Y Children’s, Teenage and Educational::YX Children’s / Teenage: Personal and social topics::YXP Children’s / Teenage personal and social topics: Diversity, equality and inclusion"],"source":"OAPEN Library","source_url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/117023","cover_url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/ee781840-1f97-41c9-a374-f2ce2b321830/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/rest/bitstreams/39f5ed75-34fb-40ff-9e12-89dc8c8fcc32/retrieve"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ · CC-BY