iness', 'subject_page_content': 'Simple to use, simple to adopt. Our business textbooks are designed to meet the standard scope and sequence requirements of their respective courses – and are 100% free online. Complete with free resources for educators (like LMS course shells, lecture slides, instructor answer keys, and more), all OpenStax textbooks are fully customizable. Explore our texts below and adopt any and all parts u","{'id': 102, 'meta': {'type': 'books.BookCategories'}, 'subject_name': 'Business', 'subject_category': 'Management and Marketing'}"],"source":"OpenStax","source_url":"https://openstax.org/details/books/organizational-behavior","cover_url":"https://assets.openstax.org/oscms-prodcms/media/documents/organizational_behavior_book_card.svg","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://assets.openstax.org/oscms-prodcms/media/documents/organizational-behavior_-_WEB.pdf"},{"type":"read","url":"https://openstax.org/books/organizational-behavior/pages/1-introduction"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike License 4.0","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"textbook","identifiers":{"source_id":"2d941ab9-ac5b-4eb8-b21c-965d36a4f296","openstax_slug":"organizational-behavior","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/"},"providers":[{"source":"OpenStax","source_id":"2d941ab9-ac5b-4eb8-b21c-965d36a4f296","source_url":"https://openstax.org/details/books/organizational-behavior","language":"en","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://assets.openstax.org/oscms-prodcms/media/documents/organizational-behavior_-_WEB.pdf"},{"type":"read","url":"https://openstax.org/books/organizational-behavior/pages/1-introduction"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike License 4.0","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:71b6b0461a9fdd8eb38bf5fb","title":"Orientación educativa y gestión tutorial en el contexto de la educación superior","subtitle":"","description":"This book provides a comprehensive analysis of the guidance and mentoring processes in university education, highlighting their relevance for the personal, academic, and professional development of students. The work conceives educational guidance as a systematic, dynamic, and formative process that goes beyond academics, incorporating personal, social, and emotional dimensions to foster student autonomy, responsibility, and decision-making skills regarding their life projects. A central aspect is the helping relationship, based on trust, respect, and empathy, which allows students to explore themselves, recognize their strengths and areas for improvement, and develop socio-emotional competencies essential for resilience and decision-making. Additionally, the text delves into professional and vocational guidance, emphasizing the importance of assisting students in building career paths aligned with their values and interests, promoting the formation of ethical and socially committed professionals. Tutorial management is presented as a structured pedagogical strategy that facilitates continuous monitoring of learning, academic planning, and prevention of difficulties in the university trajectory. The work combines theory and practice through case studies and methodological proposals, offering practical tools for teachers, tutors, and counselors. Altogether, it constitutes an essential guide to strengthen guidance and tutoring in higher education, promoting comprehensive, inclusive, and student-centered education aligned with the challenges of 21st-century education.","authors":["Rojas-Valladares, Adalia Lisett","Domínguez-Urdanivia, Yideira"],"language":"es","year":2025,"publisher":"Sophia Editions","isbn":[],"doi":"10.64092/bgpl5137","subjects":["Orientación educativa","Acompañamiento tutorial","Relación de ayuda","Desarrollo profesional","Formación integral","thema EDItEUR::J Society and Social Sciences::JN Education"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https:/