ecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:366a553a7a55b01013a4a264","title":"Per la storia del testo di Marziale","subtitle":"","description":"Can we speak, in the case of the Epigrammaton libri , of very ancient variants, perhaps even authorship? This volume proposes a reconstruction of the textual history of the work that runs backwards-from the copyists to the ancient editors, to Martial himself-and aims to distinguish, classify and justify the numerous interventions accumulated on the text.","authors":["Russotti, Ambra"],"language":"it","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Classical antiquity","Latin literature","Martial","Textual criticism","Antike","Lateinische Literatur","Textkritik","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DB Ancient, classical and medieval texts::DBS Ancient Sagas and epics::DBSG Ancient Greek and Roman literature","thema EDItEUR::D Biography, Literature and Literary studies::DS Literature: history and criticism::DSB Literary studies: general::DSBB Literary studies: ancient, classical and medieval"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181521","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/fd5a7601-b14b-470f-8580-32aee266c035/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116769/1/9783111715407.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181521","handle":"20.500.12854/181521","dspace_uuid":"5fb776c7-393f-4708-926c-e33b5bae9e47"},"providers":[{"source":"DOAB","source_id":"20.500.12854/181521","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181521","language":"it","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116769/1/9783111715407.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true}]},{"id":"work:0fd63d06fe326667d7fb0217","title":"Persecuted, “Aryanized,” Compensated?","subtitle":"How the Department Store Group Hermann Tietz Became Hertie","description":"The Hermann Tietz family business was one of the pioneers of the German department store industry. After the National Socialist takeover, the Jewish owners were forced to give up their company. Hermann Tietz became Hertie. The troubled past of this major department store brand of the West German \"Economic Miracle\" lay in the dark for a long time. In this study, Johannes Bähr and Ingo Köhler shed light on the anti-Semitic agitation against the owners of the Hermann Tietz Group, the \"Aryanization\" of their company assets, the fate of the Tietz family after their ousting from the company and the development of the Hertie Group up to the disputes over restitution and compensation in the immediate post-war years. Drawing on a wide range of sources, including previously inaccessible documents, a detailed picture emerges of a department store history caught between the poles of persecution, loss and responsibility.","authors":["Bähr, Johannes","Köhler, Ingo"],"language":"en","year":2025,"publisher":"De Gruyter","isbn":[],"doi":"","subjects":["Business History","National Socialism","Restitution","thema EDItEUR::N History and Archaeology::NH History"],"source":"DOAB","source_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/handle/20.500.12854/181560","cover_url":"https://directory.doabooks.org/rest/bitstreams/b4aed073-8b9f-42eb-97dc-e057be5ad4d4/retrieve","formats":[{"type":"pdf","url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/116756/1/9783111706757.pdf"}],"access":"creative_commons","license":"open access · https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ · CC-BY-NC-ND","verified_legal":true,"resource_type":"book","identifiers":{"source_id":"20.500.12854/181560","ha